[Term]
id: FBbt:00000086
name: mitotic domain A
def: "At blastoderm, prior to elongation, domain A is a wide band of cells straddling the dorsal midline and spanning the length of the germ band. Germ band elongation buckles and folds this domain. This domain becomes the amnioserosa." [FlyBase:FBrf0049535]
comment: See figure 1 of Foe (1989) for an atlas of mitotic domains.
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00000059 ! mitotic domain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000087
name: mitotic domain B
def: "Mitotic domain B is a paired domain that occupies a wedge-shaped area on the dorsolateral surface of the presumptive head." [FlyBase:FBrf0049535]
comment: See figure 1 of Foe (1989) for an atlas of mitotic domains.
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00000059 ! mitotic domain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000088
name: mitotic domain M
def: "Region surrounding the segmentally reiterated mitotic domain 25 cells. Cells of mitotic domain M do not divide with any obvious bilateral symmetry." [FlyBase:FBrf0049535]
comment: See figure 1 of Foe (1989) for an atlas of mitotic domains.
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00000059 ! mitotic domain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000089
name: mitotic domain N
def: "Mitotic domain N is the ventrolateral region surrounding mitotic domains 16, 17 and 21." [FlyBase:FBrf0049535]
comment: See figure 1 of Foe (1989) for an atlas of mitotic domains.
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00000059 ! mitotic domain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000090
name: dorsal ridge
def: "Protuberance of the embryonic head that develops at stage 12. It forms from the dorsal part of the gnathal segments. It gives rise to the frontal sac." [FlyBase:FBrf0064803]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00100313 ! multicellular structure
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005327 ! part of stage 12 embryo
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005328 ! part of stage 13 embryo
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005330 ! part of stage 14 embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00016018 ! develops from dorsal ridge primordium

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000091
name: pole bud
def: "Cytoplasmic bud that forms at the posterior pole of the embryo during cycle 9. Pole buds give rise to the pole cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064779]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005305 ! part of syncytial blastoderm embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00004891 ! develops from pole plasm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000092
name: primordial germ cell
def: "Cell that begins as a pole cell, becomes incorporated into the gonad and can develop into a germline stem cell (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997; Dansereau and Lasko, 2008; Slaidina et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0101973, FlyBase:FBrf0216027, FlyBase:FBrf0244767]
comment: Can be identified in the larva by expression of vasa (Slaidina et al., 2020). Only a small subset of pole cells can become germ cells and this fate might be specified by the time the posterior midgut primordium invaginates (Okada, 1998).
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
synonym: "GC" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0244767]
synonym: "PGC" EXACT []
synonym: "pole cell" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00004860 ! germline cell
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00053322 ! develops from embryonic pole cell
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0283442 ! expresses vas
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/696" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000093
name: ventral midline of embryo
def: "The middle underside of the embryo, where the midline neurons and midline glia develop (Kearney et al., 2004)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0180108]
