[Term]
id: FBbt:00000125
name: endoderm
def: "Innermost germ layer of the embryo (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It is formed by the invagination of two anlagen, those of the anterior and posterior midgut (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0155831]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
is_a: FBbt:00000110 ! germ layer

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000126
name: mesoderm
def: "Middle germ layer of the embryo (between ectoderm and endoderm) following gastrulation (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Shortly after its formation, its cells undergo mitosis and it loses its regular epithelial architecture (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). In stage 9 it reorganizes into a regular monolayer of cuboidal cells that lines the ectoderm (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). At the end of stage 10 further cell divisions disrupt this structure and its cells reform into two layers in stage 11 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It finally splits up into separate cell masses in late stage 11 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its derivatives include the muscles, heart and fat body (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0155831]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
is_a: FBbt:00000110 ! germ layer

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000127
name: head mesoderm
def: "Anterior region of mesoderm that forms a vertical plate beside the anterior midgut rudiment (Campos Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). After its initial ingression during ventral furrow formation, it continues to recruit cells from the surface of the embryo until the end of stage 10 (Campos Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It gives rise to the pharyngeal musculature, hemocytes, the corpus cardiacum and the visceral muscle of the esophagus (Campos Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997; de Velasco et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0190261]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "head mesoderm P3 primordium" RELATED []
synonym: "head mesoderm primordium P4" RELATED []
synonym: "HeadMes" RELATED []
synonym: "HeadMesP3" RELATED []
synonym: "hms" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064803]
synonym: "P4 HeadMes" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
synonym: "procephalic mesoderm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000126 ! part of mesoderm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000128
name: trunk mesoderm
def: "Region of mesoderm of that forms a layer interior to the ectoderm of the germ band (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Following its invagination during ventral furrow formation in stages 6 and 7, it remains a coherent structure with no morphologically apparent subdivisions, apart from transient metamery during stage 9, until stage 11 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its cells divide following invagination and it loses its epithelial integrity, forming a monolayer of cuboidal cells by stage 9 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). A further division happens during stage 10 leading to two distinct layers by stage 11 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "AtrunkMes" RELATED []
synonym: "mesoderm of the germ layer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "P2 TrMes" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
synonym: "TrMes" RELATED []
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000102 ! part of germ band
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000126 ! part of mesoderm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000129
name: somatic trunk mesoderm
def: "Outer layer of the trunk mesoderm that arises due to mitosis at the end of stage 10 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It will give rise to the segmentally-repeated body wall muscles and the fat body (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "somatopleura" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00005495 ! primordium
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000128 ! part of trunk mesoderm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00000130
name: visceral trunk mesoderm
def: "Inner layer of the trunk mesoderm that arises due to mitosis at the end of stage 10 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It will give rise to the visceral musculature of the trunk (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "splanchnopleura" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00005495 ! primordium
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000128 ! part of trunk mesoderm

