[Term]
id: FBbt:00000325
name: embryonic/larval ganglionic tracheal branch
alt_id: FBbt:00005592
def: "Embryonic/larval trachea that branches from the lateral trunk and which tracheates the ventral nerve cord. The three most anterior ganglionic branches (GB0-GB2) anastomose mid-ventrally with the branch from the opposite hemisphere, forming a ventral anastomose. In the larva, the last two pairs of ventral ganglionic branches terminate without tracheating the posterior ventral nerve cord." [FlyBase:FBrf0011558, FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
subset: cur
synonym: "i branch" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0002494]
synonym: "larval ganglionic branch" EXACT []
synonym: "larval ganglionic trachea" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0003937]
synonym: "larval ventral ganglionic branch" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0011558]
is_a: FBbt:00007472 ! primary tracheal branch
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000185 ! part of larval tracheal system
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00000233 ! continuous with embryonic/larval tracheal lateral trunk
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00001102 ! continuous with larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005591 ! develops from ganglionic tracheal branch primordium

