[Term]
id: FBbt:00001057
name: neurogenic region
def: "Region that gives rise to the neuroblasts of the central nervous system (Bossing et al., 1996). An anterior region (procephalic neurogenic region) gives rise to the brain and a posterior, ventral region (ventral neuroectoderm) gives rise to the ventral nerve cord and gnathal ganglia (Bossing et al., 1996)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0090460, FlyBase:FBrf0098344]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007006 ! developing material anatomical entity
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000111 ! part of ectoderm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001058
name: procephalic neurogenic region
def: "Tissue which becomes morphologically distinct shortly after cephalic furrow formation as two strips of about 80 enlarged cells which extend dorso-ventrally on either side of the developing head. It gives rise to neuroblasts of the brain." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0090460]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "pregnathal neuroectoderm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0161020]
synonym: "procephalic neuroectoderm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0161020]
is_a: FBbt:00001057 ! neurogenic region
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000119 ! part of anterior ectoderm
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00000155 ! part of embryonic head

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001059
name: visual primordium
def: "Primordium that develops from the posterior procephalic region of the embryo and gives rise to visual structures of the larva and adult (Green et al., 1993; Chang et al., 2001). An optic placode forms from cells of the visual primordium when they become columnar in shape towards the end of stage 11 (Green et al., 1993; Chang et al., 2001). This placode invaginates during stages 12-13, forming a deep pouch of approximately 85 cells (Green et al., 1993). Its ventral lip segregates from the rest of the primordium and develops into the Bolwig organ (Green et al., 1993). The remainder of the placode, which will form the optic lobe, detaches from the surface of the embryo and attaches to the lateral brain, maintaining a tubular appearance until larval hatching (Green et al., 1993). Its anterior and posterior domains will become the larval inner and outer optic anlage, respectively (Chang et al., 2001). The cells that will become the eye disc are anterior and dorsal to the optic lobe placode cells (Chang et al., 2001). They move into the interior of the embryo during head involution, when they are pushed under the dorsal ridge (Huang et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064481, FlyBase:FBrf0141490, FlyBase:FBrf0235170, FlyBase:FBrf0243080]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "optic lobe placode" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0141490]
synonym: "optic lobe primordium" NARROW []
synonym: "P2 VisSys" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00014201 ! part of early extended germ band embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001060
name: embryonic brain
def: "Brain of the embryo, consisting of the protocerebrum, deutocerebrum and tritocerebrum (Urbach and Technau, 2003; Crews, 2019). It develops from the procephalic neurogenic region (Urbach and Technau, 2003)." [FlyBase:FBrf0161020, FlyBase:FBrf0244240]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00003626 ! supraesophageal ganglion
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00001058 ! develops from procephalic neurogenic region

