[Term]
id: FBbt:00001244
name: embryonic glioblast
def: "Glioblast of the embryo." [FlyBase:FBrf0105240]
subset: cur

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001245
name: embryonic dorsal procephalic subperineural glial cell
def: "Glial cell of the embryo that arises at the dorsoposterior edge of the protocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 1998). At early stage 12 there are 2-3 cells, and this number increases to 5-6 (Hartenstein et al., 1998). Until stage 15, cells of this cluster stay together in a wedge-shaped formation, but later spread out to cover the dorso-posterior surface of the supraesophageal ganglion (Hartenstein et al., 1998). Most of these cells become larval surface glia, but some may become cell body glia (Hartenstein et al., 1998; Hartenstein et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0105240, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
subset: cur
synonym: "dorsal procephalic subperineural glia cluster" BROAD []
synonym: "DPSG cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0105240]
is_a: FBbt:00052369 ! embryonic glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001060 ! part of embryonic brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001246
name: embryonic ventral procephalic subperineural glial cell
def: "Glial cell of the embryo that arises near the boundary between the protocerebrum and deutocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 1998). There are around 12 of these cells by embryonic stage 12 (Hartenstein et al., 1998). During stage 12, cells of this cluster spread out to cover the anterior and lateral surface of the deutocerebrum and basal protocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 1998). Most of these cells develop into larval subperineurial glia, but some may become cell body glia (Hartenstein et al., 1998)." [FlyBase:FBrf0105240, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
subset: cur
synonym: "ventral procephalic subperineural glia cluster" BROAD []
synonym: "VPSG cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0105240]
is_a: FBbt:00052369 ! embryonic glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005662 ! part of embryonic central brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001247
name: embryonic basal procephalic longitudinal glial cell
def: "Glial cell of the embryo that arises close to the boundary between the tritocerebrum and deutocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 1998). There are only two or three of these cells early in stage 11, but they increase in number to around 20 by the end of stage 12 (Hartenstein et al., 1998). They spread out dorsally and ventrally, at the medial surface of the brain neuropil, reaching the precursor to the brain connective dorsally and the connectives joining the brain to the VNC ventrally (Hartenstein et al., 1998; Omoto et al., 2015). These cells become larval neuropil glia (Hartenstein et al., 1998)." [FlyBase:FBrf0105240, FlyBase:FBrf0214261, FlyBase:FBrf0229106]
comment: Thought to descend from Td7 neuroblast based on its position and gcm expression, but no direct evidence (Hartenstein et al., 2011; Omoto et al., 2015).
subset: cur
synonym: "basal procephalic longitudinal glia cluster" BROAD []
synonym: "BPLG cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0105240]
is_a: FBbt:00052369 ! embryonic glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005662 ! part of embryonic central brain
relationship: RO:0002203 FBbt:00047857 ! develops into larval brain neuropil glial cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001248
name: embryonic anterior deutocerebral subperineurial glial cell
def: "Glial cell of the embryo that arises in the anterior deutocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 1998). During stage 12, these cells increase in number from two to four or five (Hartenstein et al., 1998). They spread out and, together with the PDSG cells, form a band of cells that cover the deutocerebrum and ventral protocerebrum by stage 14 (Hartenstein et al., 1998; Hartenstein et al., 2011). These cells develop into larval surface glia (Hartenstein et al., 1998)." [FlyBase:FBrf0105240, FlyBase:FBrf0229106]
subset: cur
synonym: "ADSG cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0105240]
synonym: "anterior deuterocerebral subperineurial glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "anterior deutocerebral subperineurial glial cluster" BROAD []
is_a: FBbt:00052369 ! embryonic glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005662 ! part of embryonic central brain

