[Term]
id: FBbt:00001253
name: exit glial cell
def: "A surface associated glial cell that is associated with the exit point of a nerve from the central nervous system." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: Disambiguation: Some authors consider 'exit glia' to be a distinct class (e.g. see Sepp et al., 2001). However, we follow a more recent system (von Hilchen, 2008) that considers exit glia cells to be a type of peripheral glia. Their nomenclature (ePG1-12) reflects this.
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00001320 ! PNS glial cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001255
name: larval channel glial cell
def: "Surface associated glial cell that lies along a dorsoventral channel of the larval ventral nerve cord (Ito et al., 1995). The cell bodies lie close to and send processes along the channel surface (Ito et al., 1995). The nuclei of these glial cells are smaller and more spherical compared to the flattened nuclei of the subperineurial glia (Ito et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
subset: cur
synonym: "CG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "CNS channel glial cell" EXACT []
