[Term]
id: FBbt:00001276
name: larval B-subperineurial glial cell
def: "Large subperineural glial cell that sits over the posterior commissure just medial to the longitudinal connectives (Klambt and Goodman, 1991; Ito et al., 1995). It sends processes in three directions: medially to the midline, anteriorly and posteriorly (Ito et al., 1995). Unlike the A-subperineural glial cell, the B-subperineural glial cell is only found in abdominal neuromeres, and lies at approximately the center of the segment along the antero-posterior axis (Ito et al., 1995). It develops from neuroblast NB1-1 of the abdomen (Beckervordersandforth et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0054242, FlyBase:FBrf0057603, FlyBase:FBrf0205499, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
subset: cur
