[Term]
id: FBbt:00001366
name: supraesophageal ganglion neuron
def: "." [FBC:Autogenerated]
subset: cur

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001367
name: SP1 neuron
def: "Bilaterally paired neuron of the embryo/larva. Each (?) abdominal segment contains a pair of SP1 neurons with an axon that crosses the ventral midline as part of the anterior commissure, wraps around the cell body of its contralateral partner and then extends anteriorly as part of the longitudinal connective. During development, these axons pioneer the anterior commissure and longitudinal connectives." [FlyBase:FBrf0053374, FlyBase:FBrf0064795, FlyBase:FBrf0144965]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00005128 ! pioneer neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00005097 ! has soma location ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00001103 ! fasciculates with larval longitudinal connective
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00001110 ! fasciculates with larval abdominal anterior commissure

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001368
name: serotonergic SP2 neuron
def: "Serotonergic neuron whose cell body is located in the in the anterodorsal brain, in a cluster posterior to the serotonergic SP1 neurons. There are approximately three of these cells in the larva and five in the adult (Giang et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0048551, FlyBase:FBrf0213697]
subset: cur
synonym: "SP2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048551]
synonym: "supraesophageal ganglion neuron 2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048551]
is_a: FBbt:00100359 ! serotonergic SP neuron

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001369
name: neuroblast of ventral nervous system
def: "Neuroblast that generates cells of the ventral nervous system, including interneurons, motor neurons and/or glial cells (Bossing et al., 1996). These neuroblasts derive from the ventral neurectoderm (Bossing et al., 1996)." [FlyBase:FBrf0090460, FlyBase:FBrf0098344]
comment: Applies to neuroblasts at all stages of development.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "neuroblast of ventral nerve cord primordium" RELATED []
synonym: "VNC neuroblast" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00001061 ! develops from ventral neuroectoderm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001370
name: stage 1 neuroblast
def: "The first neuroblast subpopulation delaminating from the ventral neurectoderm towards the end of the second mesodermal cell division, shortly after gastrulation (Hartenstein and Campos-Ortega, 1984). These neuroblasts are generally arranged in two fairly regular longitudinal rows (the medial and lateral longitudinal rows), with a few cells scattered in an intermediate row. Doe (1992) defines the end of S1 as being early embryonic stage 9 following the development of NB3-2." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0076117, FlyBase:FBrf0112030]
comment: Figure 7 of Hartenstein and Campos-Ortega, (1984), graphically depicts the pattern formed by the population of neuroblasts for the left half of the germ band.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "S1 neuroblast" RELATED []
synonym: "SI neuroblast" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00005146 ! neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001371 ! neuroblast NB1-1
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at stage 1 as the anteriormost neuroblast and generates the aCC and pCC neurons from its first ganglion mother cell (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S2-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). There are some differences in its progeny between gnathal, abdominal and thoracic segments (Schmid et al., 1999; Rickert et al., 2018). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 16 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0058118, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096, FlyBase:FBrf0238045]
comment: Originally referred to as NB2-2 by Doe (1992), this was renamed to NB1-1 by Broadus et al. (1995) to reflect the fact that it makes the aCC/pCC lineage in both Drosophila and Schistocerca.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "neuroglioblast NB1-1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0058118]
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001372 ! thoracic neuroblast NB1-1
def: "Neuroblast NB1-1 found in a thoracic segment. During embryonic development, it generates the CoA motorneuron in addition to aCC (DA1) (Schmid et al., 1999), but does not generate glia (Schmid et al., 1999; Beckervordersandforth et al., 2008). It resumes proliferation in the larva in all thoracic segments to generate postembryonic lineage 16 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0205499, FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
subset: cur
synonym: "neuroblast NB1-1 of thorax" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001373 ! abdominal neuroblast NB1-1
def: "Neuroblast NB1-1 found in an abdominal segment. It generates subperineurial glia as well as neurons (Schmid et al., 1999; Beckervordersandforth et al., 2008). It is a type II neuroglioblast and its glial progeny are part of its Notch ON hemilineage (Udolph et al., 2001). It does not produce a secondary lineage (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0135724, FlyBase:FBrf0205499, FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
subset: cur
synonym: "NB1-1A" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205499]
synonym: "neuroblast NB1-1 of abdomen" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001374 ! neuroblast NB2-5
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S1 and generates a diverse array of cell types during the embryonic stage, including a motorneuron, interneurons, glial cells and glia (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S2-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in T1 to A1 segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016; Marin et al., 2024). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 17 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00005147 ! neuroglioblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001375 ! neuroblast NB3-5
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at stage 1 in the interior-most row of the lateral column (Hartenstein and Campos-Ortega, 1984), and generates a diverse array of cell types including motorneurons, intersegmental interneurons, local interneurons, glial cells and sometimes a PNS sub-clone. In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A10 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments, and anterior (A1-A7) abdominal segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 9." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: This is equivalent to the 'dorsolateral neuroblast' of Truman and Bate (1988) - FBrf0047815, due to existence in A2-7 and large size of lineage (Lacin and Truman, 2016). Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres posterior to A7.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "dorsolateral neuroblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
synonym: "neuroblast dl" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001376 ! neuroblast NB5-2
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at stage 1 in the medial column (Hartenstein and Campos-Ortega, 1984). It generates a single motorneuron innervating muscle 12 via the SNb and a large number of interneurons, which constitute most of the posterior commissure (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S2-A8 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in at least S3-A7 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 6 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0076117, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0180161, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: This is equivalent to the 'ventromedial neuroblast' of Truman and Bate (1988) - FBrf0047815, due to existence in A2-7 and its relatively medial location (Lacin and Truman, 2016). Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres anterior to S3 (labial) or posterior to A7.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "medial SI neuroblast NB 5-2" RELATED []
synonym: "neuroblast vm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
synonym: "ventromedial neuroblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001377 ! neuroblast NB5-6
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates during S1 and generates subperineural glia, cell body glia and interneurons during the embryonic stage (Schmid et al., 1999). Its first division produces a glioblast and a neuroblast that does not produce any glia (Bernardoni et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A10 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). It dies in abdominal and thoracic segments by apoptosis during late embryogenesis (Baumgardt et al., 2009; Lacin and Truman, 2016), but survives to produce a secondary lineage in the labial neuromere (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0124972, FlyBase:FBrf0209429, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres anterior to S3 (labial).
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00052381 ! type I neuroglioblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001378 ! thoracic neuroblast NB5-6
def: "Neuroblast NB5-6 found in a thoracic segment. It generates 10 to 14 interneurons and 3 to 5 glial cells. It exits the cell cycle at stage 15 and dies via apoptosis at stage 16." [FlyBase:FBrf0098344, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0209429]
subset: cur
synonym: "NB 5-6T" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098344]
synonym: "NB5-6T" EXACT []
synonym: "neuroblast NB5-6 of thorax" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001379 ! abdominal neuroblast NB5-6
def: "Neuroblast NB5-6 found in an abdominal segment. It generates 3 to 5 interneurons and 2 to 6 glial cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0098344, FlyBase:FBrf0112030]
subset: cur
synonym: "NB 5-6A" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098344]
synonym: "NB5-6A" EXACT []
synonym: "neuroblast NB5-6 of abdomen" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001380 ! neuroblast NB7-1
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates in the first wave and generates the largest primary lineage, producing more than 40 cells in each hemisegment (Schmid et al., 1999). Its embryonic progeny include the U neurons and a large number of local interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in segments S3 to A1 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 3, located at the posterior border of the neuromere (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0180161, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres anterior to S3 (labial).
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001381 ! neuroblast NB7-4
def: "Neuroblast that generates several glia during the embryonic stage, including channel, subperineurial and cell body glia, as well as interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999; Beckervordersandforth et al., 2008). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A8 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in segments S3 to A1 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 23, which has its cell bodies located laterally, just ventral to the neuropil (Birkholz et al., 2015; Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0073294, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0180161, FlyBase:FBrf0205499, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres anterior to S3 (labial).
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00005147 ! neuroglioblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001382
name: neuroblast MP2
def: "Midline precursor cell that forms during the first wave of delamination in the medial column and divides only once (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S3-A10 and three are found in S1 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In abdominal and thoracic segments, it produces the intersegmental interneurons dMP2 and vMP2 (Schmid et al., 1999)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001383
name: stage 2 neuroblast
def: "A neuroblast delaminating in the second wave of neuroblast delamination from the ventral neuroectoderm. This stage begins in embryonic stage 9 ending in stage 10, and the neuroblasts primarily delaminate into the intermediate column (Doe, 1992)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0076117]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "S2 neuroblast" RELATED []
synonym: "SII neuroblast" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00005146 ! neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001384 ! neuroblast NB1-2
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates in the S2 wave and generates 4-6 intersegmental interneurons. It also produces approximately 20 local interneurons and, in thoracic segments, the semaphorin II (FBgn0011260) positive DC motorneuron. In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S2-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments and the first abdominal segment, generating secondary lineage 1 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0180161, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Originally referred to as NB1-1 by Doe (1992), this was renamed to NB1-2 by Broadus et al. (1995) to reflect the fact that it is the only engrailed-expressing anterior row neuroblast in both Drosophila and Schistocerca.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001383 ! stage 2 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001385 ! neuroblast NB2-2
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S2 and generates three to four primary motorneurons that innervate anterior lateral muscles via the SNa and a large number of interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A10 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 10 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055900, FlyBase:FBrf0084809, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Originally referred to as NB2-3 by Doe (1992), this was renamed to NB2-2 by Broadus et al. (1995) to keep the names of row 2 neuroblasts consistent with their position in Schistocerca.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001383 ! stage 2 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001386 ! thoracic neuroblast NB2-2
def: "Neuroblast NB2-2 found in a thoracic segment. In the embryonic phase, it produces a subperineurial glial cell in addition to neurons (Schmid et al., 1999; Beckervordersandforth et al., 2008). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments to produce postembryonic lineage 10 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0205499, FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
subset: cur
synonym: "NB2-2T" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205499]
synonym: "neuroblast NB2-2 of thorax" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001387 ! abdominal neuroblast NB2-2
def: "Neuroblast NB2-2 found in an abdominal segment. It does not produce a secondary lineage (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
subset: cur
synonym: "NB2-2A" EXACT []
synonym: "neuroblast NB2-2 of abdomen" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001388 ! neuroblast NB3-2
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S1 and generates around 6 motorneurons and a cluster of local interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S2-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in T1 to A1 segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 7 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Birkholz et al. (2015) suggest that NB3-2 generates postembryonic lineage 15 and NB4-2 generates postembryonic lineage 7, but Lacin and Truman (2016) provide lineage tracing and marker data showing that NB3-2 generates lineage 7. Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres anterior to S3 (labial).
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001389 ! neuroblast NB4-2
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S2 in the intermediate column and, in thoracic and abdominal segments, produces the RP2 motorneuron, which innervates muscles 2, 9 and 11, and the cousin of RP2 motorneuron (CoR), which innervates muscles 26, 27 and 29 (Schmid et al., 1999; Birkholz et al., 2013). It also generates around 19 interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 13 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Birkholz et al. (2015) suggest that NB4-2 generates postembryonic lineage 7 and NB3-3 generates postembryonic lineage 13, but Lacin and Truman (2016) provide lineage tracing and marker data showing that NB4-2 generates lineage 13.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001383 ! stage 2 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001390 ! neuroblast NB5-3
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S1 and generates an SNa motorneuron and intersegmental interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A8 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in at least all thoracic segments and A1-A7 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 5 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: This is equivalent to the 'ventrolateral neuroblast' of Truman and Bate (1988) - FBrf0047815, due to existence in A2-7 and its relatively lateral location (Lacin and Truman, 2016). Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres posterior to A7.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "neuroblast vl" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
synonym: "ventrolateral neuroblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
is_a: FBbt:00001370 ! stage 1 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001391 ! neuroblast NB6-2
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates in S2 in the intermediate column and, in thoracic and abdominal hemisegments, generates 8-16 primary interneurons that project in two bundles across the posterior commissure (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A8 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016), and it migrates dorsally during embryonic development (Lacin and Truman, 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in segments S3 to A2 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 19 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for neuromeres anterior to S3 (labial).
