[Term]
id: FBbt:00001414 ! neuroblast NB3-4
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S5 and produces a motorneuron, located on the posterior boundary of the clone, that projects into the anterior root of the ISN, as well as several interneurons (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A10 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments, producing postembryonic lineage 25, which contains motor neurons and glia (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Birkholz et al. (2015) suggest that NB3-4 generates postembryonic lineage 18, but Lacin and Truman (2016) identify lineage 25 and provide lineage tracing data showing that it is generated by NB3-4. Lacin and Truman (2016) only find this cell in thoracic segments in the embryo.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001420 ! stage 5 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00005147 ! neuroglioblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001415 ! neuroblast NB4-4
def: "Neuroblast that delaminates at S4 and generates a motorneuron and several interneurons during the embryonic stage (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S1-A9 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 24, composed exclusively of motorneurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001409 ! stage 4 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001416 ! neuroblast NB5-4
def: "Neuroblast that most frequently delaminates at S4 (Schmid et al., 1997). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each hemisegment from S3-A10 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in all thoracic segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016) and in the male abdominal 9 neuromere (Birkholz et al., 2013). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 22 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0098344, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0180161, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Using DiI with antibody labelling, Schmidt et al. (1997) propose NB5-4 produces 5-9 thoracic neurons or 3-4 abdominal motorneurons with ipsilateral targets. Schmid et al. (1999), also use DiI with en-GFP, but find 2-3 large cells that match descriptions of CCAP/CAP+ neurosecretory cells, along with abdomen-specific interneurons. Also, Schmid et al. (1999) state that NB5-4 delaminates during S5, whilst Schmidt et al. (1997) find that delamination occurs over the period of S3/4 to S5, most frequently at S4, and as such we have chosen to define NB5-4 as a stage 4 neuroblast.
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
subset: olfactory_system_draft
is_a: FBbt:00001409 ! stage 4 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001417 ! thoracic neuroblast NB5-4
def: "Neuroblast NB5-4 found in a thoracic segment. It resumes proliferation in the larva to generate postembryonic lineage 22 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
subset: cur
synonym: "neuroblast NB5-4 of thorax" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001418 ! abdominal neuroblast NB5-4
def: "Neuroblast NB5-4 found in an abdominal segment. In A9, it begins to express doublesex in the late embryo, resulting in sexually-dimorphic behavior in the larva (Birkholz et al., 2013). It does not produce a secondary lineage in A1-7 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
subset: cur
synonym: "neuroblast NB5-4 of abdomen" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001419 ! neuroblast MNB
def: "Unpaired neuroblast that forms from the mesectodermal cells of the ventral midline during the fourth wave of delamination (Schmid et al., 1999). During embryonic development, it gives rise to a cluster of around 8 cells with bilateral projections (Schmid et al., 1999). In the embryo, one of these cells can be found in each segment from S1-A10 (Birkholz et al., 2013; Urbach et al., 2016). In the larva, it resumes proliferation in segments S3 to A1 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). The neurons that develop from this neuroblast after larval hatching form postembryonic lineage 0 (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0072659, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0221210, FlyBase:FBrf0228122, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0232096]
comment: Lacin and Truman (2016) do not show data for segments anterior to S3.
subset: cur
