[Term]
id: FBbt:00001761
name: imaginal disc
def: "A sac shaped epithelial structure in the larva that gives rise to part of the adult integumentary system. One side of the sac consists of peripodial epithelium, the other of columnar epithelium. A single anterior-posterior compartment boundary bisects both peripodial membrane and columnar epithelium. Cells do not cross this boundary during growth and development of the disc." [FBC:GG]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
synonym: "imaginal disk" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00001760 ! larval imaginal tissue
is_a: FBbt:00007010 ! multi-tissue structure
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00001649 ! develops from imaginal disc primordium
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/320" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001762
name: peripodial epithelium
def: "A squamous epithelium that makes up one side of the epithelial sac of which each imaginal disc consists, with the other side being the columnar epithelium that will form the main adult structure generated by the disc (Gibson et al., 2000). The anterior-posterior compartment boundary of each disc runs through the middle of this epithelium. During the third larval instar stage, some of the cells in this epithelium send out long processes, known as lumenal extensions, which traverse the disc lumen to contact the columnar cells of the disc (Gibson et al., 2000). During metamorphosis, peripodial epithelia tend to give rise to parts of the body wall integument (Milner et al., 1984; Gibson et al., 2000)." [FlyBase:FBrf0041702, FlyBase:FBrf0131300]
subset: cur
synonym: "peripodial membrane" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0131300]
synonym: "squamous peripodial membrane" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0041702]
is_a: FBbt:00007028 ! squamous epithelium
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001761 ! part of imaginal disc

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001763
name: peripodial stalk
def: "Stalk that connects an imaginal disc to the larval epidermis (Milner et al., 1984; Aldaz and Escudero, 2010). Differentiated components of the adult can evaginate from the disc via this stalk during metamorphosis (Milner et al., 1984)." [FlyBase:FBrf0041702, FlyBase:FBrf0214885]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007003 ! portion of tissue
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00001761 ! continuous with imaginal disc
relationship: RO:0002371 FBbt:00005398 ! attached to embryonic/larval epidermis

