[Term]
id: FBbt:00001996
name: larval transverse nerve
def: "Nerve that exits the ventral nerve cord at the dorsal midline and bifurcates to form two lateral branches to the periphery (Gorczyca et al., 1994; Santos et al., 2006). These nerves are only found in abdominal segments (Gorczyca et al., 1994; Santos et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0075005, FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
comment: Santos et al. (2006) refer to the proximal region as the median nerve (MeN) and the post-branch point region as the transverse nerve.
