[Term]
id: FBbt:00002027
name: larval dorsal multidendritic neuron ddaC
def: "Larval class IV multidendritic neuron whose cell body is located fairly centrally among the dendritic arborizing neurons of the dorsal sensory cluster (Grueber et al., 2002; Orgogozo and Grueber, 2005). Its dendrites cover a dorsal region of the body wall of its segment and do not overlap with the dendrites of the anterior ventral (vdaa) neuron (Grueber et al., 2002). Its axon terminals are found in a dorsal region of the nociceptive neuropil (Li et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0148966, FlyBase:FBrf0183734, FlyBase:FBrf0244259]
comment: Following the classification system proposed by Grueber et al. (2002), ddaC is a class IV neuron.
subset: cur
synonym: "larval C4da D neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244259]
synonym: "larval class IV dendritic arborization dorsal neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244259]
is_a: FBbt:00007275 ! larval multidendritic class IV neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00007296 ! has soma location larval dorsal sensory cluster

