[Term]
id: FBbt:00002037
name: larval segmental nerve
def: "Larval nerve found in segments T1-A7 that has two roots, both carrying fibers from the neuromere of the nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It exits the lateral ventral nerve cord in line with the anterior commissure and its proximal region shares a glial sheath with the intersegmental nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It does not extend as far dorsally as the intersegmental nerve, and mainly innervates ventral muscles and sense organs (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "larval SN" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior fascicle" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00005105 ! nerve
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005893 ! part of larval peripheral nervous system

