[Term]
id: FBbt:00002041
name: obsolete vesA neuron
def: "Sensory PNS neuron of embryonic/larval abdominal segments 1-7, the pro-, meta- or mesothoracic segments (Dambly-Chaudiere and Ghysen, 1986). In the thoracic segments it innervates the anterior lateral hair of the Keilin organ. In the abdominal segments it is located ventral to vesB." [FlyBase:FBrf0045359, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: Obsoleted as thoracic and abdominal vesA neurons innervate different sense organs, so should not be considered to belong to the same segmentally-repeated type. Suggesting 'larval segmental nerve sensory neuron' as replacement as this is the closest shared parent of abdominal and thoracic (Keilin organ) vesA neurons.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00002038

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002042
name: obsolete vesB neuron
def: "Sensory PNS neuron of embryonic/larval abdominal segments 1-7, the pro-, meta- or mesothoracic segments (Dambly-Chaudiere and Ghysen, 1986). In the thoracic segments it innervates the anterior medial hair of the Keilin organ, together with the vesC neuron. In the abdominal segments it is located dorsal to vesA and ventral to vesC." [FlyBase:FBrf0045359, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: Obsoleted as thoracic and abdominal vesB neurons innervate different sense organs, so should not be considered to belong to the same segmentally-repeated type. Suggesting 'larval segmental nerve sensory neuron' as replacement as this is the closest shared parent of abdominal and thoracic (Keilin organ) vesB neurons.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00002038

