[Term]
id: FBbt:00002142
name: larval metathoracic intersegmental nerve
def: "Larval intersegmental nerve of the metathoracic segment. Similar to the A1-A7 nerves, it has two roots; an anterior root that is formed by neurons of the anteriorly adjacent neuromere, and a posterior root, that is formed by neurons of the same neuromere as the nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Proximally it shares a glial sheath with the segmental nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It receives a branch from the metathoracic lateral sensory cluster (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its main trunk continues dorsally and innervates the dorsal sensory cluster and dorsal musculature (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "ISN" BROAD []
synonym: "metathoracic anterior fascicle" EXACT []

