[Term]
id: FBbt:00002197
name: larval abdominal segmental nerve
alt_id: FBbt:00002450
def: "Larval segmental nerve of a larval abdominal segment. These are only found in segments A1-7, as A8 and A9 do not have separate segmental and intersegmental nerves (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It has two roots, anterior and posterior, both formed from neurons of the same segment as the nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Proximally it shares a glial sheath with the intersegmental nerve before branching from it at the ventral edge of the ventral oblique muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). A thick, posteriorly directed branch (SNc) leaves the main trunk of the nerve (SNa) and splits into fine branches - 3 carrying axons from the ventral sensory cluster and a 4th carrying efferents to the ventral acute musculature (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The SNa branch continues dorsally and carries efferent axons innervating the external lateral transverse and lateral oblique muscles and the axons of v'es2 and v'ch1 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0099344]
subset: cur
synonym: "larval abdominal posterior fascicle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval abdominal SN" EXACT []
synonym: "larval segmental nerve of A1-7" EXACT []
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1565" xsd:anyURI

