[Term]
id: FBbt:00002434
name: larval abdominal lateral multidendritic neuron ldaA
alt_id: FBbt:00002035
def: "Class II multidendritic neuron with its cell body in a lateral sensory cluster of a larval abdominal segment (Grueber et al., 2002). It develops from a common precursor with the abdominal lesA neuron (Brewster and Bodmer, 1995; Veling et al., 2019). It is remodeled into the adult ldaA neuron during metamorphosis (Shimono et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0083795, FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0148966, FlyBase:FBrf0209127, FlyBase:FBrf0244192, FlyPNS:PNSdescription.html#ldaA]
comment: Disambiguation - there is a multidendritic neuron of the lateral sensory cluster of T2 and T3 with the name ldaA (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997), but this likely reflects a naming coincidence rather than indicating they should be classified with the ldaA neurons of A1-7.
subset: cur
synonym: "abdominal lateral multidendritic neuron lda" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "abdominal lda" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
