[Term]
id: FBbt:00002517
name: abdominal anterior ventral multidendritic neuron vdaa
def: "Larval class IV multidendritic neuron with its soma located relatively anteriorly in the dorsal (v') part of a ventral sensory cluster of an abdominal segment (Grueber et al., 2002; Orgogozo and Grueber, 2005). Its dendrites cover a lateral region of the body wall of its segment and do not overlap with the dendrites of the dorsal (ddaC) or ventral (vdaB) neurons (Grueber et al., 2002). It develops from a common precursor with the abdominal v'esB neuron (Brewster and Bodmer, 1995; Veling et al., 2019). Its axon terminals are initially found in the ventral nociceptive neuropil, alongside vdaB (Li et al., 2019). In the early second instar, these terminals separate, leaving vdaa in an intermediate position between ddaC and vdaB (Li et al., 2019). It is remodeled into the adult vdaa neuron during metamorphosis (Shimono et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0083795, FlyBase:FBrf0148966, FlyBase:FBrf0183734, FlyBase:FBrf0209127, FlyBase:FBrf0244192, FlyBase:FBrf0244259, FlyPNS:PNSdescription.html#vmd4a]
subset: cur
synonym: "larval C4da M neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244259]
synonym: "larval class IV dendritic arborization middle neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244259]
synonym: "v'ada" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0183734]
synonym: "vmd4a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0151928, FlyBase:FBrf0183734]
is_a: FBbt:00007275 ! larval multidendritic class IV neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00052122 ! has soma location larval ventral' sensory cluster of A1-7
