[Term]
id: FBbt:00002598
name: larval abdominal 1 median nerve
def: "Median nerve that exits the dorsal part of abdominal neuromere 1 (Santos et al., 2006). It has a large swelling, corresponding to an abdominal neurohemal organ. It does not give rise to transverse nerves in the first instar (Gorczyca et al., 1994), but does branch relatively proximally to produce these nerves in the third instar (Santos et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0075005, FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
subset: cur
synonym: "MeN-1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002599
name: larval abdominal 2 median nerve
def: "Median nerve that exits the dorsal part of abdominal neuromere 2 (Santos et al., 2006). It has a slightly smaller swelling than the A1 nerve, corresponding to an abdominal neurohemal organ, and it bifurcates relatively proximally to give rise to two transverse nerves (Santos et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
subset: cur
synonym: "MeN-2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002600
name: larval abdominal 3 median nerve
def: "Median nerve that exits the dorsal part of abdominal neuromere 3 (Santos et al., 2006). It has a smaller swelling than the two anterior nerves, corresponding to an abdominal neurohemal organ, and it bifurcates relatively proximally to give rise to two transverse nerves (Santos et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
subset: cur
synonym: "MeN-3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002601
name: larval abdominal 4 median nerve
def: "Median nerve that exits the dorsal part of abdominal neuromere 3 (Santos et al., 2006). It does not possess a swelling at its base (Santos et al., 2006), but still bifurcates relatively proximally to form two transverse nerves (Gorczyca et al., 1994)." [FlyBase:FBrf0075005, FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
subset: cur
synonym: "MeN-4" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002602
name: larval abdominal 5 median nerve
def: "Median nerve that exits the dorsal part of abdominal neuromere 5 (Santos et al., 2006). It does not possess a swelling at its base (Santos et al., 2006), and bifurcates more distally than more anterior nerves, to form two transverse nerves (Gorczyca et al., 1994)." [FlyBase:FBrf0075005, FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
subset: cur
synonym: "MeN-5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002603
name: larval abdominal 6 median nerve
def: "Median nerve that exits the dorsal part of abdominal neuromere 6 (Santos et al., 2006). It does not possess a swelling at its base (Santos et al., 2006), and bifurcates more distally than more anterior nerves, to form two transverse nerves (Gorczyca et al., 1994)." [FlyBase:FBrf0075005, FlyBase:FBrf0195119]
subset: cur
synonym: "MeN-6" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195119]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002604
