comment: Not clear from Santos et al. (2006) - FBrf0195119 whether this exists in third instar.
subset: cur

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002606
name: larval abdominal 8 nerve
def: "Nerve of larval abdominal segment 8 that has features of both the intersegmental and segmental nerves of more anterior segments (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). This nerve has three roots, in a pattern corresponding the roots of the segmental and intersegmental nerves of A1-7 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its proximal section is closely attached to the abdominal 9 nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It carries motor neurons that innervate the ventral longitudinal and lateral transverse muscles of A8, and sensory neurons innervating the spiracular hairs and the A8 sensilla (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "abdominal 8 intersegmental nerve" RELATED []
synonym: "embryonic/larval abdominal 8 nerve" EXACT []
