[Term]
id: FBbt:00002618
name: larval abdominal 9 nerve
def: "Nerve of larval abdominal segment 9 that has features of both the intersegmental and segmental nerves of more anterior segments (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It has two roots and its proximal section is closely attached to the abdominal 8 nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). After passing beneath the gut suspensor muscles, it gives off a thick recurrent branch, the hindgut nerve, which innervates the hindgut (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its main branch continues dorsoposteriorly and gives off a motor branch that innervates the A9 terminal oblique muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). A posterior branch carries sensory axons from the anal sense organ and a dorsal branch carries axons of motor and sensory neurons of A9 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "larval abdominal 9 intersegmental nerve" RELATED []
synonym: "nerve of a9" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00005105 ! nerve
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001756 ! part of larval abdominal segment 9
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00052537 ! continuous with larval hindgut nerve
