[Term]
id: FBbt:00002684
name: associated organ
def: "A cluster of 4-6 sensory neurons of the intercalary segment attached to the basal aspect of neurons belonging to the terminal organ (Schmidt-Ott et al., 1994; Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). These neurons have no associated cuticular structure and do not have the typical morphology of bipolar sensory neurons (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0075072, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: Neurons might be multidendritic (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997).
