[Term]
id: FBbt:00002720
name: larval labial organ
def: "Compound external sense organ of the late embryo or larva that is located in the lower lip of the external opening of the atrium (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997; Richter et al., 2024). It consists of 3 sensilla, one with 3 neurons and the others with one each (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Neurons of the labial organ and ventral pharyngeal sense organ form a large cluster flanking the salivary duct (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.91155.2, FlyBase:FBrf0034076, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: Richter et al. (2024) only find the two mono-innervated sensilla on the external larva.
