[Term]
id: FBbt:00002966
name: pupal cerebral tracheal branch
def: "A pupal specific tracheal branch that arises from the cerebropharyngeal branch, lateral to the cerebral anastomosis and anterior to the pharyngeal branch. It tracheates the developing eyes and brain." [FlyBase:FBrf0011558, FlyBase:FBrf0034081, FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
comment: Figure 23 of Manning and Krasnow (1993) establishes a correspondence between their nomenclature and the one used by Whitten (1957) - FBrf0011558 in figure 2. To note, however, that the larval cerebral branch (FBbt:00000395) corresponds to the dorsal cervical posterior branch (as in table 1 of Manning and Krasnow (1993)), not to the anterior one.
subset: cur
synonym: "dorsal cervical anterior pupal trachea" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0011558]
