intersection_of: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004642 ! part of tibia

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003177
name: obsolete wing pulsatile organ
def: "Pulsatile organ of the wing. There are 5 of these, all located in or near the wing hinge. They all beat independently of the main heartbeat and asynchronously with each other except for 3 and 4 which pulsate synchronously." [FlyBase:FBrf0031012]
comment: Obsoleted - there is only one (bilateral) pair of pulsatile organs per organism that circulate hemolymph to the wings (Lehmacher et al., 2009 - FBrf0206946), making this equivalent to FBbt:00003174 "scutellar pulsatile organ".
