[Term]
id: FBbt:00003185
name: adult oenocyte
def: "Large, acidophilic cell found in rows under the epidermis of each abdominal segment. Two dorsal rows run from the heart tube to the spiracle, close to the posterior boundary of the segment. A single, or sometimes split, transverse row is found under each sternite." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004995 ! oenocyte
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00007317 ! part of adult oenocyte band

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003186
name: adult dorsal oenocyte band
def: "Dorsal band of adult oenocytes that extends from the spiracle to the heart (Miller, 1950). There is one of these on each side of each of abdominal segments 1-7 in females, but in males the A6 and A7 bands are merged into a single group (Miller, 1950). The band of abdominal segment 1 extends further after reaching the heart, whereas others terminate at the heart (Miller, 1950). Oenocytes at the lower end of the strand lie flat against the trachea, then the band extends backwards and upwards on the inner side of the fat body along the posterior edge of the tergite and outside the dorsal longitudinal muscles (Miller, 1950)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
subset: cur
synonym: "adult dorsal strand of oenocytes" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "adult tergal oenocyte band" EXACT []
synonym: "dorsal group of adult oenocytes" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "oenocytes of adult tergite" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007317 ! adult oenocyte band

