[Term]
id: FBbt:00003667
name: adult lateral ellipsoid fascicle
def: "A transverse tract within the protocerebrum of the adult brain that is connected to the inferior medial/lateral protocerebrum and the central complex (Strausfeld, 1976; Lovick et al., 2013). It passes ventral to the mushroom body medial lobe (Lovick et al., 2013). It connects the bulb and the fan-shaped body (Ito et al., 2014). It has an anterior component, contributed to by the DALv2/3 and DALcl2 lineages, and a posterior component, containing fibers of BAmv1 neurons entering via the medial ventral longitudinal fascicle (Lovick et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, FlyBase:FBrf0239233, FlyBase:FBrf0239234, FlyBase:FBrf0240929]
