[Term]
id: FBbt:00003835
name: proximal medullary amacrine neuron Pm2
def: "Proximal medullary wide-field amacrine neuron that projects along M7 and branches extensively at the M7/M8 boundary with each branch projecting into medulla layer M9 where it forms an arbor with mixed bleb-type and fine terminals (Morante and Desplan, 2008; Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652]
comment: Neurotransmitter determined to be glutamate based on vGlut[CNSIII]-GAL4 driver (FBti0129148) expression (Raghu and Borst, 2011 - FBrf0213690), but scRNAseq data assigns as GABA based on Gad1 transcripts and lineage (Konstantinides et al., 2022 - FBrf0253187). Nern et al. (2025) - FBrf0262545 identify two subtypes (Pm2a and Pm2b) in the EM data, but do not distinguish these at light level.
subset: cur
synonym: "Pm03" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0260545]
synonym: "Pm08" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0260545]
