[Term]
id: FBbt:00003918
name: dorsal giant horizontal cell HSN
def: "Horizontal system neuron whose dendritic arbor extends over the dorsal lobula plate (Scott et al., 2002). The area covered by its dendrite corresponds to the center of the large dorsal field of vision. It is electrically coupled to HSE and HSS (Schnell et al., 2010). There is one of these cells on each side (Shinomiya et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0032046, FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0179400, FlyBase:FBrf0210299, FlyBase:FBrf0254308]
comment: Electrical coupling was shown indirectly by neurobiotin dye coupling in HSN and HSE cells labelled using the P\{GawB\}CG1090[NP0282] (FBti0033586) driver (Schnell et al., 2010). Due to their morphology and functional similarity, this cell is judged to be homologous to the dorsal horizontal system cell in larger flies (Heisenberg et al., 1978; Rajashekhar and Shamprasad, 2004; Scott et al., 2002).
subset: cur
synonym: "dorsal horizontal neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "horizontal system north" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0229441]
synonym: "horizontal system north cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0254308]
synonym: "HS north" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
synonym: "LPT01" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634]
is_a: FBbt:00003917 ! horizontal system neuron
relationship: RO:0002003 FBbt:00003919 ! electrically_synapsed_to equatorial giant horizontal cell HSE
relationship: RO:0002003 FBbt:00003920 ! electrically_synapsed_to ventral giant horizontal cell HSS

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003919
name: equatorial giant horizontal cell HSE
def: "Horizontal system neuron whose dendritic arbor extends over the central lobula plate (Scott et al., 2002). It has both synaptic input and output in the axon terminal in the protocerebral region (Raghu et al., 2007). The area covered by its dendrite corresponds to the center of the large equatorial field of vision. It is electrically coupled to HSN and HSS (Schnell et al., 2010). There is one of these cells on each side (Shinomiya et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0032046, FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0179400, FlyBase:FBrf0200428, FlyBase:FBrf0207482, FlyBase:FBrf0210299, FlyBase:FBrf0254308]
comment: Electrical coupling was shown indirectly by neurobiotin dye coupling in HSN and HSE cells labelled using the P\{GawB\}CG1090[NP0282] (FBti0033586) driver (Schnell et al., 2010). The postsynaptic terminals in the protocerebral region were identified by the presence of a subunit of the GABA receptor (Rdl) in horizontal system cells labelled with P\{UAS-Rdl.HA\} (FBtp0021350] driven by the P\{GAL4\}3A driver [FBti0131277) (Raghu et al., 2007). Due to their morphology and functional similarity, this cell is judged to be homologous to the equatorial horizontal system cell in larger flies (Heisenberg et al., 1978; Rajashekhar and Shamprasad, 2004; Scott et al., 2002).
subset: cur
synonym: "horizontal system equatorial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0254308]
synonym: "HS equatorial" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
synonym: "LPT02" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634]
is_a: FBbt:00003917 ! horizontal system neuron
relationship: RO:0002003 FBbt:00003918 ! electrically_synapsed_to dorsal giant horizontal cell HSN
relationship: RO:0002003 FBbt:00003920 ! electrically_synapsed_to ventral giant horizontal cell HSS
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007145 ! receives synaptic input in region adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003920
name: ventral giant horizontal cell HSS
def: "Horizontal system neuron whose dendritic arbor extends over the ventral lobula plate. It is a glutamatergic neuron (Raghu and Borst, 2011). There is one of these cells on each side (Shinomiya et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0213690, FlyBase:FBrf0254308]
comment: The neurotransmitter was assessed by labelling cells with a vGlut[CNSIII]-GAL4 driver (FBti0129148) (Raghu and Borst, 2011).
