[Term]
id: FBbt:00004045
name: LNd neuron
def: "Lateral period-expressing neuron (LN) of the adult brain whose cell body is located in the dorsal-most cluster of LNs. There are six of these cells per hemisphere (Schubert et al., 2018; Ma et al., 2021). Initially all LNds follow the anterior optic tract (AOT) to the surface of the lateral horn (LH) (Schubert et al., 2018). These neurons project axons to the dorsal protocerebrum and terminate predominantly in the neuropil region close to the pars intercerebralis. These projections overlap with those of the DN neurons and many project contralaterally through the dorsal fusion commissure. These cells are a heterogeneous population with different combinations of cryptochrome (CRY), ion transport peptide (ITP) and neuropeptide F (sNPF) expression (Schubert et al., 2018). They are evening cells (Liang et al., 2016; Liang et al., 2017; Delventhal et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0193849, FlyBase:FBrf0205220, FlyBase:FBrf0225654, FlyBase:FBrf0231110, FlyBase:FBrf0235909, FlyBase:FBrf0238313, FlyBase:FBrf0243753, FlyBase:FBrf0247880]
comment: Projection of axons vs dendrites judged on the basis of the presence (dendrites) or absence (axons) of synaptobrevin (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2007).
synonym: "dorsal adult lateral neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "dorsolateral neurons" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193849]
is_a: FBbt:00004044 ! LN period neuron
is_a: FBbt:00049636 ! adult evening cell
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00100337 ! fasciculates with adult anterior optic tract

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004046
name: LNv neuron
def: "Lateral period-expressing neuron (LN) of the adult brain whose cell body is located in the ventral cluster of LNs, at the level of the esophageal foramen (Helfrich-Forster, 1998). It has neurites associated with the accessory medulla (aMe) (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2007). The LN neuronal group are necessary and sufficient for generation of robust adult locomotor rhythms in the absence of environmental cues (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2007). There are approximately nine of these cells per hemisphere (Ma et al., 2021). They are peptidergic, with eight per hemisphere expressing Pdf and the other expressing ion transport peptide (Johard et al., 2009; Ma et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0056576, FlyBase:FBrf0101921, FlyBase:FBrf0123172, FlyBase:FBrf0193849, FlyBase:FBrf0208477, FlyBase:FBrf0247880]
comment: Assertion that LNvs are necessary and sufficient for locomotor rhythms based on mosaic analysis (Ewer et al., 1992), and by similarity of period-mutant flies to those with ablation of Pdf-expressing neurons (i.e. all LNvs except one cell), (Renn et al., 1999).
synonym: "lateral neuron ventral" RELATED []
synonym: "ventral adult lateral neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "ventral lateral neurons" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00004044 ! LN period neuron
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0030072 ! capable of peptide hormone secretion
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00045003 ! has synaptic IO in region accessory medulla

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004047
name: adult hypocerebral ganglion
def: "Ganglion of the adult nervous system, found between the esophagus and the aorta (Mahishi and Huetteroth, 2019). It is fused to the corpus cardiacum (Predel et al., 2004; Mahishi and Huetteroth, 2019) and is part of the adult ring gland (Hartenstein, 1993). It is connected to the tritocerebrum via the stomodeal nerve and receives sensory input from the esophagus, aorta and anterior midgut (Mahishi and Huetteroth, 2019). It contributes to the innervation of the crop (Hadjieconomou et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0034076, FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0179393, FlyBase:FBrf0239029, FlyBase:FBrf0244208, FlyBase:FBrf0247015, FlyBase:FBrf0247320]
comment: Min et al. (2021) - FBrf0248237 casually mention that the hypocerebral ganglion and the adjacent corpora cardiaca together contain approximately 35 neurons, including 20 Akh-expressing neurons, 5 mechanosensory neurons expressing Piezo, and 5 chemosensory neurons expressing Gr43a.
subset: cur
synonym: "adult esophageal ganglion" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0034076]
synonym: "adult pharyngeal ganglion" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0034076]
synonym: "adult ventricular ganglion" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0034076]
synonym: "HG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247015]
synonym: "StG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244208]
