[Term]
id: FBbt:00004155
name: mechano-chemo-sensory labral sensillum
def: "Sensillum of the adult labral sense organ (LSO) in the adult pharynx that is innervated both one mechanosensory and one gustatory receptor neuron (Nayak and Singh, 1983; Chen and Dahanukar, 2017). There are 2 of these sensilla per LSO and they are the most distal of the nine labral organ sensilla (Nayak and Singh, 1983; Chen and Dahanukar, 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0074012, FlyBase:FBrf0237413]
