[Term]
id: FBbt:00004239
name: ocellus cornea
def: "Chitinous extracellular laminar secretion that covers the adult ocelli. The lens is laminated with around 45 strata. Underlying it is a monolayer of corneagenous cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0050358]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004241 ! part of ocellus lens

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004240
name: ocellus corneagenous cell
def: "Corneagenous cells of the adult ocellus. The cells form a monolayer that separates the ocellus cornea from the rhabdomeres." [FlyBase:FBrf0050358]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004192 ! corneagenous cell
is_a: FBbt:00005163 ! sensory organ cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004241 ! part of ocellus lens

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004241
name: ocellus lens
def: "Lens of an adult ocellus. It is composed of the outer cornea and underlying monolayer of corneagenous cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0050358]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004505 ! part of ocellus

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004242
name: ocellar retinula cell
def: "Photoreceptor cell of an adult ocellus. It expresses the violet-sensitive Rh2 (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). Its axons are found proximal to its nucleus, and they target their corresponding ocellar ganglion (Caldwell et al., 2007). The lateral ocelli each have around 100 photoreceptor cells, whereas the medial one has around 75 (Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Some of these cells directly target the lobula or lobula plate (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). These cells aid flight stabilization and augment the phototactic response (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). They form simpler circuits with fewer connections before reaching the central brain, resulting in faster transmission of information (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0050358, FlyBase:FBrf0200339, FlyBase:FBrf0255165, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
subset: cur
synonym: "ocellar photoreceptor cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0255165]
synonym: "ocellus photoreceptor" EXACT []
synonym: "ocellus retinula cell" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007251 ! rhabdomeric photoreceptor cell
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00004505 ! overlaps ocellus
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0042331 ! capable of part of phototaxis
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0003248 ! expresses Rh2
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00049817 ! sends synaptic output to region ocellar ganglion
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/2006" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004243
name: ocellus rhabdomere
def: "Rhabdomere of the adult ocellus. In contrast to the ones in the compound eye, it is open on its distal lateral surface." [FlyBase:FBrf0050358]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004212 ! rhabdomere
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004242 ! part of ocellar retinula cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004244
name: ocellus pigment granule
def: "Pigment granule of the photoreceptor cell of the adult ocellus. Pigment granules are found distally around the rim of the ocellus, and proximally down from the level of the nucleus. They are composed of ommatins (brown color pigments) which do not migrate in response to light." [FlyBase:FBrf0050358]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004234 ! pigment granule
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004242 ! part of ocellar retinula cell

