[Term]
id: FBbt:00004483
name: ptilinum
def: "Membranous sac that is part of the front of the head capsule. It is everted at eclosion and serves to break open the operculum at the end of the puparium. Following eclosion, it is withdrawn into the head where it collapses and becomes sclerotized, externally leaving the ptilinal suture." [FlyBase:FBrf0007310, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007284 ! region of integument
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004482 ! part of adult head capsule
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00110832 ! develops from presumptive ptilinum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004484
name: ptilinal suture
def: "Suture across the front of the head, in between the eyes and just dorsal to the base of the antennae. It is a remnant of the internalization of the ptilinum after eclosion." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004479 ! suture
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004483 ! part of ptilinum

