[Term]
id: FBbt:00004547
name: salivary stylet
def: "Papilla located just posterior to the oral opening that bears the opening of the adult salivary duct at its apex." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
comment: Ferris, 1950 claims that the hypopharynx does not exist in D.melanogaster, although the salivary stylet is often mistaken for it. It seems likely that the salivary stylet (FBbt:00004547) and the hypopharynx described by Bodenstein, 1950 (FBbt:00003130) are the same structure.
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007288 ! integumentary specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004540 ! part of rostrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004548
name: fused cervical sclerite
def: "Triangular sclerite located in the anterior thorax, lateral to the neck (Gorko et al., 2024). Anteriorly it forms a point where the neck meets the head (Gorko et al., 2024). It is formed from two (anterior and posterior) sclerites that are fused into a single composite structure (Ferris, 1950; Fabian et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0233988, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004550 ! part of neck

