[Term]
id: FBbt:00004580
name: mesonotum
def: "Dorsal part of the external adult mesothorax. It is composed of four partially fused regions, the prescutum, scutum, scutellum and postnotum (Fabian et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0037040, FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
comment: Sometimes referred to as the notum. Strictly, notum refers to the upper part (tergum) of a thoracic segment (McAlpine, 1981), so there are 3 nota; the pro-, meso- and meta-notum.
