[Term]
id: FBbt:00004653
name: pretarsus
def: "The most distal segment of the adult leg. This segment is highly derived and bears the claws." [FlyBase:FBim0000836, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0111704, FlyBase:FBrf0219028]
comment: Schubiger et al. (2012) list this as part of the tarsus (fifth tarsal segment).
subset: cur
synonym: "claw organ" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0219028]
is_a: FBbt:00007018 ! appendage segment
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004640 ! part of leg

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004654
name: auxilia
def: "A small, lateral sclerite of the pretarsus. Each pretarsus has a symmetrical pair of these structures - one proximal to each claw (unguis)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0111704]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004655
name: pulvillus
def: "Lateral lobe of the pretarsus, ventral to the auxiliae and proximal to the claws (unguis). It consists of a proximal, stiffer base part and a more flexible part, as well as approximately 30 setae (Husken et al., 2015). The setae are hair-like cuticle outgrowths that differentiate from epidermal cells and have spatula-like terminal contact zones (Husken et al., 2015; Kimura et al., 2020; Tanaka et al., 2023). Fluid secretions coat these terminal contact zones, facilitating adhesion to smooth surfaces and leaving footprints where the fly walks (Husken et al., 2015). There are two of these per leg (Husken et al., 2015; Tanaka et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0111704, FlyBase:FBrf0228206, FlyBase:FBrf0256338]
subset: cur
synonym: "adhesive organ" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0228206]
synonym: "adhesive pad" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0228206]
synonym: "footpad" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0256338]
synonym: "plantula" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
is_a: FBbt:00007596 ! integumentary process
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00052778 ! develops from footpad hair cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004656
name: pulvillar membrane
def: "Membrane that is found between the pulvillus and the unguis (claw)." [FlyBase:FBrf0010489, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00100313 ! multicellular structure
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004657
name: ungulfus
def: "Median process of the pretarsus that articulates with the claws (unguis)." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0239229]
subset: cur
synonym: "unguifer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0010489, FlyBase:FBrf0239229]
is_a: FBbt:00007596 ! integumentary process
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004658
name: unguitractor plate
def: "A small ventral, median sclerite of the pretarsus that is partially invaginated into the end of the 5th tarsal segment and is the attachment site of the attachment of a long tendon connected to the pretarsal depressor muscle." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0111704]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004659
name: empodium
def: "A spine-like process that lies in a medial position on the base of the foot (pretarsus) between the two claws (unguis)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0111704]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007596 ! integumentary process
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004660
name: unguis
def: "The paired, hollow chitinous hooks at the end of the pretarsus. These are sclerotized extensions of the integument (i.e. they consist of underlying epidermis and overlying cuticle)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0111704, FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
synonym: "claw" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
is_a: FBbt:00007596 ! integumentary process
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004653 ! part of pretarsus
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046029 ! develops from presumptive unguis

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004661
name: unguis scale
def: "Scale present on the dorsal surface of the unguis, close to the mid-point of the long axis of the unguis." [FlyBase:FBrf0010489, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004660 ! part of unguis

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004662
name: seta of pulvillus
def: "Seta (hair) of found on a pulvillus (Husken et al., 2015). It has a thin spatula-like tip, which is coated in fluid secretions and forms a contact zone allowing for adhesion to smooth surfaces (Husken et al., 2015). It does not have an opening near its tip, indicating that fluid secretion may be from porous channels in the setal cuticle (Husken et al., 2015). There are approximately 30 of these per pulvillus (Husken et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0166419, FlyBase:FBrf0228206, FlyBase:FBrf0256338]
subset: cur
synonym: "footpad hair" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0256338]
synonym: "pulvillar seta" EXACT []
synonym: "retineria" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
is_a: FBbt:00007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004655 ! part of pulvillus
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00052778 ! develops from footpad hair cell

