intersection_of: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004733
name: pleural wing sclerite
def: "Ventrally located sclerite of the wing hinge, located immediately posterior to the pleural wing process (FBbt:00004595) and distal to the axillary pouch (FBbt:00004745)." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "pleural sclerite" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004734
name: humeral sclerite
def: "An anteriorly located sclerite of the wing hinge, closely associated with the anterior arm of the 1st axillary sclerite (FBbt:00004738). It is immediately distal to the tegula (FBbt:00004730) and its distal end as associates with the proximal end of the costal vein." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
synonym: "humeral plate" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00059379 ! develops from presumptive humeral sclerite

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004735
name: median sclerite
def: "Small sclerite at the base of the anal veins." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
subset: cur
synonym: "median plate" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004736
name: unnamed wing hinge sclerite
def: "Small sclerite of the wing hinge that lies immediately posterior to the humeral sclerite (FBbt:00004734) and closely associated with the 1st axillary sclerite (FBbt:00004738)." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
comment: The designation 'unnamed' probably originates with Ferris (1950), who follows Snodgrass (1935) in naming wing hinge plates and notes that there is 'one small sclerite that seems to be additional to the usual number'.
subset: cur
synonym: "unnamed plate" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
synonym: "unnamed sclerite" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00084736 ! develops from presumptive unnamed wing hinge sclerite

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004737
name: axillary sclerite
def: "One of a small group of small sclerites in the middle and posterior of the wing hinge that function in articulation of the wing. Except for the proximal region of the 4th axillary sclerite, they are hairless." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0111704]
subset: cur
synonym: "pterale" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098527]
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004738
name: 1st axillary sclerite
def: "Sclerite of the wing hinge that articulates with the notal wing processes and the 2nd axillary sclerite. Its anterior end is immediately posterior to the humeral sclerite (FBbt:00004734)." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "pterale I" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098527]
is_a: FBbt:00004737 ! axillary sclerite
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00084738 ! develops from presumptive 1st axillary sclerite

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004739
name: 2nd axillary sclerite
def: "A small, irregularly shaped sclerite of the wing hinge, located immediately distal to the 1st axillary sclerite (FBbt:00004738) with which it articulates." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "pterale II" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098527]
is_a: FBbt:00004737 ! axillary sclerite
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00084739 ! develops from presumptive 2nd axillary sclerite

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004740
name: 3rd axillary sclerite
def: "A small sclerite of the wing hinge, located immediately anterior to the alula (FBbt:00004747)." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "pterale III" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098527]
is_a: FBbt:00004737 ! axillary sclerite
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00084740 ! develops from presumptive 3rd axillary sclerite

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004741
name: 4th axillary sclerite
def: "The most posterior and proximal of the sclerites of the wing hinge. The proximal end of this sclerite is adjacent to the distal end of the posterior notal wing process." [FlyBase:FBim0000802, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "pterale IV" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098527]
is_a: FBbt:00004737 ! axillary sclerite
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00084741 ! develops from presumptive 4th axillary sclerite

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004742
name: basal sclerite
def: "Small sclerite of the wing that is embedded in the pleural membrane ventrally adjacent to where the wing articulates (Sink, 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0098527, FlyBase:FBrf0192609, FlyBase:FBrf0193310]
subset: cur
synonym: "basalare" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098527]
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004743
name: yellow club
def: "Club-shaped, anteriorly located ventral sclerite of the wing hinge." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00004475 ! sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004744
name: axillary cord
def: "A thickened, corrugated region of the posterior margin of the wing hinge. It has a crenellated appearance and harbors a single row of short, fine hairs (Bryant, 1975)." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793, FlyBase:FBrf0111704]
comment: Ferris (1950) - FBrf0007734 notes that 'alula' may refer to either a proximal lobe of the posterior wing (='alar lobe') or the membranous area between this lobe and the body, which is referred to as 'axillary cord' in Bryant (1975).
subset: cur
synonym: "alula" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00085378 ! section of wing margin
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00084745 ! develops from presumptive axillary cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004745
name: axillary pouch
def: "A pouch-shaped specialization of the integument located at the base of the ventral side of the wing hinge, adjacent to the pleural wing process." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007288 ! integumentary specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004747
name: alar lobe
alt_id: FBbt:00004746
def: "A small lobe at the posterior base of the wing (Ferris, 1950; Bryant, 1975). It has extremely long marginal hairs (Bryant, 1975)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
comment: Ferris (1950) notes that 'alula' may refer to either a proximal lobe of the posterior wing (='alar lobe') or the membranous area between this lobe and the body, which is referred to as 'axillary cord' in Bryant (1975).
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
synonym: "alula" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00100313 ! multicellular structure
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004731 ! part of wing hinge

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004748
name: wing septum
def: "Septum on the dorsal surface of the wing, in the radial vein." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00047863 ! part of radial vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004749
name: radius septum 1
def: "Most proximal of the two septa of the radius, located between the proximal radius (containing the Sc25 sensilla) and the medial radius (containing the Sc12 sensilla) (Bryant, 1975)." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "sep1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
synonym: "wing septum 1" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004748 ! wing septum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004750
name: radius septum 2
def: "Most distal of the two septa of the radius, located between the medial radius (containing the Sc12 sensilla) and the distal radius (containing the Sc1 sensilla) (Bryant, 1975)." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
subset: cur
synonym: "sep2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0027793]
synonym: "wing septum 2" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004748 ! wing septum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004751
name: wing vein
def: "Wing veins are epidermal sclerotizations above hemolymph lacunae that run between the dorsal and the ventral wing surfaces and carry trachea and nerves. The two-dimensional pattern of wing veins is the result of the cuticular differentiation of stripes of epidermal cells on the wing blade, which can be contrasted with the two-dimensional pattern of sensory organs derived from discrete cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0055233, FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
is_a: FBbt:00007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00006015 ! part of wing blade
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046035 ! develops from presumptive wing vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004752
name: second anal vein
def: "Posteriormost vein of the basal wing area (Stark, 1999; Fabian et al., 2016). It begins distal to the median plate and ends around the level of the humeral crossvein (Fabian et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0107299, FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
subset: cur
synonym: "1st vannal vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "posterior branch of anal vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
synonym: "wing vein A2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004753
name: obsolete 1st anal vein
comment: This term has been obsoleted because it corresponds to wing vein L6 (FBbt:00004764) - mc160309.
subset: cur
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00004764

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004754
name: subcostal vein
def: "Smaller longitudinal vein that arises from the humeral crossvein and is found just posterior to the costal vein (Ferris, 1950; Fabian et al., 2016). Its distal end does not reach the wing margin or any other vein (Fabian et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0107299, FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
subset: cur
synonym: "auxiliary vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "axillary vein" EXACT []
synonym: "subcosta" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
synonym: "wing vein L0" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004755
name: costal vein
def: "Vein that follows the full length of the anterior edge of the wing blade (Stark et al., 1999; Blair, 2007). Its longest (distal) segment is contiguous with wing vein L1 (Blair, 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0107299, FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
comment: The distal costa is sometimes also referred to as marginal vein or wing vein L1 (Blair, 2007).
subset: cur
synonym: "costa" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "marginal vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004756
name: distal costal vein
def: "Distal-most of the three segments of the costal vein. It bears two rows of widely spaced, recurved microchaetae and two large macrochaetae at its distal tip." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
comment: The distal costa is sometimes also referred to as marginal vein or wing vein L1 (Blair, 2007).
subset: cur
synonym: "DCo" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: FBbt:00084751 ! wing vein segment
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004755 ! part of costal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004757
name: medial costal vein
def: "Second most proximal (middle) segment of the costal vein. It bears 8 microchaetae, one of which curves away from the cuticle, and a single macrochaeta." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
synonym: "MCo" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: FBbt:00084751 ! wing vein segment
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004755 ! part of costal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004758
name: proximal costal vein
def: "Proximal-most segment of the costal vein. It bears two rows (dorsal an ventral) of bracted microchaetae with a single unbracted microchaeta between the two rows." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
subset: cur
synonym: "PCo" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: FBbt:00084751 ! wing vein segment
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004755 ! part of costal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004759
name: wing vein L1
def: "Anterior longitudinal vein of the wing blade. It is contiguous with the distal costal vein, which follows the anterior wing margin, and posterior to the proximal costal vein." [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
comment: The distal costa is sometimes also referred to as marginal vein or wing vein L1 (Blair, 2007).
subset: cur
synonym: "marginal vein" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
synonym: "radius 1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
synonym: "wing vein R1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046009 ! develops from presumptive wing vein L1

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004760
name: wing vein L2
def: "The second most anterior longitudinal vein of the wing blade." [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
subset: cur
synonym: "fused second and third branches of radius" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
synonym: "radius 2+3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "wing veins R2+3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046030 ! develops from presumptive wing vein L2

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004761
name: wing vein L3
def: "The third most anterior longitudinal vein of the wing blade." [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
subset: cur
synonym: "fused fourth and fifth branches of radius" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
synonym: "medial anterior" RELATED []
synonym: "radius 4+5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "wing veins R4+5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046031 ! develops from presumptive wing vein L3

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004762
name: wing vein L4
def: "The fourth most anterior longitudinal vein of the wing blade." [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
subset: cur
synonym: "media 1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "median vein" EXACT []
synonym: "wing vein M1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046032 ! develops from presumptive wing vein L4

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004763
name: wing vein L5
def: "The fifth most anterior longitudinal vein of the wing blade (Sturtevant and Bier, 1995; Stark et al., 1999; Alba et al., 2021). It encompasses the anterior cubital vein (prior to branching) and the first anterior cubital vein (Sturtevant and Bier, 1995; Fabian et al., 2016; Alba et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0076146, FlyBase:FBrf0107299, FlyBase:FBrf0233988, FlyBase:FBrf0249356]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00046033 ! develops from presumptive wing vein L5

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004764
name: wing vein L6
def: "Posteriormost longitudinal vein (Stark et al., 1999; Blair, 2007; Alba et al., 2021). It branches from wing vein L5 (Sturtevant and Bier, 1995; Alba et al., 2021) and comprises the second anterior cubital vein and the product of its fusion with the first anal vein (McAlpine, 1981; Stark et al., 1999; Blair, 2007). It is relatively short and does not reach the wing margin (Ferris, 1950; Stark et al., 1999; Blair, 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0076146, FlyBase:FBrf0107299, FlyBase:FBrf0202743, FlyBase:FBrf0249356]
subset: cur
synonym: "anal crossvein" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0239368]
synonym: "anal vein" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "wing veins A1+CuA2" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
is_a: FBbt:00047212 ! longitudinal vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004765
name: crossvein
def: "A short wing vein that runs anterior-posterior, joining two longitudinal wing veins (Stark et al., 1999). It lacks underlying tracheae and its formation requires a different set of genes to longitudinal veins (Stark et al., 1999)." [FlyBase:FBrf0107299]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
synonym: "cross-vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00004751 ! wing vein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004766
name: humeral crossvein
def: "Crossvein that connects the proximal anterior wing margin (proximal costal vein) and the subcostal vein (Ferris, 1950; Fabian et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0202743, FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
subset: cur
synonym: "HCV" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
synonym: "humeral cross-vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00004765 ! crossvein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004767
name: anterior crossvein
def: "Crossvein that connects the wing vein L3 and wing vein L4." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
subset: cur
synonym: "ACV" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
synonym: "radial-medial cross-vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00004765 ! crossvein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004768
name: posterior crossvein
def: "Crossvein that connects the wing vein L4 and wing vein L5." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
subset: cur
synonym: "medial cross-vein" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "PCV" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0202743]
is_a: FBbt:00004765 ! crossvein

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004769
name: wing cell
def: "A region of wing cuticle interposed between wing veins." [FBC:GG, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0027-0858]
