relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00004924 ! continuous with uterus
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00110692 ! develops from presumptive oviduct

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004912
name: lateral oviduct
def: "Epithelial tube that connects the ovary to the common oviduct (McQueen et al., 2022). It is lined with a chitinous intima, and surrounded by muscle (McQueen et al., 2022). There are two of these per organism (one per ovary) (McQueen et al., 2022). They usually have a loop near the base of the ovary in unmated females; the loop relaxes after mating to allow egg transit (Kapelnikov et al., 2008; McQueen et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0207006, FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00007474 ! epithelial tube
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004911 ! part of oviduct
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0060003 ! has characteristic female-specific
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00004865 ! continuous with ovary
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00004913 ! continuous with common oviduct

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004913
name: common oviduct
def: "Epithelial tube that connects the lateral oviducts to the uterus (Heifetz et al., 2000; Adams and Wolfner, 2007; Kapelnikov et al., 2008; Heifetz et al., 2014; McQueen et al., 2022). It is lined with a chitinous intima, and surrounded by circular muscles (McQueen et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0125489, FlyBase:FBrf0200717, FlyBase:FBrf0207258, FlyBase:FBrf0224569, FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
