relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00004915 ! continuous with female accessory gland duct
relationship: RO:0002170 FBbt:00004924 ! connected to uterus
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00110687 ! develops from presumptive female accessory gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004915
name: female accessory gland duct
def: "A duct connecting the female accessory gland to the uterus, opening just caudal to the spermathecal ducts (McQueen et al., 2022). It consists of a tube of thin epithelium lined with a thin chitinous intima, irregularly ringed with sharp ridges that project into the lumen (McQueen et al., 2022). It develops from the male genital primordium of the female genital disc (Keisman et al., 2001)." [FlyBase:FBrf0141451, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
subset: cur
