[Term]
id: FBbt:00004921
name: spermatheca
def: "Mushroom-shaped organ consisting of a capsule surrounded by secretory cells, connected to the dorsal side of the uterus by a slender duct, which protrudes into the capsule to form an introvert (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010; Mayhew and Merritt, 2013; McQueen et al., 2022). The capsule is lined by a sclerotized cuticular intima (Mayhew and Merritt, 2013), which is produced by the secretory cells (Miller, 1950; McQueen et al., 2022). Each secretory cell wraps around a specialized cuticle-like structure called an end-apparatus, which is connected to the intima by a duct (Mayhew and Merritt, 2013). Sperm is stored in this organ after mating; it stores fewer sperm that the seminal recepticle, but retains them for a longer period of time (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010; McQueen et al., 2022). There are two spermathecae per female (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010; Mayhew and Merritt, 2013; McQueen et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0210152, FlyBase:FBrf0222595, FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
subset: cur
synonym: "spermathecae" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128516]
synonym: "spermathecum" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222595]
is_a: FBbt:00007474 ! epithelial tube
is_a: FBbt:00048425 ! female reproductive gland
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00110691 ! develops from presumptive spermatheca
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0046693 ! capable of sperm storage

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004922
name: seminal receptacle
def: "Coiled epithelial tube connected to the anterior ventral part of the uterus (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010; McQueen et al., 2022). The tube is approximately 2 millimeters long, with a funnel-shaped entrance, a narrow proximal region and a wide distal region (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010). The proximal region is lined by an epithelium with dense microvilli covered by a thick extracellular matrix (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010). The epithelium of the distal region has its microvilli arranged in a highly ordered brush border covered by a thin extracellular matrix (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010). External to the epithelium is a basal lamina surrounded by a circular muscle layer (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010). After mating, sperm are stored in this organ and remain active and motile (Heifetz and Rivlin, 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210152, FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
subset: cur
synonym: "tubular receptacle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
synonym: "ventral receptacle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0253444]
is_a: FBbt:00007474 ! epithelial tube
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004864 ! part of female reproductive system
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0060003 ! has characteristic female-specific
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00004924 ! continuous with uterus
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00110701 ! develops from presumptive seminal receptacle
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0046693 ! capable of sperm storage

