[Term]
id: FBbt:00005057
name: circulatory system
def: "System that functions to circulate hemolymph throughout the body. It is an open circulatory system, consisting of the dorsal vessel, body cavity, accessory pulsatile organs and the hemolymph (Miller, 1950)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
subset: cur
subset: expressionslim_flybase_ribbon
is_a: FBbt:00004856 ! organ system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005058
name: pericardial cell
def: "Cell which forms the outer layer of the dorsal vessel." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0207370]
