[Term]
id: FBbt:00005062
name: prohemocyte
def: "An immature hemocyte. It is highly basophilic, with a round to polygonal morphology and measures approximately 4 to 6 micrometers in diameter (Shrestha and Gateff, 1982). The nucleus is rich in nucleoli and is surrounded by a thin band of ribosome-rich cytoplasm (Shrestha and Gateff, 1982). In the larva, these cells can be found in the lymph gland primary lobe, or in circulation (Lanot et al., 2001)." [FlyBase:FBrf0074444, FlyBase:FBrf0134542]
subset: cur
synonym: "blast cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134542]
synonym: "hematopoietic precursor cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0228311]
synonym: "HSC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0228311]
synonym: "polygonal cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0036192]
synonym: "Pr" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0066479]
synonym: "prohaemocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0066479]
is_a: FBbt:00007008 ! somatic precursor cell
is_a: FBbt:00025998 ! mesodermal derivative

