[Term]
id: FBbt:00005064
name: melanotic mass
def: "Dark melanin-containing mass that is formed at a wound site in response to injury (Markus et al., 2005; Tang, 2009; Evans et al., 2022). Its formation is mainly mediated by hemocytes (Tang, 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0187734, FlyBase:FBrf0215359, FlyBase:FBrf0252938]
comment: Melanotic masses can be caused by genetic manipulations, however this term only represents the wild-type structure produced in response to injury. Consider FBcv:0000446 for the mutant phenotype, which is sometimes also referred to as a 'melanotic tumor' or 'pseudotumor' (Minakhina and Steward, 2006 - FBrf0194475).
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00100313 ! multicellular structure
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005057 ! part of circulatory system
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1976" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005065
name: adipose system
def: "The system of organs and cells involved in fat storage." [FBC:GG]
subset: cur
subset: expressionslim_flybase_ribbon
subset: FB_gloss
is_a: FBbt:00004856 ! organ system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005066
name: fat body
def: "Collective term for the masses and sheets of adipose tissue that are distributed throughout the organism's body. The adult and larval fat bodies are composed of different cell lineages, but perform the same main function of fat storage (Musselman and Kuhnlein, 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020, FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0238315]
subset: cur
subset: FB_gloss
is_a: FBbt:00007003 ! portion of tissue
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005065 ! part of adipose system
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0019915 ! capable of lipid storage
relationship: RO:0002473 FBbt:00046052 ! composed primarily of fat cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005067
name: fat body primordium
def: "The fat body primordium after the gonadal sheath primordium splits from it during stage 14. By stage 15, the different primordia fuse to form a continuous layer (Hoshizaki et al., 1994). The precursor fat cells it contains continue differentiating until stage 17, when the primordium becomes the fat body proper (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0073371, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "embryonic fat body" NARROW [FBC:DPG]
synonym: "fat body specific anlage" RELATED []
