[Term]
id: FBbt:00005317
name: gastrula embryo
def: "Embryo that is in the process of gastrulation (encompassing embryonic stages 6-8), during which complex morphogenetic movements result in the formation of the three germ layers; ectoderm, mesoderm and endoderm (Hartenstein, 1993)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064803]
synonym: "gastrulation stage embryo" EXACT []
xref: FBdv:00005317
is_a: FBbt:00000052 ! embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005304 ! develops from blastoderm embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005318
name: stage 6 embryo
def: "Stage 6 begins when the ventral furrow becomes apparent, an event which is followed rapidly by the formation of the cephalic furrow. Stage 6 ends when the pole cells have adopted a dorsal (horizontal) position at the posterior. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 10 minutes (170-180 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005317 ! gastrula embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005311 ! develops from stage 5 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005319
name: stage 7 embryo
def: "Stage 7 begins when the pole cells have adopted a dorsal (horizontal) position at the posterior. Invagination of the anterior and posterior midgut and hindgut follows. The 'discoid plate' carrying the pole cells forms a pocket. Transverse furrows (dorsal folds) form on the dorsal surface. This stage ends when the anterior wall of the amnioproctodeal invagination starts moving anteriorly and the pole cells are no longer visible externally. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 10 minutes (180-190 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005317 ! gastrula embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005318 ! develops from stage 6 embryo

