[Term]
id: FBbt:00005321
name: extended germ band embryo
def: "Embryo during stages 9-12." [FlyBase:FBrf0229323, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
xref: FBdv:00005321
is_a: FBbt:00000052 ! embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005317 ! develops from gastrula embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005322
name: stage 8 embryo
def: "Stage 8 starts with the rapid phase of germ band extension and ends with the beginning of mesodermal segmentation. By the end of this stage germ band extension has progressed to the point where the proctodeal opening is at about 60% egg length and the dorsal folds (transverse furrows) are no longer visible. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 30 minutes (190-220 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005317 ! gastrula embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005319 ! develops from stage 7 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005323
name: stage 9 embryo
def: "Stage 9 begins when mesodermal segmentation becomes (transiently) visible, and ends with the appearance of the stomodeal invagination slightly ventral to the anterior pole. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 40 minutes (220-260 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00014201 ! early extended germ band embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005322 ! develops from stage 8 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005324
name: stage 10 embryo
def: "Stage 10 begins with the appearance of the stomodeal invagination, slightly ventral to the anterior pole. Periodic furrows appear in the embryonic epidermis around the middle of the stage. The germ band continues to extend, reaching its maximum extent of 75% egg length towards the end of the stage. The end of the stage is marked by the beginning of invagination of the tracheal placodes. Duration at 25 degrees: approximately 60 minutes (260-320 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00014201 ! early extended germ band embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005323 ! develops from stage 9 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005325
name: stage 11 embryo
def: "Stage 11 begins with the invagination of the tracheal placodes. Para-segmental furrows form and segment boundary furrows become deep folds. Within the head, gnathal protuberances become apparent. The end of this stage is signalled by the appearance of a distinct cleft at the posterior pole of the embryo, which becomes detached from the vitelline membrane. This marks the beginning of germ band retraction. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 120 minutes (320-440 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
synonym: "Segmented germ band stage" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00004450 ! late extended germ band embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005324 ! develops from stage 10 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005326
name: stomodeal invagination
def: "Infolding of the anteroventral embryo that arises during stage 10 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its formation begins when cells surrounding the stomodeal anlage, which consists of a plate of tall cylindrical cells just prior to invagination, divide synchronously (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The invaginated cells divide immediately afterwards, forming a monolayered epithelium (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It is initially oriented perpendicular to the horizontal plane, but progressively bends towards the ventral plane (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It grows caudally by cell divisions and incorporation of neighboring ectodermal cells (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "anterior midgut invagination" RELATED []
synonym: "stomodeum" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00100313 ! multicellular structure
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005321 ! part of extended germ band embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005327
name: stage 12 embryo
def: "Germ band retraction. Stage 12 begins when germ-band retraction starts and ends when this process is complete so that the prospective anal plate occupies the posterior pole. During this stage the posterior and anterior hindgut primordia meet and fuse and the tracheal pits fuse to form the tracheal tree. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 120 minutes (440-560 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00004450 ! late extended germ band embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005325 ! develops from stage 11 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005328
name: stage 13 embryo
def: "Stage 13 begins at the completion of germ-band retraction, when the prospective anal plate occupy the posterior pole. The dorsal ridge becomes apparent externally; the clypeolabrum retracts, leaving a triangular shaped gap at the anterior pole; the labium moves to the ventral midline. This stage ends when head involution begins. Duration at 25 degrees C:Approximately 60 minutes (560-620 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005331 ! dorsal closure embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005327 ! develops from stage 12 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005329
name: cultured cell-line
def: "Somatic cell that originates from a cell-line that is being cultured in vitro, under controlled conditions." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005330
name: stage 14 embryo
def: "Stage 14 begins with the initiation of head involution. Closure of the midgut around the yolk and dorsal closure continue. Dorsal closure is 80% complete by the end of this stage. This stage ends with the appearance of the second midgut constriction. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 60 minutes (620-680 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005331 ! dorsal closure embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005328 ! develops from stage 13 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005331
name: dorsal closure embryo
def: "Embryo during the dorsal closure stage, which corresponds to stages 13-15 (Hartenstein, 1993; Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Dorsal closure occurs by extension of the dorsal epidermal primordium on either side, leading to fusion at the dorsal midline (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "contracted germ band embryo" RELATED []
synonym: "head involution embryo" RELATED []
xref: FBdv:00005331
is_a: FBbt:00000052 ! embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00004450 ! develops from late extended germ band embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005321 ! develops from extended germ band embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005332
name: stage 15 embryo
def: "Stage 15 begins with the appearance of the second midgut constriction. During this stage the 1st and 3rd midgut constrictions form, dorsal closure is completed, and epidermal segmentation is accomplished. This stage ends when the intersegmental grooves can be distinguished at mid-dorsal level. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 100 minutes (680-780 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005331 ! dorsal closure embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005330 ! develops from stage 14 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005333
name: late embryo
def: "Embryo during stages 16 and 17." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
xref: FBdv:00005333
is_a: FBbt:00000052 ! embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005331 ! develops from dorsal closure embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005334
name: stage 16 embryo
def: "Stage 16 begins when the intersegmental grooves can be distinguished at mid-dorsal level, and ends when the dorsal ridge (frontal sac) has overgrown the tip of the clypeolabrum, which is thereby enclosed in the atrium. During this stage the ventral nerve cord retracts to about 60% egg length. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 180 minutes (780-960 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005333 ! late embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005332 ! develops from stage 15 embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005335
name: stage 17 embryo
def: "Stage 17 begins when the dorsal ridge (frontal sac) has overgrown the tip of the clypeolabrum, which is thereby enclosed in the atrium. It lasts until hatching of the embryo (approximately 24 hours after egg laying), during which time much terminal differentiation occurs, the tracheal tree fills with air, so becoming completely visible, and the ventral nerve cord continues to retract. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 8 hours (960-1440 minutes after egg laying)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005333 ! late embryo
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005334 ! develops from stage 16 embryo

