[Term]
id: FBbt:00005343
name: stage P1 prepupa
def: "White puparium (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981). Its posterior spiracles and the ridge between the anterior spiracles tan to an orange color and the animal stops wriggling completely (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981). This stage ends when the puparium becomes brown to the unaided eye (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981)." [FlyBase:FBrf0036849]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
synonym: "L3-2" RELATED []
