relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005341 ! develops from stage 2 third instar larva

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005344
name: stage P2 prepupa
def: "Prepupa from when the puparium becomes brown until a gas bubble becomes visible in the abdomen (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981). In the male, the gonads become less distinct (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981). The oral armature stops moving permanently and the dorsal medial abdominal contractions stop (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981)." [FlyBase:FBrf0036849]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00002952 ! prepupa
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005343 ! develops from stage P1 prepupa

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005345
name: stage P3 prepupa
def: "Prepupa from when a gas bubble becomes visible in the abdomen until it begins to float (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981). The ridge of the operculum becomes distinct during this stage (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981)." [FlyBase:FBrf0036849]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
synonym: "bubble prepupa" RELATED []
synonym: "cryptocephalic pupa" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00002952 ! prepupa
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005344 ! develops from stage P2 prepupa

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005346
name: stage P4 prepupa
def: "Prepupa from when the abdominal gas bubble begins to float until the oral armature of the larva is expelled (Bainbridge and Bownes, 1981)." [FlyBase:FBrf0036849]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00002952 ! prepupa
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005345 ! develops from stage P3 prepupa

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005347
name: stage P4(i) prepupa
def: "Bouyant (approximately 6.5-12 hrs at 25'C). Prepupa floats on water (6.5-7 hours). Other events: lateral trachea become obscured (6.5-8 hours); everted wing and legs discs visible (translucent); bubble appears in posterior of puparium, displacing prepupa anteriorly." [FlyBase:FBrf0036849, FlyBase:FBrf0049147]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005346 ! stage P4 prepupa

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005348
name: stage P4(ii) prepupa
def: "Moving bubble/pupation (12-13.5 hours): Bubble within abdomen disappears; posterior bubble gradually displaced to anterior of puparium, while the (pre?) pupa withdraws to posterior end; imaginal head sac everted and mouthparts of larva expelled." [FlyBase:FBrf0036849, FlyBase:FBrf0049147]
comment: DEPRECATION WARNING.
subset: deprecated
is_a: FBbt:00005346 ! stage P4 prepupa
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005347 ! develops from stage P4(i) prepupa

