[Term]
id: FBbt:00005518
name: somatic muscle primordium
def: "Primordium of the larval segmentally-repeated body wall musculature. It arises from the outer layer of the trunk mesoderm. During germ band shortening (stage 13), it segregates into loose segmental clusters. Within these clusters, muscle formation proceeds by fusion of fusion competent myoblasts to muscle founder cells. Formation of the embryonic/larval somatic musculature is complete by stage 17." [FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "P1 SoMus" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
synonym: "somatic muscle specific anlage" RELATED []
synonym: "SoMusP2" RELATED []
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005647 ! part of presumptive embryonic/larval muscle system
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/492" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005519
name: trunk visceral muscle primordium
def: "Primordium that is derived from the trunk mesoderm and produces larval visceral musculature (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). This produces all of the visceral muscle except for that of the esophagus (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997; de Velasco et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0190261]
subset: cur
synonym: "ViMusP2" RELATED []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005520
name: fat body/gonad primordium
def: "Primordium which develops into the fat body and gonadal sheath. The cells that comprise it are specified from stage 10 (Jemc, 2010), though the first morphological sign of its development comes during stage 11, when the outer of the two layers of the trunk mesoderm thickens medially to become 2-3 cells thick. Segmentally arranged groups of cells split off from inner most layer of this thickening, becoming sandwiched between the somatic muscle primordium and the circular visceral muscle primordium. By stage 13, these segmental clusters have fused into continuous columns on either side of the embryo. These bands split into dorsal and ventral subdivisions. A sub-population of cells in the dorsal subdivision in parasegments 10-12 split off to form the gonadal sheath primordium during stage 14-15. The other cells then form the fat body primordium proper." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0092473, FlyBase:FBrf0216740]
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
synonym: "bipotential lateral mesoderm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0102832]
synonym: "FaB/GP2" RELATED []
synonym: "gonadal mesoderm" NARROW []
synonym: "P2 FaB/GP" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004450 ! part of late extended germ band embryo
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1015" xsd:anyURI

