[Term]
id: FBbt:00005643
name: embryonic Malpighian tubule tip cell
def: "Tip cell of the embryonic Malpighian tubule. It persists throughout tubule elongation during stages 13-16 and contacts a specific target by the end of the process (Weavers and Skaer, 2013). It adopts a specialized morphology with the cell body projecting from the tubule tip on the end of a microtubule-enriched stalk (Weavers and Skaer, 2013). It can extend filopodia and lamellipodia to explore its environment and remains free of basement membrane (Weavers and Skaer, 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0223292]
subset: cur
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005502 ! develops from Malpighian tubule tip cell primordium

