[Term]
id: FBbt:00005739
name: eyelet
def: "Cluster of four extra-retinal Rh6-expressing, green-light sensitive photoreceptor cells located between the eye and the optic lobe (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). It is found beneath the basement membrane, at the posterior margin of the compound eye, near to the equator. There is one of these on each side (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). It is derived from the Rh5-expressing cells of the larval Bolwig organ, which switch their rhodopsin expression during pupal development (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). It participates in entrainment of the molecular clock (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0111143, FlyBase:FBrf0152146, FlyBase:FBrf0248270, FlyBase:FBrf0255165]
subset: cur
synonym: "H-B eyelet" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0248270]
synonym: "Hofbauer-Buchner eyelet" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0248270]
is_a: FBbt:00007233 ! internal sensillum
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003007 ! part of adult head
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00005805 ! develops from Bolwig organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005740
name: eyelet photoreceptor cell
def: "Cholinergic, rhabdomeric photoreceptor cell of the eyelet (Yasuyama and Meinertzhagen, 1999). It expresses Rh6 and is green light-sensitive (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). It develops from an Rh5 photoreceptor of the larval Bolwig organ, which changes its Rhodopsin expression during pupal development (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022). Its functions in the entrainment of the circadian clock (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2002). Its axon terminates in the accessory medulla (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2007). There are four of these cells per eyelet (Jean-Guillaume and Kumar, 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0111143, FlyBase:FBrf0152146, FlyBase:FBrf0193849, FlyBase:FBrf0255165]
comment: Evidence that this is a cholinergic sensory neuron comes from staining for choline acetyltransferase expression. (Yasuyama and Meinertzhagen, 1999).
subset: cur
synonym: "H-B eyelet photoreceptor" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007251 ! rhabdomeric photoreceptor cell
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00005739 ! has soma location eyelet
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100100 ! develops from Rh5 photoreceptor of Bolwig organ
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0043153 ! capable of entrainment of circadian clock by photoperiod
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0019940 ! expresses Rh6
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045003 ! sends synaptic output to region accessory medulla

