[Term]
id: FBbt:00007129
name: embryonic/larval periesophageal neuropils
def: "Larval counterpart to the adult periesophageal neuropils (Pereanu et al., 2010). It is located adjacent to the esophagus and guides the medial cervical tract (Younossi-Hartenstein et al., 2003; Hartenstein et al., 2015). Its anterior portion corresponds to the tritocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900, FlyBase:FBrf0211016, FlyBase:FBrf0229672]
