[Term]
id: FBbt:00007189
name: dorsal organ dome sensillum
def: "Dome shaped cuticular process of the larval dorsal organ, innervated by seven circularly arranged triplets of olfactory receptor neuron (ORN) dendrites. The wall of the dome has numerous pore channels, consistent with a role as an olfactory sense organ." [FlyBase:FBrf0074007, FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0251522]
subset: larval_OF
synonym: "central dome sensillum" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007231 ! external sensillum
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00002655 ! part of dorsal organ
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-09-08T12:36:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007190
name: olfactory receptor neuron of dorsal organ
def: "Odorant receptor expressing bipolar neuron whose dendrite innervates the central dome sensillum of the larval dorsal organ, whose cell body is part of the dorsal organ ganglion and whose axon is carried by the antennal nerve to innervate a larval antennal lobe glomerulus. There are 21 neurons of this type. They receive input from and send output to local neurons in the antennal lobe (Berck et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0147119, FlyBase:FBrf0187327, FlyBase:FBrf0232785]
subset: larval_OF
synonym: "DO ORN" EXACT []
synonym: "DO OSN" EXACT []
synonym: "odorant receptor neuron of dorsal organ" EXACT []
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007127 ! receives synaptic input in region embryonic/larval antennal lobe
relationship: RO:0013006 FBbt:00007153 ! sends synaptic output throughout embryonic/larval antennal lobe glomerulus
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00007226 ! receives synaptic input from neuron larval antennal lobe local neuron
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00007226 ! sends synaptic output to cell larval antennal lobe local neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-09-08T12:42:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007191
name: calyx of larval mushroom body
def: "Calyx of the larval mushroom body. It contains dendrites of the larval Kenyon cells (Masuda-Nakagawa et al., 2009; Saumweber et al., 2018). It is organized into around 34 glomeruli, each innervated by a single projection neuron (Masuda-Nakagawa et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0238440]
subset: larval_OF
synonym: "larval calyx" EXACT []
synonym: "MB-C" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211533]
is_a: FBbt:00003685 ! mushroom body calyx
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00011929 ! part of embryonic/larval mushroom body
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-09-08T12:52:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007192
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus A1
