[Term]
id: FBbt:00007295
name: larval ventral sensory cluster group
def: "Group of sense organs, and the somas and dendrites of sensory neurons, located ventrally in a larval segment (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It lies outside the ventrolateral and ventral muscles, beneath the ventral insertion of the lateral transverse muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It can be divided into two smaller clusters (ventral and ventral'), with the axons of neurons of each cluster following a different branch of the segmental nerve (Willams and Shepherd, 1999). The pattern of sense organs and neurons is highly similar in segments A1-7, and slightly modified in the thoracic segments (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0108300, FlyBase:FBrf0183734]
comment: Terminal (A8-10) segments have substantially different morphology, such that no 'ventral cluster' is present as seen in more anterior segments.
synonym: "embryonic/larval thoracic/abdominal ventral sensory cluster" RELATED []
synonym: "larval thoracic/abdominal ventral sensory cluster" RELATED []
synonym: "ventral group of sensory organs" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00007316 ! sensory cluster
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001727 ! part of larva
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00059198 ! develops from embryonic ventral sensory organ precursor cluster group
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-11-18T01:31:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007296
name: larval dorsal sensory cluster
def: "Cluster of sense organs, and the somas and dendrites of sensory neurons, located dorsally, close to the surface of a larval segment (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It lies above the dorsal insertion of the lateral transverse muscles, outside the dorsal intersegmental muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The pattern of sense organs and neurons is highly similar in segments A1-7, and slightly modified in the thoracic segments (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The axons of neurons in this cluster fasciculate with the intersegmental nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyPNS:PNSorganization0.html]
comment: Terminal (A8-10) segments have substantially different morphology, such that no 'dorsal cluster' is present as seen in more anterior segments.
synonym: "dorsal group of sensory organs" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "embryonic/larval thoracic/abdominal dorsal sensory cluster" EXACT []
synonym: "larval thoracic/abdominal dorsal sensory cluster" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007316 ! sensory cluster
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001727 ! part of larva
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00059182 ! develops from embryonic dorsal sensory organ precursor cluster
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-11-18T01:36:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007297
name: larval lateral sensory cluster
def: "Cluster of sense organs, and the somas and dendrites of sensory neurons, located laterally, close to the surface of a larval segment (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It is located in the niche formed between the lateral transverse muscles and the lateral epidermis (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The pattern of sense organs and neurons is highly similar in segments A1-7, and slightly modified in the thoracic segments (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The axons of most neurons in this cluster fasciculate with the intersegmental nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyPNS:PNSorganization0.html]
comment: Terminal (A8-10) segments have substantially different morphology, such that no 'lateral cluster' is present as seen in more anterior segments.
synonym: "embryonic/larval thoracic/abdominal lateral sensory cluster" EXACT []
synonym: "larval thoracic/abdominal lateral sensory cluster" EXACT []
synonym: "lateral group of sensory organs" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00007316 ! sensory cluster
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001727 ! part of larva
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00059197 ! develops from embryonic lateral sensory organ precursor cluster
