[Term]
id: FBbt:00007320
name: larval cardial cell
def: "Cell that is part of the wall of the dorsal vessel of the late embryo or larva. It connects to a contralateral partner cardial cell dorsally and ventrally, via adhesive junctional domains, leaving a medial lumen (Medioni et al., 2008; Lehmacher et al., 2012). There are 104 of these cells per dorsal vessel (Lehmacher et al., 2012)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0151925, FlyBase:FBrf0219200]
synonym: "embryonic/larval cardial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "embryonic/larval cardiomyocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0151925, FlyBase:FBrf0219200]
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001673 ! part of embryonic/larval dorsal vessel
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00007321 ! develops from embryonic cardioblast
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-12-03T02:12:58Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1289" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007321
name: embryonic cardioblast
def: "Embryonic precursor of a cardial cell, which forms part of the inner, contractile layer of the dorsal vessel. These cells become morphologically distinct during stage 14, when they stretch, flatten and develop dorsally directed processes (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). During dorsal closure, they are squeezed between the amnioserosa and epidermis, and the cardioblasts of either side meet at the dorsal midline once the amnioserosa separates from the epidermis (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The dorsal vessel is formed when the lateral edges of the cardioblasts curve around ventrally to meet and interdigitate leaving a medial lumen (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). These cells do not finish differentiating into specialized subtypes until after larval hatching (Lehmacher et al., 2012)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0151925, FlyBase:FBrf0219200]
synonym: "embryonic cardiomyoblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0219200]
is_a: FBbt:00001666 ! dorsal vessel wall cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-12-03T02:19:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007322
name: embryonic heart cardioblast
def: "Cardioblast which is a precursor of embryonic/larval heart cardial cell in the posterior dorsal vessel. During stage 14, these cells increase in size and elongate in the transverse axis to adopt a columnar shape." [FlyBase:FBrf0151925]
is_a: FBbt:00007321 ! embryonic cardioblast
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-12-03T03:07:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007323
name: embryonic aortic cardioblast
def: "Cardioblast which is the precursor of cardial cells of the aorta in the anterior dorsal vessel. These cells become distinct from heart cardioblasts during stage 14: they remain small and cuboidal while the heart cardioblasts enlarge and elongate to become columnar." [FlyBase:FBrf0151925]
synonym: "embryonic anterior cardioblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00007321 ! embryonic cardioblast
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2008-12-03T03:11:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007324
name: embryonic heart ostial cardioblast
def: "Embryonic cardioblast that will become a larval ostial cell (Molina and Cripps, 2001).They can be recognized by their expression of seven up, and in the assembled dorsal vessel of the late embryo, there are two in each of hemisegments A5-A7 (Molina and Cripps, 2001; Zaffran et al., 2006; Chen et al., 2016). They begin to differentiate into ostial cells at the end of embryogenesis (Lehmacher et al., 2012)." [FlyBase:FBrf0139748, FlyBase:FBrf0151925, FlyBase:FBrf0219200, FlyBase:FBrf0232177]
is_a: FBbt:00007322 ! embryonic heart cardioblast
is_a: FBbt:00053291 ! embryonic ostial cardioblast
