relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00003987 ! continuous with broad root
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00007127 ! develops from embryonic/larval antennal lobe
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2009-12-14T10:59:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007402
name: GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe
def: "A GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe. The majority of the local interneurons of the adult antennal lobe fall into this class." [FlyBase:FBrf0191055, FlyBase:FBrf0201103, FlyBase:FBrf0210390, FlyBase:FBrf0219809]
comment: Based on GABA expression, approximately 80% of the local interneurons of the adult antennal lobe are GABAergic (Wilson and Laurent, 2005). Tanaka et al (2012) distinguishes two different types: LN1 and LN2L. LN1 neurons arborize in most of the glomeruli, whereas LN2L neurons are much more diverse.
