[Term]
id: FBbt:00007494
name: obsolete fan-shaped body segment pair W
def: "Most lateral segment pair of the fan-shaped body." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0221742, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
comment: Obsoleted as the number of columns is variable for different cell types (Hulse et al., 2021 - FBrf0254510) and the most common number is nine, rather than eight or 16 (Wolff et al., 2015 - FBrf0227801; Boyan et al., 2017 - FBrf0236238; Hulse et al., 2021 - FBrf0254510). Hanesch et al. (1989) define 8 segments (A-H), 4 per hemisphere, that correspond to the segment pairs (groups) of slices defined by Ito et al. (2014) and used here. Segment group W corresponds to A and H in Hanesch's nomenclature, to slices 7 and 8 in Ito et al. (2014) and to column 4 in Lin et al. (2013).
synonym: "column 4 of fan-shaped body" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "fan shaped body segment pair W" EXACT []
synonym: "segment A of fan-shaped body" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
synonym: "segment H of fan-shaped body" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
