[Term]
id: FBbt:00007534
name: adult lateral fan-shaped body tangential-protocerebrum neuron ExFl1
def: "Lateral fan-shaped body tangential neuron that projects posteriorly, arborizing in the middle inferior medial protocerebrum and lateral accessory lobe (ventral body), before projecting across the midline to circle around the contralateral side of the ellipsoid body, and innervating the fan-shaped body (Young and Armstrong, 2010). Innervation of the lateral accessory lobes is postsynaptic, whilst that of the fan-shaped body, in layer 2, is presynaptic (Young and Armstrong, 2010; Hulse et al., 2021). The cell bodies of neurons in this class are found in the anterior brain, dorsal to the antennal lobes (Young and Armstrong, 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210154, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
comment: Hulse et al. (2021) - FBrf0254510 say this likely corresponds to what they call FB2B_a and/or FB2B_b. Different FB2B cells may originate from different lineages (Kandimalla et al., 2023 - FBrf0257023).
synonym: "ExFl1" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10519]
synonym: "F1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210154]
synonym: "lateral fan-shaped neuron ExFl1" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003659 ! adult lateral fan-shaped body tangential neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00040037 ! has synaptic IO in region inferior neuropils
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003681 ! receives synaptic input in region adult lateral accessory lobe
relationship: RO:0013006 FBbt:00007488 ! sends synaptic output throughout fan-shaped body layer 2
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-10-19T06:03:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007535
name: adult lateral fan-shaped body tangential-protocerebrum neuron ExFl2
def: "GABAergic extrinsic lateral fan-shaped body tangential neuron that projects dorso-anteriorly to the posterior superior medial protocerebrum where it forms postsynaptic arborizations prior to forming presynaptic arborizations in the dorsal fan-shaped body (Young and Armstrong, 2010; Liu et al., 2016; Ni et al., 2019). The cell bodies of these neurons lie in a cluster lateral to the mushroom body calyx (Young and Armstrong, 2010). Arborization in the fan-shaped body spans a whole layer, but within that layer boundaries split the arborization into 16 segments (Young and Armstrong, 2010). These neurons express AstA-R1 and are activated downstream of glutamatergic AstA-expressing neurons, which synapse onto ExFl2 neurons in the superior medial protocerebrum, to increase daytime sleep; they also receive inhibitory input from dopaminergic neurons (Ni et al., 2019) and R2 ring neurons (Liu et al., 2016). They output onto and inhibit octopaminergic neurons in the fan-shaped body (Ni et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0210154, FlyBase:FBrf0232501, FlyBase:FBrf0241449]
comment: 'dFB neuron' synonym added based on reference to FBrf0232501 in FBrf0241449 and paper seems to refer to a specific set rather than all neurons of dFB - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705. Synapsing shown by GRASP and functional data (Ni et al., 2019). Dopaminergic input may be from PPL1-dFB, but not clear from Ni et al. (2019); identity of octopaminergic neurons also not clear. Fl6 mapped to ExFl2 as FlyBrain NDB (Fl6) and Young and Armstrong (2010) (ExFl2) both cite Hanesch et al. (1989) fig 22g.
synonym: "dFB neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0241449]
synonym: "F5 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210154]
synonym: "Fl6" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210154, FlyBrain_NDB:10272]
synonym: "lateral fan-shaped neuron ExFl2" EXACT []
synonym: "lateral fan-shaped neuron Fl6" EXACT []
