[Term]
id: FBbt:00007681
name: type II motor neuron
def: "Neuron that is synapsed to a muscle via type II terminals. These terminals are characterized by the presence of dense core vesicles that store and release octopamine and the absence of T-bars and clear vesicles (Stocker et al., 2018). Type II motor neurons can be found in the adult and in the larva (Stocker et al., 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0238580]
