def: "Pericardial cell of the adult abdomen. These are serially arranges in a row of 20-25 on each side of the heart from the first to the 6th segment." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00003184 ! adult pericardial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003023 ! part of adult abdomen

[Term]
id: FBbt:00013243
name: abdominal dorsolateral adult muscle precursor cell
def: "An adult muscle precursor cell that is located in a dorsolateral cluster of adult muscle precursors in an anterior abdominal segment. This cluster begins life as a pair of cells associated with the intersegmental nerve and connected to other abdominal adult muscle precursor cells in the same segment by filopodia (Figeac et al., 2010). The cluster remains associated with this nerve through most of development, but migrates to the epidermal histoblast nests where muscle formation is initiated during metamorphosis (Bate, 1993)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0210887]
comment: Corresponds to the two lateral-most of the 3 dorsal adult muscle precursor cells described by Bate et al., 1991.
subset: cur
synonym: "abdominal dorso-lateral adult muscle precursor cell" EXACT []
synonym: "DLAMP" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210887]
synonym: "DLaP" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0100229]
synonym: "dorsolateral adult muscle precursor" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210887]
synonym: "dorsolateral adult muscle precursor cluster abdominal" EXACT []
synonym: "dorsolateral adult precursor" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0100229]
is_a: FBbt:00003232 ! embryonic precursor cell of adult muscle
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00052393 ! part of anterior abdominal segment

