id: FBbt:00040072
name: posterior slope
def: "Synaptic neuropil domain of the adult brain that is the inferior (ventral) part of the posterior cerebral ganglion, covering the area between the inferior bridge and the gnathal ganglion with its superior part lying behind the ventral complex. It contains extensive arborizations of ascending and descending neurons. Its superior boundary is the level above which such arborizations do not occur. It also contains the terminals of axons from the ocellar ganglia, projecting via the ocellar nerves." [FlyBase:FBrf0212704, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, VFB_vol:00040072]
comment: The ventral complex corresponds to the caudal medial protocerebrum (CMP) and possibly includes part of the ventromedial protocerebrum (VMP) of Chiang et al. (2011) (Ito et al., 2014).
subset: BrainName
synonym: "CMP" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0212704]
is_a: FBbt:00040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00040002 ! part of ventromedial neuropils
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-02-24T03:41:00Z" xsd:dateTime

