[Term]
id: FBbt:00047035
name: adult ellipsoid body extrinsic ring neuron ExR3
def: "Adult serotonergic extrinsic ring neuron that follows the longitudinal superior medial fascicle and innervates the superior medial and intermediate protocerebrum, the crepine, the lateral accessory lobe and a dorsal layer of the fan-shaped body, with mixed terminals (Omoto et al., 2018; Hulse et al., 2021). It has mainly presynaptic terminals in both (bilateral) bulbs and the inner central domain of the ellipsoid body (Omoto et al., 2018; Hulse et al., 2021). There is one of these cells per hemisphere and it develops from neuroblast DM6 (Kandimalla et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0240929, FlyBase:FBrf0254510, FlyBase:FBrf0257023]
comment: Previously assigned to DM3 in Omoto et al. (2018), but same authors assign to DM6 in Kandimalla et al. (2023).
