[Term]
id: FBbt:00047043
name: adult ellipsoid body ring neuron R6
def: "R-neuron whose distal neurites enter the ellipsoid body centripetally and form a sparse mesh along the posterior and postero-lateral boundary of the outer posterior domain, with short branches also extending anteriorly into this domain (Omoto et al., 2018). Proximal neurites have a unique projection pattern, first forming dense branches within the gall, and then continuing into the bulb, where they show a web-like innervation reaching throughout the anterior, inferior and superior bulb (Omoto et al., 2018). There are two of these cells per hemisphere (Omoto et al., 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0240929]
