[Term]
id: FBbt:00047221
name: adult fruitless mSG neuron
def: "Neuron of the adult brain that expresses fruitless, whose cell body is located in the ventral medial gnathal ganglion (Tran et al., 2014). It projects to the tritocerebrum and descends to the ventral nerve cord (Tran et al., 2014). There are two of these cells per brain (Tran et al., 2014)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224741]
