[Term]
id: FBbt:00047351
name: adult doublesex pC2 (male) neuron
def: "Doublesex-expressing neuron of the male that is part of a cluster in the posterior region of the protocerebrum. There are more of these cells in the male than pC2 (female) cells in the female. Many of these are activated by the presence of females, but not males (Takayanagi-Kiya and Kiya, 2019). Approximately 26 of these cells per hemisphere arise from the CP3 (DL2) neuroblast (Ren et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0159058, FlyBase:FBrf0210397, FlyBase:FBrf0210735, FlyBase:FBrf0233706, FlyBase:FBrf0234085, FlyBase:FBrf0241873]
