[Term]
id: FBbt:00047365
name: adult abdominal doublesex (male) neuron
def: "Doublesex-expressing neuron of the adult male that has its cell body in the abdominal ganglion (Lee et al., 2002). There are nearly 300 of these cells per (male) organism (Pavlou et al., 2016). Some of these neurons innervate the internal genitalia via the abdominal nerve trunk and some ascend to the brain via the cervical connection (Rideout et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0159058, FlyBase:FBrf0210397, FlyBase:FBrf0210735, FlyBase:FBrf0234085]
