[Term]
id: FBbt:00047446
name: adult ingestion neuron 1
def: "Cholinergic interneuron of the subesophageal ganglion that receives input from Gr43a/Gr46a-expressing sweet taste neurons of the pharynx, but not the Gr5a-expressing neurons of the labellum (Yapici et al., 2016). Sugar must therefore be ingested for these neurons to be activated (Yapici et al., 2016). Activation increases feeding in hungry flies (Yapici et al., 2016). There are 12 of these cells per organism, and their processes cross the midline to arborize in both the ipsilateral and contralateral sides of the subesophageal zone (Yapici et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0232084]
comment: Synapsing shown by GRASP (Yapici et al., 2016).
is_a: FBbt:00005125 ! interneuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00049781 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult subesophageal zone
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0060259 ! capable of regulation of feeding behavior
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0050916 ! capable of part of sensory perception of sweet taste
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00110639 ! receives synaptic input in region adult subesophageal zone
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00110639 ! sends synaptic output to region adult subesophageal zone
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00110886 ! receives synaptic input from neuron gustatory receptor neuron of the adult pharynx
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2018-07-13T12:53:37Z" xsd:dateTime

