[Term]
id: FBbt:00047454
name: gustatory receptor neuron B2 of the terminal organ dorsolateral group
def: "Larval gustatory receptor neuron of the terminal organ dorsolateral group. This neuron has a cell body in the dorsal organ ganglion and innervates the dorsomedial papilla of the terminal organ (Rist and Thum, 2017). There is one of these cells per hemisphere and it expresses Gr33a, Gr66a, Gr32a and Gr10a (Kwon et al., 2011). The B2 neuron responds to bitter stimuli, including quinine and denatonium (van Giesen et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0216529, FlyBase:FBrf0230951, FlyBase:FBrf0236934]
