[Term]
id: FBbt:00047603
name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg11
def: "Descending neuron belonging to the DNg group, having a cell body in the cell body rind around the gnathal ganglion (Namiki et al., 2018). It has dendrites in the superior posterior slope and gnathal ganglion, mainly in the ipsilateral hemisphere, and a large axon descending on the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective to the intermediate tectulum, spanning all three thoracic neuromeres (Namiki et al., 2018; Guo et al., 2022). An axon crosses the midline in the brain and is indirectly connected to contralateral DNg11 neurons (Guo et al., 2022). It fasciculates with the intermediate tract of the dorsal cervical fascicle in the ventral nerve cord (Namiki et al., 2018). There are usually three of these cells in each hemisphere (Namiki et al., 2018; Guo et al., 2022). Its activity is associated with bilateral front leg grooming (Guo et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0239335, FlyBase:FBrf0252837]
synonym: "DNxn014" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
is_a: FBbt:00047516 ! descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00047534 ! fasciculates with intermediate tract of dorsal cervical fasciculus
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0007625 ! capable of part of grooming behavior
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00014013 ! receives synaptic input in region adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00045040 ! receives synaptic input in region superior posterior slope
