[Term]
id: FBbt:00047604
name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg12
def: "Descending neuron belonging to the DNg group, having a cell body in the cell body rind around the gnathal ganglion (Namiki et al., 2018). Its dendrites arborize extensively in the gnathal ganglion, where it receives input from mechanosensory bristle neurons of the head, and its axon projects via the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective to the ipsilateral T1 leg neuropil (Namiki et al., 2018; Guo et al., 2022). There is a cluster of up to ten of these cells in each hemisphere (Namiki et al., 2018). Its activity induces ipsilateral ventral head and front leg grooming (Guo et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0239335, FlyBase:FBrf0252837]
comment: Namiki et al. (2018), identify this as being morphologically similar to the antennal grooming descending neuron 1 (FBbt:00111647), described by Hampel et al. (2015) (FBrf0229838), but Guo et al. (2022) consider these to be distinct. Synaptic input from mechanosensory neurons of chaeta determined by GRASP (Guo et al., 2022).
synonym: "DNfl001" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
synonym: "DNfl002" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
synonym: "DNfl003" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
is_a: FBbt:00047516 ! descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0007625 ! capable of part of grooming behavior
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00014013 ! receives synaptic input in region adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00047140 ! sends synaptic output to region adult T1 leg neuropil
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00052184 ! receives synaptic input from neuron mechanosensory neuron of adult head bristle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2018-09-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00047605
name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg13
def: "Descending neuron belonging to the DNg group, having a cell body in the cell body rind around the gnathal ganglion (Namiki et al., 2018). It descends on the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective, but also has contralateral innervation (Namiki et al., 2018). It has neurites in the lateral accessory lobe, inferior posterior slope, superior posterior slope, epaulette, vest, gnathal ganglion, T1 leg neuropil, T2 leg neuropil and T3 leg neuropil (Namiki et al., 2018). It fasciculates with the ventral lateral tract of the ventral cervical fascicle in the ventral nerve cord (Namiki et al., 2018). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Namiki et al., 2018). It is cholinergic (Cheong et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, FlyBase:FBrf0239335]
synonym: "DNxl005" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
