[Term]
id: FBbt:00047619
name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg27
def: "Descending neuron belonging to the DNg group, having a cell body in the cell body rind around the gnathal ganglion (Namiki et al., 2018). It descends on the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective, but also has contralateral innervation (Namiki et al., 2018). It has neurites in the inferior clamp, inferior bridge, cantle, flange, prow, superior posterior slope, gnathal ganglion and wing neuropil (Namiki et al., 2018). It fasciculates with the median dorsal abdominal tract in the ventral nerve cord (Namiki et al., 2018). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Namiki et al., 2018). It is cholinergic and glutamatergic (Cheong et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, FlyBase:FBrf0239335]
