[Term]
id: FBbt:00047620
name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg28
def: "Serotonergic descending neuron belonging to the DNg group, having a large cell body in the SE1 cluster, in the lateral part of the cell body rind around the gnathal ganglion (Alekseyenko et al., 2010; Namiki et al., 2018; Yao and Scott, 2022). It has dendrites in the flange, prow and gnathal ganglion (Namiki et al., 2018; Yao and Scott, 2022) and it responds to bitter taste stimuli from the proboscis and legs (Yao and Scott, 2022). This neuron does not cross the midline and it sends an axonal projection via the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective to the ventral nerve cord (Namiki et al., 2018; Yao and Scott, 2022). It also sends projections into the labial nerve and to the hypocerebral ganglion, via the recurrent nerve (Yao and Scott, 2022). It activates enteric neurons that express serotonin receptors and can stimulate crop contraction (Yao and Scott, 2022). There are two of these cells per hemisphere (Alekseyenko et al., 2010; Namiki et al., 2018; Yao and Scott, 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210961, FlyBase:FBrf0239335, FlyBase:FBrf0252961]
synonym: "adult serotonergic bitter-SEL descending neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0252961]
synonym: "bitter-SEL" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0252961]
is_a: FBbt:00110949 ! adult serotonergic SE1 neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00004028 ! fasciculates with adult labial nerve
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00100332 ! fasciculates with adult recurrent nerve
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00005804 ! overlaps hypocerebral ganglion
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0022600 ! capable of part of digestive system process
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0050913 ! capable of part of sensory perception of bitter taste
