[Term]
id: FBbt:00047639
name: descending neuron of the posterior brain DNp06
def: "Descending neuron belonging to the DNp group, having a cell body posterior to the posterior to the posterior lateral protocerebrum (Matsuo et al., 2016; Namiki et al., 2018). The primary neurite extends anteriomedially, turns ventrally at the medial side of the PLP and branches, to form postsynaptic terminals in the ipsilateral antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) zones A and B, wedge, anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (AVLP), the LC4 glomerulus of the posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (PVLP), inferior clamp and gorget (Matsuo et al., 2016). A branch extends posterioventrally to form presynaptic terminals in the saddle and posterior gnathal ganglion (Matsuo et al., 2016). It does not cross the midline and descends on the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective, then fasciculates with the dorsal lateral tract of the ventral cervical fascicle (Namiki et al., 2018). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Namiki et al., 2018). It is cholinergic (Cheong et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, FlyBase:FBrf0230862, FlyBase:FBrf0239335]
comment: Namiki et al. (2018), identify this as being morphologically similar to the inferior giant descending neuron, described by Milde and Strausfeld (1990) (FBrf0239829), the antennal mechanosensory and motor center Di5 neuron (FBbt:00111490), described by Matsuo et al. (2016) (FBrf0230862) and VGlut-F-900015, described by FlyCircuit (FBrf0212704).
synonym: "AMMC-Di5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
