[Term]
id: FBbt:00047657
name: descending neuron of the posterior brain DNp24
def: "Descending neuron belonging to the DNp group, having a cell body on the posterior surface of the brain (Namiki et al., 2018). This neuron does not cross the midline and descends on the ipsilateral side of the cervical connective. It has neurites in the flange, superior lateral protocerebrum, gnathal ganglion and intermediate tectulum (Namiki et al., 2018). It fasciculates with the median dorsal abdominal tract in the ventral nerve cord (Namiki et al., 2018). It is GABAergic (Cheong et al., 2024). There is a cluster of up to two of these cells in each hemisphere (Namiki et al., 2018)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, FlyBase:FBrf0239335]
comment: Namiki et al. (2018), identify this as being morphologically similar to E0585-F-200004, described by FlyCircuit (FBrf0212704).
synonym: "DNxn038" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
