[Term]
id: FBbt:00047703
name: embryonic/larval peritracheal PM cell
def: "Neuropeptide-secreting peritracheal cell. There is one of these cells among each cluster of embryonic/larval peritracheal cells and 14 in total per organism (Park et al., 2008; Laneve et al., 2013). It has a more complex morphology than the PMa cells, extending several cytoplasmic processes (Laneve et al., 2013). It is located on the main dorsal trunk trachea, adjacent to the branch point from which the transverse connective trachea splits off (O'Brien and Taghert, 1998; Laneve et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0100681, FlyBase:FBrf0158877, FlyBase:FBrf0210278, FlyBase:FBrf0220777]
comment: This cell stains with molluscan myomodulin antibody just before ecdysis and staining disappears at the time of ecdysis, indicating release of myomodulin-related peptides. In other insects, these cells release ecdysis triggering hormone (ETH), but this was not seen in Drosophila (O'Brien and Taghert, 1998). It expresses dimm and Phm, as is typical for peptidergic cells (Hewes et al., 2003). Additionally expresses gcm (Laneve et al., 2013).
synonym: "embryonic/larval peritracheal myomodulin cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0100681]
synonym: "inka cell" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0100681, FlyBase:FBrf0210278]
synonym: "inka endocrine cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210278]
is_a: FBbt:00006017 ! embryonic/larval peritracheal cell
is_a: FBbt:00007294 ! endocrine cell
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00000212 ! continuous with embryonic/larval tracheal dorsal trunk
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0030072 ! capable of peptide hormone secretion
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0023091 ! expresses dimm
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2018-09-11T15:10:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00047704
name: embryonic/larval peritracheal PMa cell
def: "Non-peptidergic peritracheal cell of the larva. These have fewer processes than the PM cells and are located on the transverse connective of the trachea, adjacent to the branch point from which it leaves the main dorsal trunk trachea (O'Brien and Taghert, 1998; Laneve et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0100681, FlyBase:FBrf0220777]
is_a: FBbt:00006017 ! embryonic/larval peritracheal cell
relationship: RO:0002150 FBbt:00000254 ! continuous with embryonic/larval tracheal transverse connective
