property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2018-10-23T09:00:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00047866
name: distal radius
def: "Region of the radial vein that is furthest from the body of the fly (Cole and Palka, 1982). Its proximal boundary is marked by radius septum 2 and it ends where wing vein L1 (R1) branches from the radial vein (Bryant, 1975; Cole and Palka, 1982)." [FlyBase:FBrf0027793, FlyBase:FBrf0038304]
