[Term]
id: FBbt:00047964
name: larval mushroom body output neuron c2
def: "Dopaminergic larval neuron that has presynapses in the subesophageal zone and the thoracic neuromeres of the ventral nerve cord (Saumweber et al., 2018). It has postsynapses in the lower pedunculus (spur) of the mushroom body and in the basoposterior lateral compartment (ventrolateral protocerebrum) and basoposterior medial compartment (ventromedial cerebrum) (Saumweber et al., 2018). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Saumweber et al., 2018). It develops from the DPMl1 neuroblast (Saumweber et al., 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0238440]
comment: Saumweber et al. (2018) states that DM1 (from Selcho et al., 2009 - FBrf0208252) is a synonym for MBON-c2. Saumweber et al. (2018) found this neuron in the L3 larva, but were not able to identify it in the L1.
