[Term]
id: FBbt:00047965
name: larval mushroom body output neuron a1
def: "Larval odd neuron with its soma just posterior to the mushroom body (Mohamed et al., 2023). It receives input in the ipsilateral calyx, predominantly from Kenyon cells (Saumweber et al., 2018; Mohamed et al., 2023), and has presynaptic terminals in the regions surrounding the ipsilateral and contralateral medial lobes (Mohamed et al., 2023). It is synapsed to MBIN-e1 and FAN-8 (Eschbach et al., 2020). It is involved in odor-based learning (Mohamed et al., 2023) and its activity inhibits turning behavior (Eschbach et al., 2021). It develops from neuroblast CP3 (DL2) and becomes adult MBON29 during metamorphosis (Saumweber et al., 2018; Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0236359, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0245294, FlyBase:FBrf0251872, FlyBase:FBrf0255928, FlyBase:FBrf0256709]
comment: MBE7a synonym from catmaid.
