[Term]
id: FBbt:00047967
name: larval mushroom body output neuron c1
def: "Larval neuron that has postsynaptic terminals in the lower mushroom body pedunculus (spur) and presynaptic terminals in the basoposterior medial compartment (ventromedial cerebrum), centroposterior medial compartment (posterior inferior protocerebrum) and centroposterior lateral compartment (clamp). It is cholinergic (Eichler et al., 2017). It outputs onto FAN-9 (Eschbach et al., 2020). It develops from a BLD neuroblast (Saumweber et al., 2018) and develops into a calyx-innervating mushroom body extrinsic neuron (Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0236359, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0245294, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
comment: Lineage given as 'BLDc' in Saumweber et al. (2018) - seems to be a catmaid annotation for BLD2-4 in Andrade et al. (2019) - FBrf0241389. Adult neuron not precisely identified as not followed to maturity in Truman et al. (2023). MBE18 and CN-59 synonyms from catmaid.
