[Term]
id: FBbt:00047977
name: larval mushroom body output neuron g2
def: "Larval neuron that has presynapses in the ipsilateral centroposterior medial compartment (posterior inferior protocerebrum) and postsynapses in the ipsilateral mushroom body lower vertical lobe (V1) (Saumweber et al., 2018). It is GABAergic (Eichler et al., 2017). It develops from neuroblast DALv2 (Saumweber et al., 2018; Kandimalla et al., 2023) and becomes a LAL.s-NO2i.b (LNO1) neuron during metamorphosis (Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0236359, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
comment: MBE15b synonym from catmaid. Neuroblast either DALv2 or DALv3 (Saumweber et al., 2018). Lineage of LNO1 assigned as DALv2 (primary) in Kandimalla et al. (2023).
