[Term]
id: FBbt:00047983
name: larval mushroom body output neuron j1
def: "Larval neuron that has presynapses in the centroposterior lateral compartment (clamp), dorsoposterior compartment (posterior superior medial protocerebrum) and dorsoanterior compartment (anterior superior medial protocerebrum). It has postsynapses in the medialmost part of the medial lobe (intermediate toe) of the mushroom body in both hemispheres (Saumweber et al., 2018). It is glutamatergic (Eichler et al., 2017). It outputs onto FBN-1 (Eschbach et al., 2020). It develops from neuroblast DAMd1 (Saumweber et al., 2018) and becomes an MBON02 during metamorphosis (Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0236359, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0245294, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
