[Term]
id: FBbt:00048129
name: vertical system twin neuron 1
def: "Lobula plate tangential neuron that resembles vertical system neuron 2, having little lobula plate arborization outside of layer 4, but with a smaller diameter and sparser dendrites (Boergens et al., 2018). It additionally has a main branch in the ventral part of the dendrite (Boergens et al., 2018). It receives input in around 100 columns of lobula plate layer 4, remains ipsilateral, and sends output mainly to the inferior posterior slope (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). It is predicted to be cholinergic (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are two of these cells on each side (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025)." [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634, FlyBase:FBrf0240805, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: VSlike1 from Boergens et al. (2018) judged to correspond to VST1 from Zhao et al. (2023) based on LOP layer 4 restricted innervation.
synonym: "vertical system-like neuron 1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0240805]
synonym: "VS twin 1" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634]
synonym: "VSlike1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0240805]
is_a: FBbt:00048128 ! vertical system-like neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045046 ! sends synaptic output to region inferior posterior slope
