comment: Robinett et al. (2010) state that pMN2 cells are not sexually dimorphic. Kimura et al. (2015) show that these neurons are sex-specific, with males having what they refer to as pMN3 neurons and females having what they refer to as pMN2 in a similar location. These are different cells, as genetic manipulations can result in both cell types being present in one fly (Kimura et al., 2015).
