[Term]
id: FBbt:00048490
name: male-specific anatomical entity
def: "Anatomical entity of the male that is not found in the same form in the female. If there is a counterpart in the female, the male and female types are substantially different." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705]
comment: For example, the testis is male-specific since it is substantially different to the ovary, which may be considered to be the female-specific counterpart. A male wing is not substantially different to a female wing, so is not considered male-specific.
intersection_of: FBbt:10000000 ! anatomical entity
intersection_of: RO:0000053 PATO:0060002 ! has characteristic male-specific
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00007004 ! part of male organism
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2019-11-11T10:56:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
