[Term]
id: FBbt:00048550
name: corpus luteum
def: "Structure formed from the follicle cell layer of the egg chamber after the egg has been released from the ovary (Deady et al., 2015). The posterior follicle cells begin to be lost prior to ovulation so that only the anterior and posterior follicle cells are behind left as a mass in the ovary to become the corpus luteum (Deady et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0227625, FlyBase:FBrf0245616]
is_a: FBbt:00100313 ! multicellular structure
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00004865 ! part of ovary
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0060003 ! has characteristic female-specific
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00004894 ! develops from egg chamber
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-16T15:25:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048551
name: corpus luteum cell
def: "Cell of the corpus luteum. These develop from follicle cells that are shed when the egg leaves the ovary, gaining a yellow pigmentation and upregulating ecdysone biosynthetic enzymes (Deady et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0227625, FlyBase:FBrf0245616]
synonym: "CL cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227625]
intersection_of: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell
intersection_of: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00048550 ! part of corpus luteum
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0060003 ! has characteristic female-specific
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00004904 ! develops from follicle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-16T15:31:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048552
name: terminal follicle cell
def: "Follicle cell found relatively close to the polar cells at the anterior or posterior of the egg chamber. The anterior terminal follicle cells develop into border, stretched (nurse) and centripetal cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0205319]
is_a: FBbt:00004904 ! follicle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-17T10:58:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048553
name: anterior terminal follicle cell
def: "Follicle cell found relatively close to the anterior polar cells of the egg chamber. Different subsets of these cells will develop into border, stretched (nurse) and centripetal follicle cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0205319, FlyBase:FBrf0245616]
synonym: "anterior main body follicle cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247148]
is_a: FBbt:00048552 ! terminal follicle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-17T10:58:26Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1429" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048554
name: posterior terminal follicle cell
def: "Follicle cell found relatively close to the posterior polar cells of the egg chamber. They signal back to polarize the oocyte cytoskeleton. Along with the main body (oocyte associated) follicle cells they form a columnar epithelium from stage 10, which deposits eggshell components." [FlyBase:FBrf0205319]
synonym: "posterior main body follicle cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247148]
is_a: FBbt:00048552 ! terminal follicle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-17T11:10:51Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1429" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048555
name: anterior polar follicle cell
def: "Polar follicle cell found on the anterior side of the egg chamber. They are carried posteriorly, between the nurse cells, by the border follicle cells during border follicle cell migration." [FlyBase:FBrf0205319, FlyBase:FBrf0245616]
is_a: FBbt:00004907 ! polar follicle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-17T11:34:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048556
name: posterior polar follicle cell
def: "Polar follicle cell found on the posterior side of the egg chamber." [FlyBase:FBrf0205319, FlyBase:FBrf0245616]
is_a: FBbt:00004907 ! polar follicle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-17T11:36:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048557
name: larval mooncrawler descending neuron
def: "Cholinergic descending neuron of the larva that can induce backwards locomotion in response to touch or blue light stimuli (Carreira-Rosario et al., 2018; Omamiuda-Ishikawa et al., 2020). Its cell body is found in the ventral anterior medial brain and its processes descend to abdominal neuromeres 3-5 in the ventral nerve cord (Carreira-Rosario et al., 2018). There are two per hemisphere, which can be distinguished by their ipsilateral arbor, which is either linear (MDNa) or bushy (MDNb) (Carreira-Rosario et al., 2018). It also projects via the posterior commissure to arborize contralaterally (Carreira-Rosario et al., 2018). A large proportion of its pre-synapses are to ThDN, pair1, and A18b neurons (Carreira-Rosario et al., 2018). It persists through metamorphosis and develops into an adult moonwalker descending neuron (Carreira-Rosario et al., 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0239825, FlyBase:FBrf0247105]
synonym: "larval MDN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0239825]
synonym: "larval moonwalker descending neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247105]
