[Term]
id: FBbt:00048674
name: larval A26f neuron
def: "Larval GABAergic premotor neuron of the ventral nerve cord (Zwart et al., 2016; Liu et al., 2023). From a dorsolateral soma, it extends ventromedially to the midline, where a branch extends dorsally on either side (Zwart et al., 2016). It then extends further contralaterally, mirroring the ipsilateral circular shape of the neuron (Zwart et al., 2016). Its medial branches mainly consist of input sites (Liu et al., 2023). On the contralateral side, a branch with presynapses extends anteriorly (Zarin et al., 2019), following the DL tract to span multiple neuromeres (Liu et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0233076, FlyBase:FBrf0244727, FlyBase:FBrf0257210]
comment: Reported to be Corazonin neurons in Zarin et al. (2019), but Liu et al. (2023) show that they are GABAergic and not do not secrete Corazonin.
is_a: FBbt:00005125 ! interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00047097 ! primary neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001919 ! part of larval central nervous system
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111225 ! has soma location cell body rind of larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00015900 ! fasciculates with DL fascicle
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 ! capable of gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00001102 ! has synaptic IO in region larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00007675 ! sends synaptic output to cell embryonic/larval motor neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-20T16:15:34Z" xsd:dateTime

