[Term]
id: FBbt:00048711
name: larval thoracic ladder-1 neuron
def: "Larval interneuron of the mesothoracic neuromere that is part of lineage 0 (Jovanic et al., 2019). Its soma is located medially and its neurites extend anteriorly and posteriorly either side of the midline (Jovanic et al., 2019). It receives input from mechanosensory chordotonal neurons (Jovanic et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
comment: Appears only to exist in T2 based on images in Jovanic et al. (2019).
synonym: "larval T00a neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
is_a: FBbt:00111616 ! lineage MNB primary interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00111673 ! larval medial midline neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001919 ! part of larval central nervous system
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00051210 ! has soma location cell body rind along midline of larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00051988 ! has soma location cell body rind of larval mesothoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00001419 ! develops from neuroblast MNB
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00001102 ! has synaptic IO in region larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00005222 ! receives synaptic input from neuron chordotonal neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-22T10:02:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048712
name: larval Drunken-4 neuron
def: "Larval ventral nerve cord interneuron of lineage 30 (Jovanic et al., 2019). From a lateral soma, it projects dorsomedially, then ventrally; it arborizes anteriorly and posteriorly close to the midline on the ipsilateral side (Jovanic et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
synonym: "larval A30a neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
is_a: FBbt:00005125 ! interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00047097 ! primary neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001919 ! part of larval central nervous system
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111225 ! has soma location cell body rind of larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00001102 ! has synaptic IO in region larval ventral nerve cord
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-22T10:13:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048713
name: larval abdominal 1 Drunken-4 neuron
def: "Larval Drunken-4 neuron with its soma in the abdominal 1 neuromere (Jovanic et al., 2019). It outputs onto mechanosensory chordotonal neurons and the Jupiter neurons (Jovanic et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00005222 ! sends synaptic output to cell chordotonal neuron
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00048714 ! sends synaptic output to cell larval Jupiter neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-22T10:18:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048714
name: larval Jupiter neuron
def: "Larval interneuron with a lateral soma (Jovanic et al., 2019). It extends medially, crossing the midline and projecting anteriorly, reaching the subesophageal ganglion; there are also ipsilateral branches arborizing anteriorly and posteriorly close to the midline (Jovanic et al., 2019). It receives input from mechanosensory chordotonal neurons and Drunken-4 neurons and outputs onto recliner neurons (Jovanic et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
comment: Appears only to only be one of these on each side based on images in Jovanic et al. (2019), but looks like A1 in paper and A2 in catmaid data.
synonym: "larval A08h2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
is_a: FBbt:00007392 ! projection neuron
is_a: FBbt:00047097 ! primary neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001919 ! part of larval central nervous system
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111264 ! has soma location cell body rind of larval abdominal neuromere
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00001102 ! has synaptic IO in region larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00100138 ! has synaptic IO in region larval gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00005222 ! receives synaptic input from neuron chordotonal neuron
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00048713 ! receives synaptic input from neuron larval abdominal 1 Drunken-4 neuron
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00048715 ! sends synaptic output to cell larval recliner neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-01-22T10:23:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048715
name: larval recliner neuron
def: "Larval projection neuron of the mesothoracic neuromere that is part of lineage 8 (Jovanic et al., 2019). Its soma is located laterally and it extends medially, before sending branches anteriorly and posteriorly on either side of the midline (Jovanic et al., 2019). It receives input from Jupiter neurons and its contralateral anterior branch projects to the brain (Jovanic et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
comment: Appears only to exist in T2 based on images in Jovanic et al. (2019).
synonym: "larval T08v neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0241547]
