[Term]
id: FBbt:00048874 ! NB3-3 lineage primary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB3-3 during the embryonic phase of neurogenesis. NB3-3 only divides once before switching to type 0 division (Baumgardt et al., 2014; Wang et al., 2022), so the vast majority of this primary lineage is Notch OFF (Mark et al., 2021; Wang et al., 2022). Neuronal terminals are predominantly ventral (Mark et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0225698, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0249021, FlyBase:FBrf0254149]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

