[Term]
id: FBbt:00048891 ! NB7-1 lineage primary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB7-1 during the embryonic phase of neurogenesis. Axons of Notch ON progeny reach the ipsilateral dorsal neuropil, axons of Notch OFF progeny terminate more ventrally (Mark et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0249021]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048892 ! NB7-2 lineage primary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB7-2 during the embryonic phase of neurogenesis." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048893 ! NB7-3 lineage neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB7-3. These are all primary neurons, since NB7-3 does not produce a secondary lineage (Lacin and Truman, 2016). A maximum of three interneurons and one motor neuron are produced, but this varies by segment (Rickert et al., 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0238045]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048894 ! NB7-4 lineage primary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB7-4 during the embryonic phase of neurogenesis. These all belong to the Notch OFF hemilineage, as Notch ON progeny develop as glial cells (Mark et al., 2021). Their axons project in anterior and posterior directions near the ventral midline (Mark et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0249021]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048895 ! lineage 0 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast MNB during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are mainly Notch ON hemilineage neurons, as most of the Notch OFF hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019; Pop et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251, FlyBase:FBrf0246832]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048896 ! lineage 16 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB1-1 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are glutamatergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048897 ! lineage 1 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB1-2 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. Both hemilineages survive and signal via different neurotransmitters (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048898 ! lineage 2 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB2-1 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch ON hemilineage neurons, as the Notch OFF hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are glutamatergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048899 ! lineage 10 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB2-2 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are cholinergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048900 ! lineage 15 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB2-3 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these are all glutamatergic motor neurons (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048901 ! lineage 18 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB2-4 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are cholinergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048902 ! lineage 17 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB2-5 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch ON hemilineage neurons, as the Notch OFF hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are cholinergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
comment: Some MANC neurons annotated as 17B secondary neurons indicating that some may survive, but no additional confirmatory evidence.
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048903 ! lineage 4 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB3-1 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. The vast majority of these are Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as most of the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019), leaving only a small number of interneurons (Truman et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0209606, FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048904 ! lineage 7 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB3-2 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are cholinergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
comment: Lineage 7 referred to as SA3 in maxillary neuromere in Kuert et al. (2014) - FBrf0224770 (Hartenstein et al., 2018 - FBrf0237252).
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048905 ! lineage 8 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB3-3 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. Both hemilineages survive and signal via different neurotransmitters (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048906 ! lineage 25 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB3-4 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. There are relatively few of these neurons, compared to other lineages, and they may all be leg motor neurons (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048907 ! lineage 9 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB3-5 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. A larger number of the A hemilineage neurons survive, compared to the B hemilineage (Lacin et al., 2019). Neurons of each hemilineage signal via different neurotransmitters (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048908 ! lineage 14 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB4-1 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are mainly Notch ON hemilineage neurons, as most of the Notch OFF hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019), leaving only around one neuron per hemineuromere (Shepherd et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251, FlyBase:FBrf0243156]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048909 ! lineage 13 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB4-2 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. Both hemilineages survive and are GABAergic in the adult (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048910 ! lineage 21 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB4-3 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. A much larger number of the A hemilineage neurons survive, compared to the B hemilineage (Lacin et al., 2019). These neurons are all glutamatergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048911 ! lineage 24 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB4-4 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these are all glutamatergic motor neurons (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
comment: 24B sometimes referred to as 24A in Lacin et al. (2019), but lineage 24 seems to only produce 'B' neurons based on Truman et al. (2010) - FBrf0209606.
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048912 ! lineage 6 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB5-2 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. Both hemilineages survive and are GABAergic in the adult (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048913 ! lineage 5 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB5-3 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. These are all Notch OFF hemilineage neurons, as the Notch ON hemilineage is eliminated by apoptosis (Lacin et al., 2019). In the adult, these neurons are GABAergic (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048914 ! lineage 22 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB5-4 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. A much larger number of the A hemilineage neurons survive, compared to the B hemilineage (Lacin et al., 2019). Neurons of each hemilineage signal via different neurotransmitters (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
comment: Lacin et al. (2019) cite Lacin and Truman (2016) to say that NBs 5-4 and 5-7 make lineages 20 and 22, respectively, but this is the wrong way round according to the latter.
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048915 ! lineage 20 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB5-7 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. A much larger number of the A hemilineage neurons survive, compared to the B hemilineage (Lacin et al., 2019). Neurons of each hemilineage signal via different neurotransmitters (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
comment: Lacin et al. (2019) cite Lacin and Truman (2016) to say that NBs 5-4 and 5-7 make lineages 20 and 22, respectively, but this is the wrong way round according to the latter.
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-02-20T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00048916 ! lineage 12 secondary neuron
def: "Any neuron that develops from neuroblast NB6-1 during the postembryonic phase of neurogenesis. Both hemilineages survive and signal via different neurotransmitters (Lacin et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0242251]
