[Term]
id: FBbt:00049138
name: adult lateral accessory lobe-crepine-posterior and medial nodulus 3 neuron
def: "Nodulus-innervating adult neuron that targets only ipsilateral brain regions and has its cell body ventral to the lateral accessory lobe (LAL) (Wolff and Rubin, 2018). It extends dorsally and has predominantly postsynaptic arbors throughout the LAL, also entering the crepine (Wolff and Rubin, 2018). It then projects medially to nodulus 3, where its presynaptic terminals densely innervate the medial and posterior compartments (Wolff and Rubin, 2018). It develops from the BAmv1 neuroblast (Kandimalla et al., 2023). There are approximately six of these cells per hemisphere (Kandimalla et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0240744, FlyBase:FBrf0257023]
