[Term]
id: FBbt:00049180
name: adult ellipsoid body-dorsal gall surround neuron
def: "Neuron that receives input in a wedge (slice) of the ellipsoid body, spanning its full anterior-posterior depth (Wolff et al., 2015). It has within-type synapsing in a poorly-defined region surrounding the dorsal gall (Wolff et al., 2015; Hulse et al., 2021). It receives input from several types of ring neuron (Hulse et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0227801, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
comment: Rare variants of this cell type may additionally target the protocerebral bridge or separate regions of the ellipsoid body (Wolff et al., 2015).
synonym: "EB-LAL neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
synonym: "EBGAs" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246888]
synonym: "EBw.AMP.s-Dga-s.b cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227801]
