[Term]
id: FBbt:00049193
name: adult CCAP ventral subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult neuron that expresses CCAP (Crustacean cardioactive peptide) (FBgn0039007), whose soma is located close to the midline in the ventral gnathal ganglion (Selcho et al., 2018). There is one of these neurons per hemisphere; its cell body fiber runs dorsally along the midline and it ramifies in the medial subesophageal zone (Selcho et al., 2018). It also descends to the ventral nerve cord (Selcho et al., 2018). It undergoes programmed cell death shortly after eclosion (Selcho et al., 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0238423]
synonym: "adult CCAP-rGNGv neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0238423]
synonym: "adult rGNGv CCAP neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0238423]
