property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-04-14T09:10:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00049239
name: adult longitudinal superior lateral fascicle
def: "Longitudinal (anterior-posterior) fascicle of the adult brain that belongs to the group of fiber bundles that separate the superior protocerebrum from the inferior neuropils (inferior protocerebrum) (Lovick et al., 2013). It is a thick bundle, lateral to the longitudinal superior medial fascicle (Lovick et al., 2013). It contains the axons of DPLl2/3 lineage secondary neurons, which follow the tract established by DPLl2/3 primary neurons in the early larva and contribute to the posterior part of the adult tract (Lovick et al., 2013; Wong et al., 2013; Hartenstein et al., 2015). It also has an anterior component, formed by the DPLd posterior hemilineage secondary neurons (Lovick et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0223298, FlyBase:FBrf0223329, FlyBase:FBrf0229672]
synonym: "adult loSL" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0223329]
synonym: "adult loSL fiber system" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0223329]
