[Term]
id: FBbt:00049388
name: adult lateral horn PV4a5 neuron
def: "Adult lateral horn neuron of the PV4a5 group that fasciculates with the PV4 primary neurite tract (Frechter et al., 2019; Dolan et al., 2019; Schlegel et al., 2021). It is a secondary neuron that develops from the BLP4 (LHp1) neuroblast (Schlegel et al., 2021). There are approximately 5-6 of these neurons per hemisphere and they are glutamatergic (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0242477, FlyBase:FBrf0242628, FlyBase:FBrf0249560]
comment: Schlegel et al. (2021) list two as LHON, three as LHLN. Neurotransmitter predicted based on lineage (Schlegel et al., 2021). Cell type found in both hemibrain and FAFB (Schlegel et al., 2021).
