[Term]
id: FBbt:00049443
name: adult AVLP-PN1 lateral horn input neuron
def: "Adult lateral horn input neuron that has its dendrites predominantly within the anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (Dolan et al., 2019; Baker et al., 2022). Its projections remain ipsilateral (Baker et al., 2022). It is a secondary neuron that is part of the BLP1 (VPNp&v) posterior hemilineage (Bates et al., 2020). There are ten of these neurons per hemisphere and they are cholinergic and GABAergic (Dolan et al., 2019). It responds to both male sine and pulse song (Baker et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0242477, FlyBase:FBrf0246460, FlyBase:FBrf0254226]
comment: Both neurotransmitters detected by antibody staining (Dolan et al., 2019).
