[Term]
id: FBbt:00049516
name: lobula tangential neuron LT33
def: "A wide-field lobula tangential neuron with an arbor specific to and covering the entire Lo1 stratum, and some branches in the neuropil of the posterior lateral protocerebrum (PLP) (Shinomiya et al., 2019). There is one LT33 cell per hemisphere and its cell body is located in the central brain, near the midline (Shinomiya et al., 2019). It is presynaptic to T5 neurons (Shinomiya et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0241236, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
