[Term]
id: FBbt:00049572
name: bilateral campaniform sensillum neuron of leg
def: "Mechanosensory neuron that relays input from a campaniform sensillum in the leg to multiple contralateral and ipsilateral thoracic neuromeres (Phelps et al., 2021). There are two of these neurons per leg and they have the largest diameter of any leg sensory neurons (Phelps et al., 2021). In the ventral nerve cord, they synapse directly onto a subset of leg motor neurons at their primary neurites or short second order branches (Phelps et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0247998]
synonym: "bCS neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247998]
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00004640 ! has soma location leg
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00049553 ! fasciculates with adult leg nerve
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00111027 ! sends synaptic output to region adult thoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0013007 FBbt:00048055 ! has sensory dendrite in campaniform sensillum of leg
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00049568 ! sends synaptic output to cell leg muscle motor neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-06-02T14:44:01Z" xsd:dateTime

