[Term]
id: FBbt:00049720
name: non-aristal sensory neuron VP3
def: "Thermosensory neuron that innervates the ipsilateral antennal lobe glomerulus VP3, but does not receive sensory input in the arista (Liu et al., 2015; Marin et al., 2020; Alpert et al., 2020). There are one or two of these cells per hemisphere, with their cell bodies at the edge of the antennal nerve (Alpert et al., 2020). It has simpler arbors in the antennal lobe than the VP3 neurons of the arista (Marin et al., 2020). It provides most of the input to the slow-cool VP3 vPN (Liu et al., 2015; Marin et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0227881, FlyBase:FBrf0246007, FlyBase:FBrf0246456]
comment: ACc from Alpert et al. (2020) judged to be the same as VP3RNb from Marin et al. (2020) based on lack of aristal dendrite, arborization in VP3 (cold glomerulus) and connections to VP3 vPN (slow-cool PN).
synonym: "ACc" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246007]
synonym: "anterior cold cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246007]
synonym: "VP3RNb" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246456]
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00003980 ! has soma location adult antennal nerve
relationship: RO:0013006 FBbt:00003929 ! sends synaptic output throughout antennal lobe glomerulus VP3
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00111337 ! sends synaptic output to cell adult antennal lobe projection neuron VP3 vPN
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-08-11T10:55:25Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1353" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: FBbt:00049721
name: adult antennal lobe projection neuron VP1d il2PN
def: "Adult uniglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron with its cell body in the lateral subesophageal ganglion, dendrites that mainly innervate antennal lobe glomerulus VP1d and an axon that projects via the dorsal antennal lobe tract (Marin et al., 2020). It arborizes in the mushroom body calyx and the lateral horn (Marin et al., 2020). Before entering the antennal lobe, it crosses the midline in the subesophageal zone and it has a bilaterally-symmetrical innervation pattern (Marin et al., 2020). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Bates et al., 2020; Marin et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246456, FlyBase:FBrf0246460]
synonym: "VP1d il2PN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246456]
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00007053 ! sends synaptic output to region adult lateral horn
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00007385 ! sends synaptic output to region calyx of adult mushroom body
