[Term]
id: FBbt:00049915
name: adult TwoLumps ascending neuron
def: "Adult ascending neuron with its soma in the mesothoracic neuromere, dendritic arborizations in the ipsilateral mesothoracic and prothoracic neuromeres, and axonal projections that ascend to the ipsilateral side of the central brain to the vest, flange, and the lateral accessory lobe (Sen et al., 2019). It is activated downstream of mechanosensory neurons and is involved in backwards locomotion, upstream of the moonwalker descending neurons (Sen et al., 2019). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Sen et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0244359]
synonym: "adult TLA neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244359]
synonym: "AN17A026" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2025.07.31.667571]
synonym: "TLA" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0244359]
is_a: FBbt:00048301 ! adult ascending neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111084 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult mesothoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0007628 ! capable of part of adult walking behavior
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0043057 ! capable of part of backward locomotion
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00110174 ! receives synaptic input in region adult prothoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00110175 ! receives synaptic input in region adult mesothoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00003681 ! sends synaptic output to region adult lateral accessory lobe
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00040041 ! sends synaptic output to region vest
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045050 ! sends synaptic output to region flange
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-11-19T16:08:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00049916
name: transmedullary neuron Tm29
def: "Transmedullary neuron that receives most of its input in around 5 columns of medulla layer M6, where it also has a small number of presynapses (Nern et al., 2025). It also has a small amount of arborization in the rest of M3-M8 (Nern et al., 2025). It crosses the second optic chiasm and has mixed pre- and post-synapses in around 3 columns of lobula layer 5B (Nern et al., 2025). It is glutamatergic (Davis et al., 2020). There are around 170-270 of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0244935, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "Tm5d" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
is_a: FBbt:00003788 ! transmedullary neuron
is_a: FBbt:20007266 ! adult transmedullary CB3851 neuron
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00052328 ! develops from immature transmedullary neuron Tm29
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061535 ! capable of glutamate secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003755 ! receives synaptic input in region medulla layer M6
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00111744 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula layer 5B
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00003755 ! sends synaptic output to region medulla layer M6
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00111744 ! sends synaptic output to region lobula layer 5B
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-11-20T09:32:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00049917
name: adult antennal lobe projection neuron DA2++ ilPN
def: "Adult panglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron with greatest innervation of the DA2 glomerulus (Bates et al., 2020; Marin et al., 2020). It follows the transverse antennal lobe t8ALT tract (Marin et al., 2020; Scheffer et al., 2020). There is one of these per hemisphere, with its cell body in the lateral subesophageal zone (Bates et al., 2020; Marin et al., 2020). It splits into two main branches, one extending into each hemisphere, and it has a roughly symmetrical innervation pattern (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246456, FlyBase:FBrf0246460, FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0249560]
comment: This is the same cell type as M_ilPNm90, which represented an individual that takes the 'wrong' tract in the right hemisphere of the hemibrain (Schlegel et al., 2021).
synonym: "adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron ilPN mALT" RELATED []
synonym: "adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron ilPN tALT" RELATED []
synonym: "adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron ilPN trans-mALT" RELATED []
synonym: "adult panglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron ilPN tALT" RELATED []
synonym: "adult panglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron ilPN trans-mALT" RELATED []
