[Term]
id: FBbt:00049920
name: oviposition descending neuron oviDNa
def: "Oviposition descending neuron with unilateral (contralateral) arborization in the abdominal neuromere, which is relatively anterolateral to that of other oviDN cell types (Wang et al., 2020; Sturner et al., 2025). In the brain, it lacks a dorsal projection beside the midline, instead reaching the superior medial protocerebrum via a lateral loop (Wang et al., 2020; Sturner et al., 2025). It also has an ipsilateral ventral neurite (Wang et al., 2020; Sturner et al., 2025). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Sturner et al., 2025). It expresses fruitless, but not doublesex (Wang et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0245074, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
is_a: FBbt:00049919 ! oviposition descending neuron oviDN
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0004652 ! expresses fru
