def: "Adult lateral horn output neuron of the AD1c2 group that fasciculates with the AD1 primary neurite tract (Schlegel et al., 2021). Its soma is found in the anterodorsal part of the border between the lateral horn and superior lateral protocerebrum. It receives mainly input in the lateral horn and it outputs to the superior intermediate protocerebrum. It is a secondary neuron that is part of the LHl2 (DPLal2) medial hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2021). There are approximately 5-8 of these cells per hemisphere and they are cholinergic (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0249560, http://neuprint.janelia.org/?dataset=hemibrain\:v1.1]
comment: Neurotransmitter predicted based on lineage (Schlegel et al., 2021). Cell type found in both hemibrain and FAFB (Schlegel et al., 2021).
synonym: "adult AD1c2 neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "adult anterior dorsal tract 1 neuron c2" EXACT []
synonym: "adult LHAD1c2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0249560]
is_a: FBbt:00047096 ! secondary neuron
is_a: FBbt:00049286 ! adult lateral horn output neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00049306 ! fasciculates with adult anterior dorsal primary neurite tract 1
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100592 ! develops from neuroblast DPLal2
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007053 ! receives synaptic input in region adult lateral horn
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045032 ! sends synaptic output to region superior intermediate protocerebrum
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2021-02-24T12:38:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00051056
name: adult lateral horn AD1c3 neuron
def: "Adult lateral horn output neuron of the AD1c3 group that fasciculates with the AD1 primary neurite tract (Schlegel et al., 2021). Its soma is found in the anterodorsal part of the border between the lateral horn and superior lateral protocerebrum. Most of its input and output terminals are located in the lateral horn, but a branch also extends medially into the protocerebrum. It is a secondary neuron that is part of the DPLal2 (LHl2) medial hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2021). There are 3-4 of these cells per hemisphere and they are cholinergic (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0249560, http://neuprint.janelia.org/?dataset=hemibrain\:v1.1]
comment: Neurotransmitter predicted based on lineage (Schlegel et al., 2021). Cell type found in both hemibrain and FAFB (Schlegel et al., 2021).
