[Term]
id: FBbt:00051059
name: adult lateral horn PD2a6 neuron
def: "Adult lateral horn output neuron of the PD2a6 group that fasciculates with the PD2 primary neurite tract (Schlegel et al., 2021). Its soma is found in the dorsal part of the border between the lateral horn and superior lateral protocerebrum. It receives most of its input in the lateral horn and a branch extends medially to the superior medial protocerebrum, which is its main output region. There are approximately four of these cells per hemisphere (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0249560, http://neuprint.janelia.org/?dataset=hemibrain\:v1.1]
