[Term]
id: FBbt:00051060
name: adult lateral horn PD2a7 neuron
def: "Adult lateral horn output neuron of the PD2a7 group that fasciculates with the PD2 primary neurite tract (Schlegel et al., 2021). Its soma is found in the dorsal part of the border between the lateral horn and superior lateral protocerebrum. Most of its input and output synapses are in the superior medial protocerebrum. There are around four of these cells per hemisphere (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0249560, http://neuprint.janelia.org/?dataset=hemibrain\:v1.1]
comment: Four of these cells appear in hemibrain 1.1 data on neuprint, one of these does not appear to have terminals in the lateral horn - all classed as LHON in Schlegel et al. (2021).
