[Term]
id: FBbt:00051233
name: adult protocerebral bridge 1-9 neuron
def: "Neuron with extensive innervation of the brain that has a sinuous arbor of variable density that courses through all glomeruli of the protocerebral bridge (PB) (Wolff and Rubin, 2018). It has its cell body in the subesophageal zone (Kandimalla et al., 2023). There is heterogeneity in the brain regions innervated and whether PB innervation is unilateral or bilateral (Wolff and Rubin, 2018). At least one subtype is octopaminergic (Busch et al., 2009; Wolff and Rubin, 2018)." [FlyBase:FBrf0207458, FlyBase:FBrf0240744, FlyBase:FBrf0257023]
comment: Name does not reflect full extent of neuron, but most of this neuron is not present in the hemibrain volume and it is not clear from Wolff and Rubin (2018) which regions are conserved between subtypes. May be renamed when better described in future. May only be one of these per hemisphere and may be identical to OA-AL2i1 (Kandimalla et al., 2023 - FBrf0257023).
synonym: "PB octopaminergic neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0240744]
is_a: FBbt:00005125 ! interneuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00110639 ! has soma location adult subesophageal zone
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003668 ! has synaptic IO in region protocerebral bridge
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2021-04-22T17:44:44Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0006011 FBbt:00110141 {xref="FlyBase:FBrf0257023"}

[Term]
id: FBbt:00051234
name: adult fan-shaped body 1 column-rubus neuron
def: "Small field neuron of the adult central complex that connects a column of the fan-shaped body with the rubus (Scheffer et al., 2020; Hulse et al., 2021). These neurons receive input mainly in ventral layers of a fan-shaped body column and have predominantly presynaptic terminals in the rubus and the surrounding crepine (Hulse et al., 2021). They follow a nine-column organization in the fan-shaped body (Hulse et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
comment: Stated to innervate round body (ROB) in a couple of places in Hulse et al. (2021), but this is probably a mistake.
synonym: "FB-RUB neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
is_a: FBbt:00049822 ! fan-shaped body extrinsic columnar neuron
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00049533 ! receives synaptic input in region adult ventral fan-shaped body
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00040038 ! sends synaptic output to region rubus
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045037 ! sends synaptic output to region adult crepine
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2021-04-27T09:45:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00051235
name: adult fan-shaped body 1 column-rubus neuron 1
def: "Adult fan-shaped body 1 column-rubus (FR) neuron with strong all-all connectivity of neurons of this type within each rubus (Hulse et al., 2021). These neurons have more extensive arborization (layers 2-5) in their fan-shaped body column than their FR2 counterparts (Scheffer et al., 2020; Hulse et al., 2021). There are 18 of these neurons per fan-shaped body, following a nine-column organization (Hulse et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
