[Term]
id: FBbt:00051495
name: adult olfactory receptor neuron Ir75c
def: "Olfactory receptor neuron that expresses the Ionotropic receptor (Ir) 75c and the co-receptor Ir8a (Prieto-Godino et al., 2017; Benton et al., 2025). Its dendrite transduces signals from antennal coeloconic sensillum ac3 type II and its axonal terminals are found in glomerulus DL2v (Prieto-Godino et al., 2017), bilaterally (Schlegel et al., 2021). It has a stronger response to propionic acid and a weaker response to butyric acid, compared to Ir75b neurons (Prieto-Godino et al., 2017). It develops from an Nab precursor (Benton et al., 2025). There are approximately 12 of these cells per antenna (Schlegel et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0234776, FlyBase:FBrf0249560, FlyBase:FBrf0262710]
comment: Prieto-Godino et al. (2017) showed that these cells are distinct from the Ir75b cells and that previous belief of co-expression was due to transcriptional run off from Ir75c.
synonym: "Ir75c ac3II" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234776]
synonym: "ORN (DL2v)" EXACT []
synonym: "ORN ac3" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0206496]
synonym: "ORN ac3A" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0226805]
synonym: "ORN ac3IIA" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262710]
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00003979 ! fasciculates with adult antennal lobe commissure
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2021-09-23T12:22:22Z" xsd:dateTime

