[Term]
id: FBbt:00051853
name: adult asteroid subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult local neuron with its soma in the ventral gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, with mixed synapse distribution within this region (Sterne et al., 2021). It has dense innervation in the lateral ipsilateral subesophageal zone (SEZ) and a projection to the contralateral lateral SEZ, where it has sparser arbors (Sterne et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280]
