[Term]
id: FBbt:00051857
name: adult bluebell subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult GABAergic descending neuron with its soma in the lateral subesophageal zone (Sterne et al., 2021; Sapkal et al., 2024). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, with polarized synapse distribution within this region (Sterne et al., 2021). It is bilateral, but most of its innervation is in the ipsilateral hemisphere (Sterne et al., 2021). Its activation causes halting (Sapkal et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0260559]
