[Term]
id: FBbt:00051861
name: adult bract subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult descending neuron with its soma in the ventral gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). It has axonal arborization in the T1 leg neuropil and both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). In the brain it is ipsilateral, and it descends on the ipsilateral side (Sterne et al., 2021). It responds to sugar stimuli and its activity stimulates proboscis extension (Shiu et al., 2022). It is predicted to be cholinergic (Shiu et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0254006]
comment: Neurotransmitter prediction based on machine learning classification (Shiu et al., 2022). Only MANC 'candidate' match is DNfl021 (Sturner et al., 2025 - FlyBase:FBrf0262850).
synonym: "DNfl021" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
synonym: "DNge173" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
