[Term]
id: FBbt:00051864
name: adult broom subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult interneuron with its soma in the lateral subesophageal zone (Sterne et al., 2021). It has dendritic arborization in the inferior posterior slope, superior posterior slope, lateral accessory lobe, epaulette, saddle and gnathal ganglion and both dendritic and axonal arborization in the vest (Sterne et al., 2021). It is bilateral, but most of its innervation is in the ipsilateral hemisphere (Sterne et al., 2021). It is predicted to be a GABAergic primary neuron (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Eckstein et al., 2024). There is one of these cells on each side (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Shiu et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0260565]
comment: Mapped to FlyWire CB0543 in Shiu et al. (2024) supplement.
