[Term]
id: FBbt:00051879
name: adult fluff subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult local neuron with its soma in the gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, with mixed synapse distribution within this region (Sterne et al., 2021). It is bilateral, with symmetrical innervation in a broad region of the subesophageal zone (Sterne et al., 2021). It is predicted to be a GABAergic primary neuron (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Eckstein et al., 2024). There are 2 of these cells per organism (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
