[Term]
id: FBbt:00051903
name: adult kitty subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult local neuron with its soma in the ventral gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, with mixed synapse distribution within this region (Sterne et al., 2021). Its primary neurite crosses the midline and most of its innervation is in the contralateral hemisphere, with a small, relatively dorsal part of the cell crossing back to the ipsilateral side (Sterne et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280]
comment: Shiu et al. (2024) - FBrf0260565 supplement maps kitty to CB0370, but only one side and the annotation is not in Codex (2024-02-07).
