[Term]
id: FBbt:00051932
name: adult rattle subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult local neuron with its soma in the ventral gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, with biased synapse distribution within this region (Sterne et al., 2021). It is mainly ipsilateral, but arborizes close to the midline (Sterne et al., 2021). It receives a large amount of input from sugar-sensing gustatory neurons and its activation results in proboscis extension (Shiu et al., 2022). It is predicted to be a cholinergic (Shiu et al., 2022) primary neuron (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). There are 2 of these cells per organism (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0254006, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
