def: "Adult interneuron with its soma in the gnathal ganglion (Sterne et al., 2021). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, with polarized synapse distribution within this region (Sterne et al., 2021). It is bilateral, but most of its innervation is in the ipsilateral hemisphere (Sterne et al., 2021). It is a feeding initiation premotor neuron and is predicted to be cholinergic (Shiu et al., 2022). It is a putative primary neuron (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). There are 2 of these cells per organism (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0254006, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
