[Term]
id: FBbt:00051951
name: adult trumpet subesophageal neuron
def: "Adult interneuron with its soma in the subesophageal zone (Sterne et al., 2021). It has both dendritic and axonal arborization in the gnathal ganglion, flange and prow, with mixed synapse distribution within these regions (Sterne et al., 2021). It is bilateral, but most of its innervation is in the ipsilateral hemisphere (Sterne et al., 2021). It is predicted to be a cholinergic primary neuron (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Eckstein et al., 2024). There are 2 of these cells per organism (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
