[Term]
id: FBbt:00051967
name: neck muscle motor neuron of VNC
def: "Motor neuron of the ventral nerve cord that innervates a muscle of the neck (Phelps et al., 2021; Cheong et al., 2024). It has its soma in the prothoracic neuromere and receives input in the neck neuropil (Phelps et al., 2021)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, FlyBase:FBrf0247998, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Cheong et al. (2024) note that some neck muscle motor neurons have somas in the brain.
