[Term]
id: FBbt:00052005
name: larval corazonin neuron of pars lateralis
def: "Larval corazonin-expressing neuron that has its soma in the pars lateralis (Siegmund and Korge, 2001). It projects to the ring gland, via the nervus corporis cardiaci, where it has peptide release sites in the aorta, corpus cardiacum, corpus allatum and the prothoracic gland (Siegmund and Korge, 2001; Imura et al., 2020; Huckesfeld et al., 2021; McKim et al., 2024). In the prothoracic gland, it makes contacts with the PTTH neurons, which express the corazonin receptor (Imura et al., 2020). There are three of these cells per hemisphere (Siegmund and Korge, 2001; Park et al., 2008; Imura et al., 2020). It also expresses short neuropeptide F (Park et al., 2008)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.102684.1, FlyBase:FBrf0134726, FlyBase:FBrf0210278, FlyBase:FBrf0245906, FlyBase:FBrf0249161]
synonym: "CC-LP 2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
synonym: "larval corpus cardiacum innervating neurosecretory neuron of the lateral protocerebrum 2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
synonym: "larval l-NSC CRZ" EXACT [doi:10.7554/eLife.102684.1]
synonym: "PL4-6" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210278]
is_a: FBbt:00047097 ! primary neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111671 ! has soma location larval pars lateralis
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00053391 ! fasciculates with larval nervus corporis cardiaci
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001674 ! overlaps embryonic/larval aorta
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001724 ! overlaps prothoracic gland
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001725 ! overlaps embryonic/larval corpus allatum
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001726 ! overlaps embryonic/larval corpus cardiacum
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0030072 ! capable of peptide hormone secretion
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0013767 ! expresses Crz
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0032840 ! expresses sNPF
