[Term]
id: FBbt:00052009
name: adult Hugin neuron of the corpus allatum
def: "Adult neuron that expresses Hugin and projects to the ring gland, where it has peptide release sites in the corpus allatum (Mizuno et al., 2021). It has synaptic contact with Dh44 neurons in the subesophageal zone (Mizuno et al., 2021). There are two of these cells per hemisphere (Mizuno et al., 2021), with their cell bodies in the subesophageal zone (McKim et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.102684.1, FlyBase:FBrf0249406]
synonym: "adult SEZ-NSC Hugin" EXACT [doi:10.7554/eLife.102684.1]
