[Term]
id: FBbt:00052021
name: type I motor neuron of oviduct/uterus
def: "Adult motor neuron that innervates the extrinsic or intrinsic muscle of the uterus, or the common oviduct muscle, with glutamatergic type I terminals (Middleton et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
comment: Type I boutons identified based on bouton morphology, and Shaker and glutamate receptor expression (Middleton et al., 2006). The set of these neurons are the only type I MNs innervating the female reproductive tract (Middleton et al., 2006).
