[Term]
id: FBbt:00052131
name: adult prothoracic 10Balpha neuron
def: "Adult cholinergic interneuron of hemilineage 10B with its soma in the prothoracic neuromere that receives input from a directionally-tuned femoral chordotonal organ (FeCO) club neuron and responds to tibial vibrations and tibial movements in both directions (Agrawal et al., 2020). These cells innervate multiple neuromeres and a subset ascend to the brain, where they innervate the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Agrawal et al., 2020). Its activation causes pausing behaviour in walking flies (Agrawal et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0247582]
