name: medulla tangential intrinsic neuron of dorsal rim area 2
def: "Medulla tangential intrinsic neuron of the dorsal rim area (DRA) with its soma on the dorsal side of the medulla (Kind et al., 2021). Its main process is in the DRA region, but it also has long processes extending ventrally into non-DRA columns (Kind et al., 2021). It receives input from R7 photoreceptors of the DRA, mainly in layers M6/M7 (Kind et al., 2021). Its predicted neurotransmitter is GABA (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are approximately 20 of these cells on each side (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0252485, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "adult central medulla neuron Cm14" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262354, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "Cm14" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262354, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "medullary tangential intrinsic neuron of dorsal rim area 2" EXACT []
synonym: "Mti-DRA-2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0252485]
synonym: "Sm23" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
is_a: FBbt:00052142 ! medulla tangential intrinsic neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 ! capable of gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003754 ! receives synaptic input in region medulla layer M5
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003755 ! receives synaptic input in region medulla layer M6
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00045002 ! receives synaptic input in region medulla dorsal rim area
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00004449 ! receives synaptic input from neuron dorsal margin photoreceptor cell R7
relationship: RO:0013010 FBbt:00003748 ! synapses restricted to region medulla
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-03-22T10:45:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052147
name: adult medulla-medulla neuron of dorsal rim area
def: "Large neuron with its soma on the dorsal side of the medulla that connects the dorsal rim areas of the ipsilateral and contralateral hemispheres (Kind et al., 2021). Its ipsilateral processes are largely dendritic and its contralateral processes are largely axonal (Kind et al., 2021). It receives input from R7 photoreceptors of the dorsal rim area in layer M6 (Kind et al., 2021). It passes through the central brain without forming synapses there (Kind et al., 2021). There are two of these cells per hemisphere, one innervating the ipsilateral anterior medulla and contralateral posterior medulla and one innervating the ipsilateral posterior medulla and the contralateral anterior medulla (Kind et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0252485]
synonym: "MeMe1" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0252485]
synonym: "MeMe_e10" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2025.07.31.667571]
synonym: "MeVPMe10" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00051040 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult dorsal medulla
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003755 ! receives synaptic input in region medulla layer M6
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00045002 ! receives synaptic input in region medulla dorsal rim area
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00004449 ! receives synaptic input from neuron dorsal margin photoreceptor cell R7
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-03-22T13:48:10Z" xsd:dateTime

