[Term]
id: FBbt:00052275
name: large DN3 neuron
def: "DN3 neuron that has a relatively large cell body (Reinhard et al., 2022). It projects anteriorly to the anterior optic tubercle forming a characteristic loop around the superior lateral protocerebrum (Reinhard et al., 2022). Some of these cells form additional loops (Reinhard et al., 2022). It has a ventral projection that reaches the accessory medulla (Reinhard et al., 2022). There are four or five of these cells per hemisphere, half with relatively anterior somas and half with relatively posterior somas (Reinhard et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0253505]
comment: Some seem to project contralaterally via the SAC, but not seen in any hemibrain large DN3s (Reinhard et al., 2022). All hemibrain cells have SLP loop, but other two loops described in Reinhard et al. (2022) are not consistent.
is_a: FBbt:00003631 ! DN3 neuron
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00007054 ! has synaptic IO in region superior lateral protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00007059 ! has synaptic IO in region anterior optic tubercle
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00045003 ! has synaptic IO in region accessory medulla
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-08-09T16:20:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052276
name: obsolete small DN3 neuron
def: "DN3 neuron that has a relatively small cell body (Reinhard et al., 2022). The majority (around 35 per hemisphere) of the DN3s belong to this class and they are heterogeneous (Reinhard et al., 2022). All of these cells project medially and arborize in the superior medial protocerebrum (Reinhard et al., 2022). Some fibers additionally cross the midline via the middle dorsal commissure and some cells extend into the posterior lateral protocerebrum (Reinhard et al., 2022)." [FlyBase:FBrf0253505]
comment: Based on comprehensive analysis by Reinhard et al. (2024) - FBrf0261099 the three main groups are large central-projecting, small central-projecting and anterior-projecting. Anterior-projecting cells "also have larger somata than the s-CPDN3", so the 'small central-projecting DN3 neuron' is the only type of 'small DN3 neuron'.
synonym: "DN3A and DN3B" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0253505]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-08-10T08:11:39Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1997" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00059241

