[Term]
id: FBbt:00052357
name: adult abdominal histaminergic neuron
def: "Adult histaminergic neuron with its cell body in the abdominal neuromere (Nassel et al., 1990). There are 12 of these cells per organism and their somas are located ventrally (Nassel et al., 1990)." [FlyBase:FBrf0052427]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-10-25T12:21:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052358
name: adult mesothoracic histaminergic neuron
def: "Adult histaminergic neuron with its cell body in the mesothoracic neuromere (Nassel et al., 1990). There is one of these cells on each side and its soma is located ventrally (Nassel et al., 1990). It has an axon that runs dorsally and anteriorly, entering the cervical connective (Nassel et al., 1990; Cheong et al., 2024). It arborizes bilaterally in the ventral nerve cord and in the brain (Cheong et al., 2024). It receives most of its input in the wing neuropil and intermediate tectulum (Cheong et al., 2024). Its presynapses are found throughout the pro- and meso-thoracic neuromeres as well as in the subesophageal zone, saddle and posterior slope (Cheong et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0052427, FlyBase:FBrf0258993]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00004019 ! fasciculates with adult cervical connective
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00047137 ! receives synaptic input in region wing neuropil
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00047519 ! receives synaptic input in region intermediate tectulum
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00040072 ! sends synaptic output to region posterior slope
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045048 ! sends synaptic output to region saddle
