[Term]
id: FBbt:00052371
name: larval VNC ensheathing glial cell
def: "Ensheathing glial cell of the larval ventral nerve cord. There are approximately four of these cells that ensheath the synaptic neuropil in each abdominal hemineuromere throughout larval development, including two that wrap the proximal parts of the nerve roots (Pogodalla et al., 2021). Three of these four synaptic neuropil-ensheathing glia derive from the longitudinal glioblast (Peco et al., 2016). There are also three or four midline glia per neuromere, which ensheath the commissural axons (Ito et al., 1995; Banerjee et al., 2017). Some of these cells also extend into the dorsal cell body rind and wrap neuronal cell bodies (Pogodalla et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0231858, FlyBase:FBrf0236333, FlyBase:FBrf0251788]
synonym: "embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord ensheathing neuropil associated glial cell" EXACT []
intersection_of: FBbt:00047836 ! ensheathing glial cell
intersection_of: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001102 ! part of larval ventral nerve cord
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-10-27T10:39:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052372
name: larval VNC astrocyte-like glial cell
def: "Astrocyte-like glial cell of the larval ventral nerve cord. It has a prominent process extending into the neuropil proximal to its nucleus (Pogodalla et al., 2021). There are approximately 6 of these cells in each hemineuromere throughout larval development, found in fixed locations: 3 dorsal, 2 lateral and one ventral (Peco et al., 2016). They develop from prospero-expressing interface glia (Peco et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231858, FlyBase:FBrf0251788]
synonym: "embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord astrocyte-like neuropil associated glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord reticulated neuropil associated glial cell" EXACT []
