[Term]
id: FBbt:00052384 ! labial neuroblast NB6-4
def: "Neuroblast NB6-4 found in a labial segment. Its first division produces a daughter cell that generates only glia and a daughter cell that produces ganglion mother cells that give rise to neurons (Becker et al., 2016). It does not produce a secondary lineage (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327, FlyBase:FBrf0231386]
synonym: "NB6-4lab" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0231386]
