[Term]
id: FBbt:00052513 ! abdominal 9 neuroblast NB5-4
def: "Neuroblast NB5-4 found in abdominal segment 9. It begins to express doublesex in the late embryo, resulting in sexually-dimorphic behavior in the larva (Birkholz et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221210]
comment: Appears to be two of these on each side in the larva (expressing same markers and generating similar male secondary lineage) - unclear whether this is due to division, migration or if one is a different type of neuroblast (Birkholz et al., 2013).
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0002451 ! has characteristic sexually dimorphic
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-11-08T08:43:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052514
name: larval abdominal 9 neuroblast NB5-4 (male)
def: "Neuroblast NB5-4 found in male abdominal segment 9 at the larval stage. It begins to express doublesex in the late embryo, and proliferates to generate a male-specific secondary lineage (Birkholz et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221210]
synonym: "A9 NB5-4 (male)" EXACT []
synonym: "female Dsx+tNB" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0243282]
