[Term]
id: FBbt:00052516
name: embryonic anterior midline glial cell
def: "Embryonic midline glial cell found in an anterior position in the neuromere (Wheeler et al., 2006). At least six of these cells are generated in the embryo, but only three survive to become mature glia in the larva, with the remainder being removed by apoptosis (Dong and Jacobs, 1997; Wheeler et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0098773, FlyBase:FBrf0195284]
subset: cur
synonym: "AMG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0195284]
synonym: "anterior MG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0098773]
synonym: "MGA" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0098773, FlyBase:FBrf0207445]
synonym: "MGM" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0098773, FlyBase:FBrf0207445]
is_a: FBbt:00052369 ! embryonic glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001082 ! part of embryonic ventral nerve cord
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00016014 ! part of midline glial primordium
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00007052 ! develops from embryonic midline glioblast
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-11-10T13:09:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052517
name: primary interneuron
def: "Any interneuron that is born during the embryonic stage. It may persist into the adult stage, usually with some remodelling (Marin et al., 2005)." [FlyBase:FBrf0183938]
