[Term]
id: FBbt:00052538
name: optic lobe amacrine neuron Am1
def: "Amacrine neuron that is intrinsic to the optic lobe and innervates the medulla, lobula and lobula plate (Shinomiya et al., 2019). Its cell body is found next to the lobula plate and its cell body fiber enters the lobula plate from the posterior side (Shinomiya et al., 2019). It branches into columnar fibers that arborize in lobula plate layer 2 (Shinomiya et al., 2019). These fibers bifurcate, projecting via the second optic chiasma to innervate lobula layer 2 and medulla layers 8-9 (Shinomiya et al., 2019). It only innervates the posterior columns of the medulla and some of its fibers terminate and make synapses within the second optic chiasma (Shinomiya et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0243899, FlyBase:FBrf0254308]
is_a: FBbt:00005127 ! optic lobe amacrine neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00001948 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult lobula plate
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003758 ! has synaptic IO in region medulla layer M8
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003759 ! has synaptic IO in region medulla layer M9
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003854 ! has synaptic IO in region lobula layer 2
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003887 ! has synaptic IO in region lobula plate layer 2
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003922 ! has synaptic IO in region second optic chiasma
relationship: RO:0013010 FBbt:00003701 ! synapses restricted to region adult optic lobe
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-12-02T16:23:37Z" xsd:dateTime

