[Term]
id: FBbt:00052601
name: prothoracic proximal femoral pretarsal depressor muscle cell
def: "Muscle cell of the prothoracic femoral pretarsal depressor muscle that attaches to the proximal tip of the long tendon (Kuan et al., 2020). There are two of these fibers per prothoracic leg and they are innervated by a single motor neuron, which is distinct from the ones innervating the distal cells (Kuan et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0247324]
