[Term]
id: FBbt:00052602
name: prothoracic distal femoral pretarsal depressor muscle cell
def: "Muscle cell of the prothoracic femoral pretarsal depressor muscle that attaches to the long tendon more distally than the proximal cells (Kuan et al., 2020). There are four of these fibers per prothoracic leg and they are innervated by two motor neurons, which are distinct from the one innervating the proximal cells (Kuan et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0247324]
synonym: "prothoracic distal femoral long tendon muscle fiber" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247324]
