id: FBbt:00052628
name: ventral scoloparium of femoral chordotonal organ
def: "Scoloparium that contains the dendrites of all claw neurons and hook extension neurons of a femoral chordotonal organ (Mamiya et al., 2023). It is ventral to the lateral scoloparium and somata are organized into two groups, with claw neurons in a proximal cluster and hook extension neurons in a distal cluster (Mamiya et al., 2023). Cell bodies in this scoloparium tend to move around during joint extension and flexion (Mamiya et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0257853]
comment: Mamiya et al. (2023) are inconsistent with use of 'group 1', 'group 2' and 'group 3' terminology, so these synonyms have not been added cp231212.
is_a: FBbt:00052626 ! scoloparium of femoral chordotonal organ
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2023-09-12T12:03:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052629
name: lateral scoloparium of femoral chordotonal organ
def: "Scoloparium that contains the dendrites of all hook flexion neurons of a femoral chordotonal organ (Mamiya et al., 2023). It is the smallest and most lateral scoloparium of the femoral chordotonal organ (Mamiya et al., 2023). Cell bodies in this scoloparium tend to move very little during joint extension and flexion (Mamiya et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0257853]
comment: Mamiya et al. (2023) are inconsistent with use of 'group 1', 'group 2' and 'group 3' terminology, so these synonyms have not been added cp231212.
is_a: FBbt:00052626 ! scoloparium of femoral chordotonal organ
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2023-09-12T12:08:33Z" xsd:dateTime

