[Term]
id: FBbt:00052653
name: larval ascending moonwalker-like backward neuron
def: "Larval primary neuron with its soma in the subesophageal zone (SEZ), dendritic arborization from the SEZ to the mesothoracic neuromere, and ascending axonal projections terminating dorsoposterior to the antennal lobe (Omamiuda-Ishikawa et al., 2020; Israel and Parnas, 2025). There is one of these cells per hemisphere and it is cholinergic (Omamiuda-Ishikawa et al., 2020). It is activated by blue light, downstream of class IV dendritic arborizing neurons (Omamiuda-Ishikawa et al., 2020). It outputs onto and can activate the mooncrawler descending neurons to stimulate backwards locomotion (Omamiuda-Ishikawa et al., 2020). It is the precursor to the adult mooSEZ neuron (Israel and Parnas, 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0247105, FlyBase:FBrf0264223]
comment: Does not fit FBbt definition of ascending as soma is in SEZ and not VNC.
synonym: "larval AMB neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0247105]
synonym: "larval moonwalker subesophageal zone neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0264223]
synonym: "larval MooSEZ neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0264223]
is_a: FBbt:00047097 ! primary neuron
