[Term]
id: FBbt:00052705
name: adult fruitless pIP-a neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron that develops from neuroblast DL2 (CP3) (Ren et al., 2016) and has its cell body in the posterior inferior protocerebrum (Yu et al., 2010). In the brain, it has arbors in the lateral protocerebral complex (Yu et al., 2010). It descends to the ventral nerve cord, where it has presynaptic terminals in all three thoracic neuromeres (Cachero et al., 2010; Yu et al., 2010). There are many more of these cells in males than females (Ren et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: Cachero et al. (2010) report 14 cells per hemisphere.
synonym: "adult fru-P neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "adult fruitless P2b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974]
synonym: "adult fruitless pIP1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
