[Term]
id: FBbt:00052710
name: adult fruitless pMP-e neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron that develops from the DM4 neuroblast (Ren et al., 2016). There are many more of these cells in males than females and they are highly sexually dimorphic (Ren et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: Ren et al. (2016) identify the DM4-derived female equivalent of the male pMP-e (P1) neurons and note that the female pMP-e clone in Cachero et al. (2010) may a be misidentified unrelated clone. Unlike in the male, there does not appear to be overlap between dsx pC1 and fru pMP-e in the female (Ren et al., 2016).
