[Term]
id: FBbt:00052765
name: adult large Ms cell of pars intercerebralis
def: "Myosuppressin-expressing neuron of the pars intercerebralis that has a relatively large soma (Hadjieconomou et al., 2020). It has a single process that bifurcates to form a projection to the gut that arborizes in the hypocerebral ganglion and also innervates the crop, and a shorter process that reaches the subesophageal zone (Hadjieconomou et al., 2020). There are approximately 18 of these cells per organism (Hadjieconomou et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0247320]
comment: McKim et al. (2024) - doi:10.7554/eLife.102684.1 only find 6 DMS cells that follow the NCC in FAFB.
