[Term]
id: FBbt:00052796
name: mechanosensory neuron of dorsal postorbital bristle
def: "Mechanosensory neuron that has its dendrite in a dorsal postorbital bristle. It follows the occipital nerve and terminates in the subesophageal zone (Eichler et al., 2024). It remains ipsilateral in the brain (Eichler et al., 2024). There is one of these per dorsal postorbital bristle (around 7 per side) (Eichler et al., 2024). Its activity elicits head grooming behavior (Eichler et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259346]
synonym: "BM-dPoOr neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259346]
