[Term]
id: FBbt:00052850
name: lobula plate intrinsic neuron LPi1-2
def: "Intrinsic neuron of the lobula plate that has its synaptic terminals throughout, but restricted to lobula plate layers 1 and 2, receiving input in layer 1 and sending output to layer 2 (Shinomiya et al., 2022). The majority of its input is from T4a and T5a cells (Shinomiya et al., 2022). It has its soma in the lobula plate cell body rind (Shinomiya et al., 2022). There are two of these cells per optic lobe and they tile the lobula plate in a jigsaw-like pattern (Matsliah et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0254308, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Matsliah et al. (2024) - FBrf0260545 nomenclature scheme unrelated to layer innervation.
synonym: "LPi12" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "LPi14" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260545]
is_a: FBbt:00003910 ! lobula plate intrinsic neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00001948 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult lobula plate
relationship: RO:0013005 FBbt:00003886 ! receives synaptic input throughout lobula plate layer 1
relationship: RO:0013006 FBbt:00003887 ! sends synaptic output throughout lobula plate layer 2
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00003732 ! receives synaptic input from neuron T4a neuron
relationship: RO:0013008 FBbt:00003737 ! receives synaptic input from neuron T5a neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-02-16T15:02:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00052851
name: lobula plate intrinsic neuron LPi2-1
def: "Intrinsic neuron of the lobula plate that has its synaptic terminals mainly restricted to lobula plate layers 1 and 2, receiving input in layer 2 and sending output to layer 1 (Shinomiya et al., 2022). The majority of its input is from T4b and T5b cells (Shinomiya et al., 2022). There is one of these cells per optic lobe (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0254308, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Matsliah et al. (2024) nomenclature scheme unrelated to layer innervation.
