[Term]
id: FBbt:00052867
name: ovarian hemocyte
def: "Plasmatocyte that is associated with the ovary and contributes to the extracellular matrix (Van De Bor et al., 2015). Some of these cells originate in the embryo and some originate in the larva (Van De Bor et al., 2015). Their numbers reach a maximum at 18 hours after puparium formation, but some still persist in the adult (Van De Bor et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0229943]
synonym: "ovarian companion hemocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0229943]
synonym: "ovarian companion plasmatocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0229943]
