[Term]
id: FBbt:00053052
name: adult fruitless vMS17 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body located in the ventral mesothoracic neuromere (Lillvis et al., 2024). It has arbors ipsilaterally in three thoracic neuromeres and contralateral arbors in the mesothoracic neuromere (Lillvis et al., 2024). There is one of these cells on each side (Lillvis et al., 2024). It is dopaminergic and serotonergic (Lillvis et al., 2024). It is the mesothoracic IN27X002 neuron (Sturner et al., 2025; Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1, FlyBase:FBrf0258823, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
