[Term]
id: FBbt:00053058
name: satellite tergotrochanter muscle motor neuron
def: "Motor neuron that is smaller than the tergotrochanter muscle motor neuron, but also innervates the mesothoracic tergotrochanter muscle (Bacon and Strausfeld, 1986; Cheong et al., 2024). It has its soma and dendritic innervation in the mesothoracic neuromere and exits the ventral nerve cord via the posterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve (Cheong et al., 2024). There are two of these on each side (Cheong et al., 2024)." [doi:10.1007/BF00603798, doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1]
