[Term]
id: FBbt:00053069
name: prothoracic tarsal levator muscle motor neuron
def: "Adult motor neuron that innervates a prothoracic tarsal levator muscle and has its soma in the (anterior) prothoracic neuromere (Brierley et al., 2012; Azevedo et al., 2024). It is a lineage 15 secondary neuron (Brierley et al., 2012). It has dendritic arborization in the anterior and lateral prothoracic neuromere and fasciculates with the prothoracic leg nerve (Azevedo et al., 2024). There are one or two of these cells on each side (Baek and Mann, 2009; Brierley et al., 2012; Azevedo et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208208, FlyBase:FBrf0218373, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
