[Term]
id: FBbt:00053163
name: adult prosternal chordotonal organ neuron
def: "Sensory neuron that has its dendrite in the prosternal (anterior prothoracic) chordotonal organ (Marin et al., 2024). It is proprioceptive (Marin et al., 2024). It follows the prothoracic chordotonal nerve to the prothoracic neuromere, where it joins the dorsal median tract and extends posteriorly (Marin et al., 2024; Gorko et al., 2024). It sends processes towards the midline Gorko et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "neck chordotonal organ neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "pCO neuron" EXACT [doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1]
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00047535 ! fasciculates with adult dorsal median tract
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00049893 ! fasciculates with adult prothoracic chordotonal nerve
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0019230 ! capable of part of proprioception
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-04-22T15:32:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053164
name: adult prosternal sense organ neuron
def: "Adult sensory neuron that has its dendrite in the prosternal sense organ (Marin et al., 2024). It is proprioceptive (Marin et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1]
synonym: "neck hair plate sensory neuron" EXACT [doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1]
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0019230 ! capable of part of proprioception
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-04-22T15:45:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053165
name: adult ventral thoracic neurosecretory neuron
def: "Adult neurosecretory neuron with its soma in the ventral part of the ventral nerve cord and an axonal projection to the dorsal ventral nerve cord, where it has neurosecretory sites (Lindquist and Nassel, 1990). Processes also run anteroposteriorly in the medial dorsal ventral nerve cord and it has an ascending projection to the anterior subesophageal zone (Lindquist and Nassel, 1990). There is one of these per thoracic hemineuromere (Lindquist and Nassel, 1990)." [FlyBase:FBrf0052426]
comment: Lindquist and Nassel (1990) identified an additional large pair of somas (referred to as accessory SPLI neurons/mesothoracic accessory cells) stained in the mesothoracic neuromere, but could not see processes, so unclear whether these are another pair of VTNCs.
synonym: "VTNC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0052426]
is_a: FBbt:00005130 ! neurosecretory neuron
is_a: FBbt:00048301 ! adult ascending neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111082 ! has soma location adult ventral nerve cord cell body rind
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-05-02T09:10:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
