[Term]
id: FBbt:00053181
name: adult oblique horizontal neck muscle 1
def: "Short dorsal neck muscle that attaches at the midline to the pronotal apodeme and extends anterolaterally (Gorko et al., 2024). It attaches via small tendon tendrils to the large tendon of the transverse horizontal muscles (Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the VCvN and CvN2 motor neurons (Gorko et al., 2024). It is posterior to the other oblique horizontal muscles (Gorko et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on dorsomedial attachment and proximity of lateral end to muscle 23 (TH muscles), OH1-3 probably correspond to muscle 20 in Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027.
synonym: "OH1 muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
is_a: FBbt:00058818 ! dorsal cervical muscle 20
relationship: RO:0002371 FBbt:00004576 ! attached to prothoracic phragma
relationship: RO:0002371 FBbt:00053180 ! attached to adult transverse horizontal neck muscle tendon cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-05-14T13:35:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053182
name: adult oblique horizontal neck muscle 2
def: "Short dorsal neck muscle that attaches at the midline to the pronotal apodeme and extends anterolaterally (Gorko et al., 2024). It attaches via small tendon tendrils to the large tendon of the transverse horizontal muscles (Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the VCvN and CvN2 motor neurons (Gorko et al., 2024). It is found between the other oblique horizontal muscles (Gorko et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on dorsomedial attachment and proximity of lateral end to muscle 23 (TH muscles), OH1-3 probably correspond to muscle 20 in Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027.
synonym: "OH2 muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
is_a: FBbt:00058818 ! dorsal cervical muscle 20
relationship: RO:0002371 FBbt:00004576 ! attached to prothoracic phragma
