[Term]
id: FBbt:00053184
name: adult ventral lateral neck muscle 1
def: "Long ventral neck muscle that attaches to a relatively lateral part of the sternal apodeme compared to other ventral muscles and lateral to the VL2 muscle (Gorko et al., 2024). It attaches via a long tendon to the posterior head (Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the CvN5-8 motor neurons (Gorko et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on lateral attachment to sternal apodeme and tendon connecting to posterior head, VL1 and VL2 probably correspond to muscle 27 in Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027.
synonym: "VL1 muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
is_a: FBbt:00058827 ! ventral cervical muscle 27
