property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-05-14T15:22:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053185
name: adult ventral lateral neck muscle 2
def: "Long ventral neck muscle that attaches to a relatively lateral part of the sternal apodeme compared to other ventral muscles and medial to the VL1 muscle (Gorko et al., 2024). It attaches via a long tendon to the posterior head (Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the CvN4 motor neuron (Gorko et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on lateral attachment to sternal apodeme and tendon connecting to posterior head, VL1 and VL2 probably correspond to muscle 27 in Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027.
synonym: "VL2 muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
