[Term]
id: FBbt:00053186
name: adult occipital condyle
def: "Stout cuticular protrusion lateral to the occipital foramen (Strausfeld et al., 1987). It has a concave underside, into which fits the front part of the cervical sclerite, separated by a narrow band of non-sclerotized cuticle to provide flexibility (Strausfeld et al., 1987)." [doi:10.1007/BF00609727, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "OC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
