[Term]
id: FBbt:00053188
name: adult cervical sclerite-occipital condyle dorsoventral neck muscle 2
def: "Dorsoventral muscle that has a broad attachment to the dorsoposterior cervical sclerite and a narrow attachment to the occipital condyle (Strausfeld et al., 1987; Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the DProN2 motor neuron (Gorko et al., 2024)." [doi:10.1007/BF00609727, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on attachment point on posterior head (lateral to occipital foramen) and attachment to cervical sclerite, SC-CO DV1-3 probably correspond to muscle 24 in Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027.
synonym: "SC-CO DV2 muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
