name: adult neck abductor muscle
def: "Dorsal neck muscle that has a transverse orientation, connecting the medial part of the cervical sclerite laterally to the pronotal cuticle (Strausfeld et al., 1987; Gorko et al., 2024)." [doi:10.1007/BF00609727, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: There does not seem to be a muscle matching this description in Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027.
synonym: "ABD muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
