[Term]
id: FBbt:00053219
name: adult abdominal doublesex neuron
def: "Adult doublesex-expressing neuron that has its cell body in the abdominal ganglion (Lee et al., 2002). There are over 300 of these cells in the female and close to 300 in the male (Pavlou et al., 2016). Some of these neurons innervate the internal genitalia via the abdominal nerve trunk and some ascend to the brain via the cervical connection (Rideout et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0159058, FlyBase:FBrf0210397, FlyBase:FBrf0210735, FlyBase:FBrf0234085]
synonym: "adult doublesex AbN neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "doublesex-expressing Abdominal Neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0159058]
synonym: "dsx-Abg" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210397]
synonym: "dsx-expressing Abdominal Neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0159058]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-05-20T11:07:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053220
name: adult doublesex abdominal DDAG_A neuron
def: "Adult doublesex neuron that also expresses dissatisfaction and has its soma in the posterior abdominal ganglion (Diamandi et al., 2024). Its arborization is restricted to a relatively small region of the abdominal ganglion (Diamandi et al., 2024). It is a remodeled primary neuron (Diamandi et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259097]
comment: Found in males and females by Diamandi et al. (2024), but unclear whether dimorphic.
