[Term]
id: FBbt:00053225
name: larval A26g neuron
def: "Larval interneuron of the ventral nerve cord that is part of lineage 26 (Diamandi et al., 2024). Its soma is located dorsolaterally, close to its dorsal dendritic arbors, which extend anteriorly and posteriorly (Diamandi et al., 2024). It extends ventromedially, crossing the midline, then sharply turns back dorsally and projects anteroventrally into the thoracic neuromeres (Diamandi et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259097]
