[Term]
id: FBbt:00053252
name: costal wing vein break
def: "Break in the costal wing vein, which follows the anterior wing margin (McAlpine, 1981). These may give the wing additional flexibility during flight (McAlpine, 1981)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0037040, FlyBase:FBrf0233988]
comment: McAlpine (1981) describes 3 possible breaks in insect wings, based on figures in Ferris (1950) and Fabian et al. (2016), only humeral and subcostal appear to exist in D. melanogaster.
