[Term]
id: FBbt:00053282
name: adult median tract of dorsal cervical fasciculus
def: "Tract that contains the axons of a large number of descending neurons that project to the tectulum (Namiki et al., 2018). The majority of its neurons bend ventrally upon entering the VNC, with a smaller number following the dorsal surface of the VNC and joining the ventral neurons more posteriorly (Namiki et al., 2018)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, FlyBase:FBrf0239335]
comment: Cheong et al. (2024) say the main ventral tract does not overlap with DMT from Court et al. (2020) - FBrf0246815.
