property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2025-04-29T15:40:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053289
name: larval SeIN128 neuron
def: "Larval neuron with its cell body and dendritic arbors in the subesophageal ganglion (Zhu et al., 2024). Its axon follows the midline along most of the length of the ventral nerve cord, innervating medial regions bilaterally (Zhu et al., 2024). There is one of these cells on each side (Zhu et al., 2024). It provides inhibitory GABAergic input to nociceptive rolling circuits (Zhu et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0260352]
