[Term]
id: FBbt:00053331
name: adult lobula plate tangential neuron LPT28
def: "Adult lobula plate tangential neuron with its dendrites spanning around 150 columns of the anterior part of the visual field in lobula plate layer 3, with some input also in layer 4 (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025). In the central brain, it remains ipsilateral and sends output to the inferior and superior posterior slope (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Cell type based on FAFB and optic lobe EM data (Zhao et al., 2023; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025).
is_a: FBbt:00003907 ! lobula plate tangential neuron
is_a: FBbt:00048287 ! visual projection neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003888 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula plate layer 3
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003889 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula plate layer 4
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045040 ! sends synaptic output to region superior posterior slope
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00045046 ! sends synaptic output to region inferior posterior slope
