[Term]
id: FBbt:00053383
name: developing dorsal longitudinal indirect flight muscle
def: "Developing muscle of the pupa that will become a dorsal longitudinal indirect flight muscle (Roy and VijayRaghavan, 1999). The larval mesothoracic dorsal oblique muscles 1-3 escape histolysis and are swarmed by myoblasts from the wing disc, which fuse with the larval muscles (Roy and VijayRaghavan, 1999). These muscles each split in two, forming six templates for the adult muscles (Roy and VijayRaghavan, 1999). They attach to clusters of tendon cell precursors on the wing disc notum (Tiwari et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0103022, FlyBase:FBrf0229972]
synonym: "developing DLM" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0229972]
