[Term]
id: FBbt:00053406
name: transmedullary neuron Tm39
def: "Transmedullary neuron that receives most of its input in around 5 columns of medulla layers M4, M6 and M7-M8, where it also has a small number of presynapses in each innervation region (Nern et al., 2025). It crosses the second optic chiasm and has mixed pre- and post-synapses in around 3 columns of lobula layers 5A-5B (Nern et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Nern et al., 2025). There are around 200 of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Mapped to the Matsliah et al. (2024) Tm7 type, but given a new name in Nern et al. (2025), indicating that it may not be Tm7. Identified in EM and LM in Nern et al. (2025).
