[Term]
id: FBbt:00053412
name: lobula plate tangential neuron Nod1
def: "Lobula plate tangential neuron of the noduli group that receives input in the anterior part of the lobula plate layer 1 visual field, spanning around 100 columns (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025). It sends output mainly to the contralateral inferior posterior slope (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). It is predicted to be cholinergic (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025). There are two of these cells per hemisphere (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025)." [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
