[Term]
id: FBbt:00053413
name: lobula plate tangential neuron Nod2
def: "Lobula plate tangential neuron of the noduli group that receives input in the central part of the lobula plate layer 1 visual field, spanning around 150 columns (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025). Some dendrites also reach layer 3 (Nern et al., 2025). It sends output mainly to the ipsilateral lateral accessory lobe and the contralateral inferior posterior slope (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025)." [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "LPT40" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634]
