[Term]
id: FBbt:00053421
name: adult lobula plate tangential neuron LPT22
def: "Adult lobula plate tangential neuron with its dendrites spanning around 200 columns of the anterior part of the visual field in lobula plate layer 2 (Zhao et al., 2023; Nern et al., 2025). It also has a smaller number of mixed pre- and post-synapses in layer 1 (Nern et al., 2025). In the central brain, it remains ipsilateral and sends output to the lateral accessory lobe (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is GABA (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [doi:10.1101/2023.10.16.562634, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
