[Term]
id: FBbt:00053464
name: lobula plate intrinsic neuron LPi1-4
def: "Lobula plate intrinsic neuron that receives input mainly in layer 1 and sends output mainly to layer 4 (Nern et al., 2025). It has distinct input and output branches (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). It is predicted to be GABAergic (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are 16 of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Matched across 2 EM datasets by Nern et al. (2025).
synonym: "LPi01" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "LPi14" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
is_a: FBbt:00003910 ! lobula plate intrinsic neuron
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 ! capable of gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003886 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula plate layer 1
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00003889 ! sends synaptic output to region lobula plate layer 4
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2025-05-08T08:06:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00053465
name: lobula plate intrinsic neuron LPi2c
def: "Lobula plate intrinsic neuron that spans around 80 columns of layer 2, with little arborization in other layers (Nern et al., 2025). It is predicted to be glutamatergic (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are around 25 of these cells on each side (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Matched across 2 EM datasets and identified at light level by Nern et al. (2025).
