[Term]
id: FBbt:00053503
name: adult medulla-lobula neuron MeLo3b
def: "Adult unilateral optic-lobe-intrinsic neuron with its soma on the dorsal side of the medulla (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). It bifurcates near the soma, sending one branch to the medulla and one to the lobula, without passing through the optic chiasm (Nern et al., 2025). It receives input, but also has presynapses, in medulla layers M3-M4 and M6-M7 in around 10 columns (Nern et al., 2025). It also has pre- and post-synapses in the lobula, in around 10 columns of layer 6 (Nern et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are approximately 40 of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
