[Term]
id: FBbt:00053566
name: mesothoracic sternal adductor muscle motor neuron
def: "Adult motor neuron that has its soma in the mesothoracic neuromere and innervates the mesothoracic sternal adductor muscle (Azevedo et al., 2024; Cheong et al., 2025). There is one of these on each side and it fasciculates with the mesothoracic leg nerve (Cheong et al., 2025; Bates et al., 2025)." [doi:10.1101/2025.07.31.667571, doi:10.7554/elife.96084, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
comment: Segmental homologue of similarly-named prothoracic neuron, but unclear from references which muscle from Miller (1950) - FBrf0186027 this innervates.
