[Term]
id: FBbt:00053589
name: larval Lgr3 neuron of pars intercerebralis
def: "Larval neuron with its soma in the pars intercerebralis that responds to Ilp8 and expresses the Lgr3 receptor (Vallejo et al., 2015). It has thin dendrites that descend into the ventral nerve cord and extensive axonal arborization in the brain, with an axon that crosses the midline (Vallejo et al., 2015). There are two of these cells per hemisphere (Vallejo et al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0230164]
comment: Based on Vallejo et al. (2015), this does not appear to project to the ring gland.
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111670 ! has soma location larval pars intercerebralis
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00001102 ! receives synaptic input in region larval ventral nerve cord
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00001920 ! sends synaptic output to region larval brain
