[Term]
id: FBbt:00058227
name: lobula-lobula plate columnar neuron LLPC1
def: "Lobula-lobula plate columnar neuron that receives input from around 5-10 columns of lobula layer 4 and around 10 columns of lobula plate layer 1, with additional postsynapses in lobula plate layers 2-3 (Isaacson, 2019; Davis et al., 2020; Nern et al., 2025). It remains ipsilateral and sends output to the posterior lateral protocerebrum (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). It is highly sensitive to front-to-back motion on the ipsilateral eye (Isaacson, 2019). It is cholinergic (Davis et al., 2020). There are around 100-120 of these cells on each side (Nern et al., 2025)." [doi:10.17863/CAM.36002, FlyBase:FBrf0244935, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00003881 ! lobula-lobula plate columnar neuron LLPC
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000634 ! has characteristic unilateral
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003856 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula layer 4
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003886 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula plate layer 1
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003887 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula plate layer 2
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003888 ! receives synaptic input in region lobula plate layer 3
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00040044 ! sends synaptic output to region posterior lateral protocerebrum
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2021-07-15T10:42:07Z" xsd:dateTime

