[Term]
id: FBbt:00058316
name: segment border muscle
def: "Most internal of the larval lateral transverse muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It runs along the transverse apodeme at the segment boundary (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It is an external muscle (Landgraf et al., 2003; Kohsaka et al., 2012)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0167986, FlyBase:FBrf0218115]
comment: Here these muscles are considered to 'belong' to the anterior segment of the boundary each muscle runs along, i.e. mesothoracic SBM is between meso- and meta-thoracic segments.
subset: cur
synonym: "SBM muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064793]
is_a: FBbt:00058305 ! lateral transverse muscle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime

