[Term]
id: FBbt:00058346
name: larval thoracic ventral intersegmental muscle
def: "Ventrally located larval hypodermal muscle that belongs to a large bundle of five fibers spanning the thoracic segments (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). They span at least the prothoracic segment (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997), with some fibers attaching to the mouthparts anteriorly (Matthes et al., 1995) and one fiber (VIS5) reaches the apodeme between T3 and A1 posteriorly (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0082330, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
comment: Hooper (1986) - FBrf0044229 shows all of these extending to at least T2-T3 in third instar.
subset: cur
synonym: "larval muscle 32-36" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0082330]
synonym: "mouthpart-associated muscle" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0044229]
synonym: "prothoracic ventral intersegmental muscle" RELATED []
synonym: "VIS" RELATED []
synonym: "VS" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00058311 ! intersegmental muscle
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001743 ! overlaps larval prothoracic segment
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1752" xsd:anyURI

