[Term]
id: FBbt:00058769
name: abdominal 8 ventral longitudinal muscle
def: "Ventral longitudinal muscle of larval segment eight. There are four of these on each side (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Along with the VA1 muscle, these follow a dorsoposterior course and insert at the base of posterior spiracle (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Their contraction pulls the posterior spiracle inside (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
subset: cur
synonym: "A8 VL" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
