[Term]
id: FBbt:00058819
name: dorsal cervical muscle 21
def: "Dorsal cervical muscle that connects to the cervical sclerite and extends anterodorsally to the pronotum (Miller, 1950; Strausfeld et al., 1987; Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the DProN4 motor neuron (Gorko et al., 2024)." [doi:10.1007/BF00609727, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on straight anteroposterior orientation, this seems to correspond to the LEV muscle in Gorko et al. (2024).
subset: cur
synonym: "LEV muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "neck levator muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
is_a: FBbt:00058817 ! dorsal cervical muscle
relationship: RO:0002371 FBbt:00004548 ! attached to fused cervical sclerite
relationship: RO:0002371 FBbt:00004561 ! attached to pronotum
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00058820
name: dorsal cervical muscle 22
def: "Dorsal cervical muscle that connects to the cervical sclerite and extends dorsomedially to the pronotum (Miller, 1950; Strausfeld et al., 1987; Gorko et al., 2024). It is innervated by the DProN5 motor neuron (Gorko et al., 2024)." [doi:10.1007/BF00609727, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on dorsoventral orientation, attachment of ventral end to the cervical sclerite and mapping of muscle 21 to LEV, this seems to correspond to the AD muscle in Gorko et al. (2024).
subset: cur
synonym: "AD muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
