[Term]
id: FBbt:00058824
name: ventral cervical muscle
def: "Muscle of the adult neck that attaches to the prothoracic sternal apodeme and extends anteriorly (Miller, 1950; Rivlin et al., 2004). It occupies a relatively ventral position (Miller, 1950; Rivlin et al., 2004). There are three of these on each side (Miller, 1950; Rivlin et al., 2004)." [FlyBase:FBrf0167817, FlyBase:FBrf0186027]
subset: cur
is_a: FBbt:00058816 ! somatic muscle of neck
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00058825
name: ventral cervical muscle 25
def: "Ventral cervical muscle that connects to a more posterior medial region of the sternal apodeme than muscle 26 (Miller, 1950; Rivlin et al., 2004). There is one of these muscles on each side, innervated by a single motor neuron (Koenig and Ikeda, 1989; Gorko et al., 2024). Its motor neuron arrives via the cervical nerve and forms a branch for each of the six muscle fibers, with each branch bifurcating to run anterior-posterior along its fiber (Koenig and Ikeda, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0050378, FlyBase:FBrf0167817, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on sternal apodeme attachment posteromedial to muscle 26 and innervation via cervical nerve, this seems to correspond to SC-RE in Gorko et al. (2024).
subset: cur
synonym: "adult cervical sclerite retractor muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "SC-RE muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "ventromedial cervical muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0050378, FlyBase:FBrf0167817]
is_a: FBbt:00058824 ! ventral cervical muscle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00058826
name: ventral cervical muscle 26
def: "Ventral cervical muscle that connects to a more anterior lateral region of the sternal apodeme than muscle 25 (Miller, 1950; Rivlin et al., 2004). It is spindle-shaped and comprises 3-4 fibers (Rivlin et al., 2004)." [FlyBase:FBrf0167817, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
comment: Based on sternal apodeme attachment between muscles 25 and 27, this seems to correspond to SC-RO in Gorko et al. (2024). Two of these exist per side in Calliphora (Strausfeld et al., 1987 - doi:10.1007/BF00609727).
subset: cur
synonym: "adult cervical sclerite rotator muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
synonym: "SC-RO muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0259326]
is_a: FBbt:00058824 ! ventral cervical muscle
