[Term]
id: FBbt:00058862
name: prothoracic sternal anterior rotator muscle 31
def: "Large adult prothoracic muscle that originates on the medial plate of the sternal apophysis (sternal furca) at the midline and extends laterally, attaching to the anterior part of the coxa (Rivlin et al., 2004). It is composed of 6-7 fibers (Rivlin et al., 2004). It moves the coxa anteriorly (Azevedo et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0167817, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
