[Term]
id: FBbt:00058874
name: prothoracic intracoxal lateral levator muscle 36
def: "Levator muscle of the adult prothoracic trochanter that extends along the lateral coxa and is lateral to the mesal levator muscle 37." [FlyBase:FBrf0186027]
comment: Azevedo et al. (2024) find only one (main) prothoracic intracoxal trochanter levator (flexor) muscle, but this is split into dorsal and ventral regions attaching on different sides of the tendon, innervated by different MNs. The 'dorsal' fibers probably correspond to this 'lateral' muscle.
