[Term]
id: FBbt:00058907
name: tergopleural muscle
def: "Indirect flight muscle that originates broadly over the dorsal episternum and inserts via a thick tendon on the meso-scutum (Dickinson and Tu, 1997). This muscle is innervated by the dorsal and ventral tp motor neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0064793, FlyBase:FBrf0074636, FlyBase:FBrf0098527, FlyBase:FBrf0192609, FlyBase:FBrf0193310]
comment: Classified as indirect in Dickinson and Tu (1997), as these muscles do not connect to a wing sclerite, but they note that the muscles do insert within the hinge region and could affect hinge mechanics.
subset: cur
synonym: "3rd & 4th basalar muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0006004]
