[Term]
id: FBbt:00058939
name: haltere dorsal ventral muscle
def: "Relatively large haltere muscle that extends dorsoventrally and attaches to the cuticle near the base of the haltere (Lawrence, 1982; Dickerson et al., 2019). It provides the power for haltere movement, analogous to dorsoventral muscles of the wing (Dickerson et al., 2019; Ehrhardt et al., 2023)." [doi:10.1101/2023.05.31.542897, FlyBase:FBrf0037610, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
comment: Muscle 77 in Lawrence (1982) (following Miller, 1950 nomenclature) is a relatively long muscle described as attaching near the base of the haltere - so probably corresponds to the haltere DVM (hDVM) in Dickerson et al. (2019) and Ehrhardt et al. (2023).
subset: cur
synonym: "haltere indirect asynchronous power muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
synonym: "haltere muscle 77" EXACT []
synonym: "hDVM" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
