id: FBbt:00058940
name: haltere axillary muscle
def: "Small muscle that attaches near the base of the haltere, posterior to the basalar muscles (Lawrence, 1982; Dickerson et al., 2019). There are five of these muscles per haltere (Dickerson et al., 2019)." [doi:10.1101/2023.05.31.542897, FlyBase:FBrf0037610, FlyBase:FBrf0186027, FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
comment: Muscle 78 in Lawrence (1982) (following Miller, 1950 nomenclature) is the posteriormost of two small muscles described as attaching near the base of the haltere - so probably corresponds to the haltere axillary muscle group in Dickerson et al. (2019) and Ehrhardt et al. (2023).
subset: cur
synonym: "haltere muscle 78" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0037610]
synonym: "hI muscle" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
synonym: "hIII muscle" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
is_a: FBbt:00059258 ! haltere steering muscle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00058941
name: haltere basalar muscle
def: "Small muscle that attaches near the base of the haltere, anterior to the axillary muscles (Lawrence, 1982; Dickerson et al., 2019). There are two of these muscles per haltere (Dickerson et al., 2019)." [doi:10.1101/2023.05.31.542897, FlyBase:FBrf0037610, FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
comment: Muscle 78a in Lawrence (1982) (following Miller, 1950 nomenclature) is the anteriormost of two small muscles described as attaching near the base of the haltere - so probably corresponds to the haltere basalare muscle group in Dickerson et al. (2019) and Ehrhardt et al. (2023).
subset: cur
synonym: "haltere basalare muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0243782]
synonym: "haltere muscle 78a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0037610]
