[Term]
id: FBbt:00059104
name: accessory tibial flexor muscle
def: "Muscle that originates in the distal femur and attaches to the proximal tibia (Soler et al., 2004; Azevedo et al., 2024). It is the shorter of two muscles that flex the femur-tibia joint (Azevedo et al., 2020; Azevedo et al., 2024). It is composed of 29 fibers (Kuan et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0180184, FlyBase:FBrf0246170, FlyBase:FBrf0247324, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
comment: Miller (1950) call this a depressor (show one large and one small tibial depressor per leg). Soler et al. (2004) refer to this (smaller) muscle as a tibia reductor. Azevedo et al. (2020, 2022) say that this muscle flexes the femur-tibia joint and it is referred to in Azevedo et al. (2024) as the 'accessory tibia flexor'.
subset: cur
synonym: "tibial reductor muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0180184, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
synonym: "TiR muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0218373]
synonym: "tirm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0180184]
is_a: FBbt:00053091 ! leg flexor muscle
is_a: FBbt:00058842 ! leg depressor muscle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2022-07-05T13:30:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00059105
name: tarsal retro depressor muscle
def: "Adult leg muscle with fibers that originate at the distal end of the tibial cuticle and attach to the tarsal depressor tendon in a position proximal their origin sites (Soler et al., 2004; Azevedo et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0180184, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
comment: Soler et al. (2004) say that fibers of these muscles do not attach to a tendon, this is corrected in Azevedo et al. (2024), who show that they insert on the tarsus depressor tendon - hence rename to tarsus retro depressor muscle.
subset: cur
synonym: "tarm" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0180184]
synonym: "tarsal reductor muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0180184, FlyBase:FBrf0259940]
is_a: FBbt:00058842 ! leg depressor muscle
