[Term]
id: FBbt:00059376
name: peripodial epithelial cell of eye disc posterior margin
def: "A short, narrow epithelial cell of the peripodial epithelium of the eye disc. These cells form a narrow band at the posterior border between the disc proper and the peripodial epithelium. They are an important source of signals regulating the development of the disc proper (Atkins and Mardon, 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208548]
