[Term]
id: FBbt:00067024
name: antennal basiconic sensillum ab3
def: "A large olfactory basiconic sensillum of the antenna that houses the dendrites of two highly-branched olfactory receptor neurons (Shanbhag et al., 1999), expressing Or22a and Or85b (Couto et al., 2005; de Bruyne and Baker, 2008; Grabe et al., 2016). It has a pore size of about 100 nm and a pore density of about 30 pores per square micrometer (Shanbhag et al., 1999). There are more of these sensilla in females than males (Benton et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0128642, FlyBase:FBrf0187305, FlyBase:FBrf0233453, FlyBase:FBrf0239032, FlyBase:FBrf0262710]
