[Term]
id: FBbt:00067038
name: antennal coeloconic sensillum ac1
def: "Coeloconic olfactory sensillum of the antenna that is innervated by four olfactory receptor neurons (ORNs), expressing Ir92, Ir31a, Ir75d and Amt/Rh50 (Benton et al., 2009; Vulpe et al., 2021). These sensilla are present on the anterior antennal surface just ventral to the arista (Benton et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0187906, FlyBase:FBrf0206496, FlyBase:FBrf0249830]
subset: olfactory_system_draft
is_a: FBbt:00004177 ! coeloconic sensillum of antennal segment 3

[Term]
id: FBbt:00067039
name: adult olfactory receptor neuron Or35a
def: "Olfactory receptor neuron (ORN) that expresses the Odorant receptor (Or) 35a (Benton et al., 2025). Its dendrite transduces signals from an antennal coeloconic ac3 sensillum (of either type) (Benton et al., 2009; Prieto-Godino et al., 2017). Its axon innervates antennal lobe glomerulus VC3, bilaterally, fasciculating with the antennal lobe commissure (Couto et al., 2005; Schlegel et al., 2021). It detects alcohols produced by yeast and is required for the enhancement of the proboscis extension reflex in response to yeast odors in combination with low-viscosity food (Oh et al., 2021). It develops from an Nba precursor (Benton et al., 2025). There are approximately 15-20 of these cells on each side (Benton et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0187305, FlyBase:FBrf0187906, FlyBase:FBrf0206496, FlyBase:FBrf0233453, FlyBase:FBrf0248109, FlyBase:FBrf0249560, FlyBase:FBrf0262710]
comment: A subset of these cells also weakly express Ir76a (Benton et al., 2025).
