[Term]
id: FBbt:00100143
name: gustatory receptor neuron of terminal organ dorsolateral group
def: "Gustatory receptor neuron whose dendrites innervate the terminal organ on the surface of the larval head, but whose soma is located in the dorsal organ ganglion (Python and Stocker, 2002). The axons of these neurons project via the antennal nerve (Python and Stocker, 2002) into area 4 of the subesophageal ganglion (Colomb et al., 2007). There are 3 of these neurons on each side, and all have a dendrite in the dorsomedial papilla of the terminal organ dorsolateral group (Rist and Thum, 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0147119, FlyBase:FBrf0201176, FlyBase:FBrf0236934]
synonym: "atypical TODO neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0201176]
synonym: "terminal organ neuron of dorsal organ ganglion" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0201176]
synonym: "TO-dorsolateral class" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216529]
synonym: "TO-dorsolateral group" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216529]
synonym: "TODO neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0201176]
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00001965 ! fasciculates with embryonic/larval antennal nerve
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00100142 ! sends synaptic output to region embryonic/larval subesophageal ganglion area 4
