[Term]
id: FBbt:00100214
name: adult dopaminergic PAM neuron
def: "A dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a cluster of approximately 100 cell bodies in the cortex of the anterior inferior medial protocerebrum of the adult brain (Mao and Davis, 2009). There are multiple subtypes, of which most (but not all) target the medial lobe (Li et al., 2020). They all follow a mushroom body commissure to the contralateral mushroom body (Li et al., 2020). They are secondary neurons, with some belonging to the CREa1A (BAMd1A) hemilineage and some belonging to the CREa2A (DALcm1A) hemilineage (Lee et al., 2020; Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208427, FlyBase:FBrf0227179, FlyBase:FBrf0248215, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
comment: The cluster of PAM neurons was judged by a curator to correspond to the AM cell cluster in Budnik and White (1988).
synonym: "adult dopaminergic PAM1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234128]
synonym: "AM cell cluster neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048550]
synonym: "PAM cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral anteriomedial dopaminergic cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral anterior medial dopaminergic cluster neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "TH-positive anteriomedial cluster neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00047957 ! adult mushroom body modulatory input neuron
is_a: FBbt:00049541 ! Notch ON hemilineage secondary neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00100213 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult inferior neuropils
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00049929 ! fasciculates with adult mushroom body commissure
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061527 ! capable of dopamine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00013688 ! sends synaptic output to region lobe system of adult mushroom body
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-09-09T10:58:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100215
name: dopaminergic PAL neuron
def: "A dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a cluster of approximately 5 cell bodies in the cortex located lateral to the dorsal portion of the vertical lobes in the middle of the superior lateral protocerebrum of the adult brain. It belongs to the DPLam primary lineage, but does not mature until the pupal stage (Hartenstein et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208427, FlyBase:FBrf0234128]
comment: Mao and Davis (2009) identify 8 protocerebral clusters coincidentally positive for TH-GAL4 activity and tyrosine hydroxylase immunoreactivity, implying these cells are dopaminergic.
synonym: "dopaminergic PAL1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234128]
synonym: "PAL cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral anteriolateral dopaminergic cluster neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "protocerebral anterior lateral dopaminergic cluster neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "TH-positive anteriolateral cluster neuron" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00100202 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult superior lateral protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00053532 ! develops from immature dopaminergic PAL neuron
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061527 ! capable of dopamine secretion, neurotransmission
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-09-09T11:03:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100216
name: dopaminergic PPM1 neuron
def: "Dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a small cluster along the dorsoventral midline of the posterior superior medial protocerebrum of the adult brain." [FlyBase:FBrf0208427]
comment: Mao and Davis (2009) identify 8 protocerebral clusters coincidentally positive for TH-GAL4 activity and tyrosine hydroxylase immunoreactivity, implying these cells are dopaminergic. They refer to the protocerebral posteriomedial dopaminergic neuron 1 as a cluster. Hartenstein et al. (2017) - FBrf0234128 show that the larval DM1 cluster (primary DPMm1/l1 lineages) becomes the adult PPM1 cluster, but unclear whether any adult cells do not derive from functional larval primary neurons.
synonym: "PPM1 cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posteriomedial dopaminergic neuron 1" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posterior medial dopaminergic neuron 1" EXACT []
synonym: "TH-positive posterior medial cluster 1 neuron" EXACT []
