relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00100204 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult superior medial protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061527 ! capable of dopamine secretion, neurotransmission
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-09-09T11:07:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100217
name: dopaminergic PPM2 neuron
def: "A dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a cluster of approximately 8 cell bodies in the cortex of the posterior inferior medial protocerebrum of the adult brain (Mao and Davis, 2009). Different subtypes develop from the DM2, DM3 and DM4 neuroblasts (Ren et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0048550, FlyBase:FBrf0208427, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: Mao and Davis (2009) identify 8 protocerebral clusters coincidentally positive for TH-GAL4 activity and tyrosine hydroxylase immunoreactivity, implying these cells are dopaminergic. The cluster of PPM2 neurons was judged by a curator to correspond to the DM cell cluster in Budnik and White (1988). Hartenstein et al. (2017) - FBrf0234128 show that the larval DM2 cluster (primary DPMpm1/2 lineages) becomes the adult PPM2 cluster, but unclear whether any adult cells do not derive from functional larval primary neurons.
synonym: "DM cell cluster neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048550]
synonym: "PPM2 cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posteriomedial dopaminergic cluster neuron 2" RELATED []
synonym: "protocerebral posterior medial dopaminergic cluster neuron 2" RELATED []
synonym: "TH-positive posterior medial cluster neuron 2" EXACT []
