relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00100213 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult inferior neuropils
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061527 ! capable of dopamine secretion, neurotransmission
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-09-09T11:11:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100218
name: dopaminergic PPM3 neuron
def: "A dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a cluster in the cortex of the superior posterior slope of the adult brain (Mao and Davis, 2009). There are approximately 8-9 of these cells and their axons project along the medial equatorial fascicle to the central complex and adjacent neuropil regions (Omoto et al., 2018). It belongs to the DM6 (CM3) primary lineage (Ren et al., 2016; Hartenstein et al., 2017; Schlegel et al., 2024), but does not mature until metamorphosis (Hartenstein et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0048550, FlyBase:FBrf0208427, FlyBase:FBrf0233706, FlyBase:FBrf0234128, FlyBase:FBrf0240929, FlyBase:FBrf0260535]
comment: Mao and Davis (2009) identify 8 protocerebral clusters coincidentally positive for TH-GAL4 activity and tyrosine hydroxylase immunoreactivity, implying these cells are dopaminergic. The cluster of PPM3 neurons was judged by a curator to correspond to the PM cell cluster in Budnik and White (1988). Hartenstein et al. (2017) map PPM3 to CM4 (DM4) primary lineage based on morphology and HU application, Ren et al. (2016) - map to CM3 (DM6) secondary lineage based on markers and heat shock induction, Schlegel et al. (2024) assign all subtypes as DM6 primary neurons based on EM.
synonym: "PM cell cluster neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048550]
synonym: "PPM3 cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posteriomedial dopaminergic cluster 3 neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posterior medial dopaminergic cluster neuron 3" EXACT []
synonym: "TH-positive posterior medial cluster neuron 3" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00100212 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult posterior slope
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00100342 ! fasciculates with adult medial equatorial fascicle
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00053531 ! develops from immature dopaminergic PPM3 neuron
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061527 ! capable of dopamine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00003632 ! sends synaptic output to region adult central complex
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2010-09-09T11:16:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100219
name: dopaminergic PPL1 neuron
def: "A dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a cluster of approximately 12 cell bodies in the cortex of the posterior inferior lateral protocerebrum of the adult brain, immediately lateral to the mushroom body calyx. Members of this group project to various parts of the mushroom body: the tip of the alpha lobe; the tip of the alpha' lobe; the upper portion of the alpha lobe segment 2; alpha lobe segment 1 and the lower part of segment 2; and the pedunculus and spur (Mao and Davis, 2009). Long-range fibers project bilaterally to and arborize in the tips and stalks of the alpha and alpha' lobes, the heel and the peduncle (Claridge-Chang et al., 2009). Other members of this group arborize in areas other than the mushroom body: the edge of the medial portions of the medial lobes; broad areas surrounding the ipsilateral vertical lobes; areas posterior to the ipsilateral vertical lobes; the entire span of the superior arch (Mao and Davis, 2009) and the central complex (Claridge-Chang et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0048550, FlyBase:FBrf0208427, FlyBase:FBrf0208958, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: Mao and Davis (2009) identify 8 protocerebral clusters coincidentally positive for TH-GAL4 activity and tyrosine hydroxylase immunoreactivity, implying these cells are dopaminergic. Mao and Davis (2009) use a heat shock-induced flip-out system to visualize the projection pattern of one or a few GFP-positive clones. The cluster of PPL1 neurons was judged by a curator to correspond to the DL1 cell cluster in Budnik and White (1988).
synonym: "DL1 cell cluster neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048550]
synonym: "PPL1 cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posteriolateral dopaminergic cluster neuron 1" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral posterior lateral cluster neuron 1" EXACT []
synonym: "TH-positive posteriolateral cluster neuron 1" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
