[Term]
id: FBbt:00100310
name: posterior signaling center of lymph gland primary lobe
def: "A cluster of specialized signaling cells at the posterior tip of the primary lobe of the larval lymph gland that serves as a niche that regulates the differentiation of prohemocytes into plasmatocytes, crystal cells and lamellocytes (Krzemien et al., 2007; Mandal et al., 2007). It arises from cells of the embryonic metathoracic segment and it can be distinguished as a distinct region of the lymph gland in the late embryo (Mandal et al., 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194088, FlyBase:FBrf0194113, FlyBase:FBrf0241407]
synonym: "posterior signaling center of anterior lymph gland pair" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior signalling center of lymph gland primary lobe" EXACT []
