[Term]
id: FBbt:00100344
name: posterior cerebro-cervical fascicle
def: "The posterior cerebro-cervical fascicle derives from the superior lateral part of the cervical connective and terminates in the inferior fiber system (Ito et al., 2014). It demarcates the boundaries of the superior posterior slope (inferior region), inferior posterior slope (superior region) and wedge (superior-medial) (Ito et al., 2014). It contains the axon of the giant fiber neuron (Ito et al., 2014)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "posterior CCF" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior cerebrocervical fascicle" EXACT []
