id: FBbt:00100362
name: antennal lobe hub
def: "Central, non-glomerular region of the adult antennal lobe. It is distinguished from the antennal lobe glomeruli in that olfactory receptor neurons do not terminate here, though antennal lobe projection neurons and many local neurons run through this area. The density of synapses is lower than in the antennal lobe glomeruli." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00007401 ! part of adult antennal lobe

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100363
name: superior bulb
def: "Region of the bulb that lies in a superior position between the mushroom body pedunculus and the ellipsoid body. It contains many small glomeruli." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003682 ! part of bulb
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00051441 ! develops from superior bulb primordium

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100364
name: inferior bulb
def: "Region of the bulb that lies in an inferior position between the mushroom body pedunculus and the ellipsoid body. It contains many small glomeruli." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003682 ! part of bulb
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00051442 ! develops from inferior bulb primordium

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100365
name: anterior bulb
def: "Region of the bulb that lies beneath the mushroom body pedunculus, closer to the somata of the ellipsoid body neurons than the superior and inferior bulb. It is formed by the antero-lateral and inferior extension of the lateral region of the superior bulb." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003682 ! part of bulb

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100366
name: plexiform lamina
def: "The main part of the lamina that does not contain the terminals of photoreceptors from dorsal rim ommatidia." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003708 ! part of lamina

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100367
name: adult antennal lobe projection neuron DA4l adPN
def: "Adult uniglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron from the ad neuroblast (ALad1) lineage with dendrites that mainly innervate antennal lobe glomerulus DA4l. It born from the fifth division of neuroblast ALad1 during embryogenesis (Yu et al., 2010). There is one of these cells per hemisphere, it fasciculates with the medial antennal lobe tract and it is cholinergic (Bates et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729, FlyBase:FBrf0246460]
subset: olfactory_system_draft
synonym: "DA4l adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00007053 ! sends synaptic output to region adult lateral horn
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00007385 ! sends synaptic output to region calyx of adult mushroom body

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100368
name: adult uniglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron adPN
def: "An adult uniglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron that is derived from the neuroblast ALad1 (FBbt:00067346). All of these neurons have axons that fasciculate with the medial antennal lobe tract (mALT) and except for V adPN neurons, innervate the mushroom body calyx (via a collateral) and the lateral horn." [FlyBase:FBrf0141667, FlyBase:FBrf0146917, FlyBase:FBrf0205814, FlyBase:FBrf0211729, FlyBase:FBrf0221835]
comment: Generalizations about fasciculation are safe here. But the 4 PNs have still not been analyzed: DA4m, DC4, VP2, and VL1. See Yu et al. (2010) for details.
subset: hidden_assertion
synonym: "adult uniglomerular adPN" EXACT []
synonym: "adult uniglomerular anterodorsal antennal lobe projection neuron" EXACT []

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100369
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron adPN
def: "An adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron that is derived from the neuroblast ALad1 (FBbt:00067346). Most of these neurons have axons that fasciculate with the medial antennal lobe tract (mALT) and innervate the lateral horn (Yu et al., 2010; Bates et al., 2020). Secondary neurons of this lineage are cholinergic (Bates et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729, FlyBase:FBrf0246460]
comment: Bates et al. (2020) found a total of 11 secondary multiglomerular adPNs in the right antennal lobe (EM data). One type fasciculates with a transverse ALT. Yu et al. (2010) found a total of 10 secondary + 1 primary (primary subsequently reclassified as uniglomerular+).

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100370
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron L1 adPN
def: "Multiglomerular adult antennal lobe projection neuron of the adPN lineage. This is the 17th cell type to be generated post-embryonically by neuroblast ALad1 (Yu et al., 2010). Its innervation targets include parts of glomeruli DC3, VC3 and VM4." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
comment: See FBrf0211729 for image.
synonym: "poly[L1] adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100371
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron L2 adPN
def: "Multiglomerular adult antennal lobe projection neuron of the adPN lineage. This is the 18th cell type to be generated post-embryonically by neuroblast ALad1 (Yu et al., 2010). Its innervation targets include parts of glomeruli VM4 and VL2p." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
comment: See FBrf0211729 for image.
synonym: "poly[L2] adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100372
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron L3 adPN
def: "Multiglomerular adult antennal lobe projection neuron of the adPN lineage. This is the 19th cell type to be generated post-embryonically by neuroblast ALad1 (Yu et al., 2010). Its dendrites innervate glomeruli VL2p, VL2a and DL1." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
comment: See FBrf0211729 for image.
synonym: "poly[L3] adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100373
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron L4 adPN
def: "Multiglomerular adult antennal lobe projection neuron of the adPN lineage. This is the 20th cell type to be generated post-embryonically by neuroblast ALad1 (Yu et al., 2010). Its innervation targets include parts of glomeruli VL2a, Dl1, DL2v and DL2d." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
comment: See FBrf0211729 for image.
synonym: "poly[L4] adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100374
name: adult uniglomerular projection neuron VP5+SEZ adPN
def: "Uniglomerular adult antennal lobe projection neuron of the adPN lineage with its dendrites predominantly in glomerulus VP5, as well as the subesophageal zone, and some innervation of other antennal glomeruli (Yu et al., 2010; Marin et al., 2020; Bates et al., 2020). It is born from the 12th embryonic division of the neuroblast ALad1, after the division that produces DC1 adPN (Yu et al., 2010). There is one of these cells per hemisphere, it follows the medial antennal lobe tract and it is cholinergic (Marin et al., 2020). Its main downstream target type is a set of around 11 gamma main Kenyon cells, that extend non-claw-like dendrites outside of the main calyx, whilst also having dendritic claws inside the main calyx (Li et al., 2020). It connects to these at three locations just anterior to the main calyx (Li et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729, FlyBase:FBrf0246456, FlyBase:FBrf0246460, FlyBase:FBrf0248215]
comment: Defined as multiglomerular by Yu et al. (2010), redefined as uniglomerular+ (has some terminals outside of main glomerulus) by Marin et al. (2020). Mapped to Li et al. (2020) ALPN2 based on neuprint bodyID.
synonym: "ALPN2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246721]
synonym: "multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron emb adPN" EXACT []
synonym: "poly[emb] adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
synonym: "VP5+SEZ adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246456]
synonym: "VP5+Z adPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0248215]
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00110639 ! receives synaptic input in region adult subesophageal zone
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00111061 ! sends synaptic output to cell gamma main Kenyon cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100375
name: obsolete antennal lobe glomerulus DL1l
def: "Lateral region of antennal lobe glomerulus DL1." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
comment: Obsoleted as this is not considered to be a distinct glomerulus in recent studies (Bates et al., 2020 - FBrf0246460; Schlegel et al., 2021 - FBrf0249560; Task et al., 2022 - FBrf0253272). Defined by terminals of polyglomerular PNs (Yu et al., 2010).
synonym: "antennal lobe glomerulus DL1 lateral compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "DL1l" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00003968

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100376
name: antennal lobe glomerulus DL2v
def: "DL2 glomerulus ventral to DL2d. It lies on the ventromedial margin of the dorsal compartment and immediately ventral to glomerulus DL1." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
synonym: "antennal lobe glomerulus DL2 ventral compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "DL2v" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100377
name: antennal lobe glomerulus DL2d
def: "DL2 glomerulus that is dorsal to DL2v. It lies at the dorsoventral margin of the ventral compartment and ventral to glomerulus DA1." [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
synonym: "antennal lobe glomerulus DL2 dorsal compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "DL2d" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211729]

