[Term]
id: FBbt:00100519
name: fenestrated glial cell
def: "Surface glial cell of the adult optic lobe. The fenestrated glia form a layer overlying the pseudocartridge glial cell layer and contact the basement membrane (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). These cells are specialized perineurial glial cells of the optic lobe (Kremer et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210316, FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "L-iPNG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "lamina interface perineurial glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
is_a: FBbt:00004210 ! adult subretinal glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00007089 ! part of perineurial glial sheath
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-05-12T02:45:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100520
name: pseudocartridge glial cell
def: "Surface glial cell of the adult optic lobe. The pseudocartridge glial cells form a layer beneath the distal fenestrated glial cells (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). These cells are specialized subperineurial glial cells of the optic lobe (Kremer et al., 2017). One cell may envelop multiple partial ommatidial bundles, with some bundles shared between neighboring glia, similar to the tiling displayed by other glial types (Kremer et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210316, FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "L-iSPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "lamina interface subperineurial glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
is_a: FBbt:00004210 ! adult subretinal glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00007091 ! part of subperineurial glial sheath
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-05-12T03:03:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100521
name: embryonic/larval wrapping glial cell of the eye disc
def: "Glial cell found among photoreceptor cell axons in the eye disc that wraps these axons as they extend to the optic stalk (Hummel et al., 2002; Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). The wrapping glial cells are, in turn, surrounded and wrapped by surface glial cells (Hummel et al., 2002). These cells develop from precursors that migrate from the optic stalk into the eye disc and differentiate upon coming into contact with photoreceptor axons (Choi and Benzer, 1994; Hummel et al., 2002; Silies et al., 2007; Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). Wrapping glial cells (of the eye disc) are associated with Bolwig's nerve, but do not wrap it (Silies et al., 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0068448, FlyBase:FBrf0145174, FlyBase:FBrf0201162, FlyBase:FBrf0210316]
synonym: "embryonic/larval wrapping glia" RELATED []
synonym: "embryonic/larval wrapping glia of the eye disc" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00049610 ! larval retinal basal glial cell
is_a: FBbt:00110171 ! embryonic/larval wrapping glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005098 ! part of peripheral nervous system
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001768 ! overlaps eye disc
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00001931 ! overlaps embryonic/larval optic stalk
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00049611 ! develops from embryonic/larval migratory optic stalk surface glial cell
