[Term]
id: FBbt:00100523
name: adult distal lamina satellite glial cell
def: "Glial cell found in the distal part of the cell body rind of the lamina. It lies in a layer beneath the pseudocartridge glial cells, and above the proximal satellite glial cells (Kremer et al., 2017). These cells are uniformly large and oblong in shape along the anterior-posterior axis (Kremer et al., 2017). They form honeycomb-like shapes that ensheath cell bodies of monopolar neurons of the lamina cortex as well as neuronal tracts (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010; Kremer et al., 2017). They lie partly on top of one another and one honeycomb may be formed by two cells. There is approximately one distal satellite glial cell for every 6 groups of monopolar neurons (Edwards et al., 2012) and around 125 of these cells per optic lobe (Edwards et al., 2012; Kremer et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210316, FlyBase:FBrf0218414, FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "adult lamina distal cortex glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "adult lamina rind satellite glial cell" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0210316]
synonym: "L-dCG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
is_a: FBbt:00005723 ! adult lamina satellite glial cell
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100518 ! develops from developing distal satellite glial cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-05-12T04:02:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100524
name: adult proximal lamina satellite glial cell
def: "Glial cell found in the proximal part of the cell body rind of the lamina. It is located in a layer between the distal satellite glial cells and the epithelial glial cells (Kremer et al., 2017). It originates from the outer optic anlage of the larva (Edwards et al., 2012). They are thin and dense, having a smaller size and more variable orientation along the anterior-posterior axis than the distal lamina satellite glia (Kremer et al., 2017). These glial cells invest the photoreceptor axon bundles and the necks of monopolar neurons (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). On their distal surface, they form pockets for the neuronal cell bodies, on their proximal surface, they send protrusions into the neuropil (Kremer et al., 2017). There is approximately one proximal satellite glial cell for every 2-3 groups of monopolar cell bodies (Edwards et al., 2012) and around 250 of these cells per optic lobe (Kremer et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210316, FlyBase:FBrf0218414, FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
comment: Sometimes referred to as interface glia (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010), as they are found at the interface between the cell body rind and the neuropil (Kremer et al., 2017). Not to be confused with interface glia found in the larval CNS.
synonym: "adult lamina interface glial cell" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0210316]
synonym: "adult lamina proximal cortex glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "L-pCG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "proximal glial cell" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00005723 ! adult lamina satellite glial cell
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00053292 ! develops from developing proximal satellite glial cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-05-12T04:07:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100525
name: adult optic chiasma glial cell
def: "Glial cell of the adult fly that is located in the optic chiasm (Tix et al., 1997). It develops from neuroblast DL1 (CP2) (Viktorin et al., 2013; Ren et al., 2018; Plazaola-Sasieta et al., 2019). Members of this group of glial cells are arranged in rows between successive dorsoventral sheets of intercrossing fibers of the outer and inner chiasmata (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010; Tix et al., 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0096428, FlyBase:FBrf0210316, FlyBase:FBrf0221770, FlyBase:FBrf0239137, FlyBase:FBrf0243725]
comment: Kremer et al. (2017) and Ren et al. (2018) expression analysis suggests that these are types of ensheathing glia, with inner tract glia being synaptic neuropil ensheathing and outer tract glia being tract neuropil ensheathing.
synonym: "adult optic chiasm glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "adult XG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
synonym: "giant glial cell" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00100504 ! adult ensheathing glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003701 ! part of adult optic lobe
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00003921 ! overlaps optic chiasma
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100609 ! develops from neuroblast CP2
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-05-23T01:49:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100526
name: adult outer optic chiasma giant glial cell
def: "Large glial cell of the outer optic chiasm of the adult optic lobe. It extends many cytoplasmic processes that enwrap fiber bundles at and near the sites of axonal intersection (Tix et al., 1997), but does not invade the neighboring synaptic neuropil (Kremer et al., 2017). There are around 50 of these per optic lobe and each envelops 8-12 fiber bundles, with multiple glial cells sharing each large strand of fibers (Kremer et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0096428, FlyBase:FBrf0234767, FlyBase:FBrf0243899]
comment: Kremer et al. (2017) expression and morphological analysis suggests that these are tract neuropil ensheathing glia - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705.
synonym: "adult outer chiasmal glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0243081]
synonym: "adult outer optic chiasm giant glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "adult outer optic chiasm large glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "adult XGO" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
is_a: FBbt:00049491 ! adult tract neuropil ensheathing glial cell
is_a: FBbt:00100525 ! adult optic chiasma glial cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00005810 ! part of first optic chiasma
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00053294 ! develops from larval outer optic chiasma giant glial cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-05-23T02:00:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100527
name: adult inner optic chiasma giant glial cell
def: "Large glial cell of the inner optic chiasm of the adult optic lobe, between the proximal medulla and lobula complex. It extends many cytoplasmic processes that enwrap fiber bundles at and near the sites of axonal intersection (Tix et al., 1997). These cells have an elongated sheet-like morphology and they send long projections into the three neighboring neuropil regions (Kremer et al., 2017). There are around 40 inner optic chiasma glial cells per optic lobe (Kremer et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0096428, FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
comment: Kremer et al. (2017) expression and morphological analysis suggests that these are synaptic neuropil ensheathing glia - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705.
synonym: "adult inner chiasmal glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0243081]
synonym: "adult inner optic chiasm giant glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "adult inner optic chiasm large glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "adult XGI" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0234767]
is_a: FBbt:00049490 ! adult synaptic neuropil ensheathing glial cell
is_a: FBbt:00100525 ! adult optic chiasma glial cell
