[Term]
id: FBbt:00100532
name: type I neuroblast
def: "Neuroblast that divides asymmetrically to regenerate itself and produce a smaller ganglion mother cell that generates two daughter neurons. Many of these neuroblasts switch to type 0 division at some point during their development, to produce daughters that develop into neurons with no further division (Baumgardt et al., 2014)." [FlyBase:FBrf0207387, FlyBase:FBrf0225698]
comment: Bayraktar et al. (2010) show that type I neuroblasts can be distinguished from type II neuroblasts as being Deadpan-, Prospero- and Asense-positive.
synonym: "type 0 neuroblast" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0225698]
is_a: FBbt:00005146 ! neuroblast
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0000137 ! expresses ase
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0004595 ! expresses pros
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0010109 ! expresses dpn
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-06-06T02:39:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100533
name: type II neuroblast
def: "Neuroblast that divides asymmetrically regenerate itself and produce a smaller intermediate neural progenitor (INP), which can produce multiple ganglion mother cells (Boone and Doe, 2008, Viktorin et al., 2011; Ren et al., 2016). Each type II neuroblast can produce multiple INPs, leading to the generation of multiple sublineages and typically more progeny than type I neuroblasts (Ren et al., 2016). It arises relatively late during embryonic development, delaminating from the dorsal cephalic neuroectoderm during stages 11-15 (Walsh and Doe, 2017). These cells and any existing INPs enter quiescence shortly before larval hatching (Walsh and Doe, 2017). There are eight type II neuroblasts per hemisphere, all belonging to the brain (Walsh and Doe, 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0204899, FlyBase:FBrf0207387, FlyBase:FBrf0209927, FlyBase:FBrf0214289, FlyBase:FBrf0214495, FlyBase:FBrf0233706, FlyBase:FBrf0237530]
comment: Bayraktar et al. (2010) show that type II neuroblasts can be distinguished from type I neuroblasts as being Deadpan-positive, but Prospero- and Asense-negative. Walsh and Doe (2017) also use pointed as a positive marker. Arise later than NBs of embryonic NB map in Urbach and Technau (2003) - FBrf0173125 (Walsh and Doe, 2017).
synonym: "TA neuroblast" EXACT []
synonym: "transiently amplifying neuroblast" EXACT []
synonym: "transit amplifying neuroblast" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00001333 ! procephalic neuroblast
