[Term]
id: FBbt:00100563 ! neuroblast BAlp1
def: "Neuroblast that generates a basoanterior secondary lineage that enters the neuropil lateral to the antennal lobe in the late larval brain (Pereanu and Hartenstein, 2006; Wong et al., 2013). Its primary lineage enters the brain at the ventromedial ventrolateral protocerebrum (Hartenstein et al., 2015). There are approximately 35 cell of this lineage in the adult, collectively innervating many brain regions (Yu et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194268, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0223298, FlyBase:FBrf0229672]
comment: Previously mapped to PSa1 based on Eckstein et al. (2020) preprint - doi:10.1101/2020.06.12.148775. This was corrected to VESa2 based on FlyBase:FBrf0260535 and personally checked by Volker Hartenstein.
