[Term]
id: FBbt:00100604 ! neuroblast DPLp2
def: "Neuroblast that forms a primary lineage with somas lateral to the larval mushroom body calyx, along with DPLp1, its tract converges onto the dorsal CP2/3 tract and enters the oblique posterior tract (Hartenstein et al., 2015). In the adult, its secondary lineage is also similar to that of DPLp1, entering the posterolateral neuropil surface at the base of the lateral horn and arborizing in the lateral horn and superior lateral protocerebrum (Wong et al., 2013). A long, medial branch follows the obP fascicle, crossing the mushroom body pedunculus and the brain midline, forming terminal arborizations along its trajectory in the posterior inferior protocerebrum of both hemispheres (Wong et al., 2013). A massive projection is directed ventrally along the vertical posterior tract into the posterior lateral protocerebrum and posterior wedge (Wong et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194268, FlyBase:FBrf0223298, FlyBase:FBrf0229672]
subset: TL_lineage_clone
