[Term]
id: FBbt:00100738
name: intermediate neuronal progenitor
def: "Progeny of a type II neuroblast that can divide asymmetrically to generate ganglion mother cells (GMCs) and maintain itself (Bayraktar et al., 2010, Viktorin et al., 2011). Each GMC cell further divides to produce a pair of neurons, glia or mixed neuronal/glial progeny (Bayraktar et al., 2010, Viktorin et al., 2011). Each progenitor produces approximately 6 GMCs (Walsh and Doe, 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0204899, FlyBase:FBrf0207387, FlyBase:FBrf0209927, FlyBase:FBrf0212061, FlyBase:FBrf0214495, FlyBase:FBrf0237530]
comment: It expresses asense and deadpan, but loses expression of pointed as it matures (Walsh and Doe, 2017).
synonym: "INP" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0212061, FlyBase:FBrf0237530]
synonym: "intermediate neural progenitor" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0212061]
synonym: "intermediate progenitor" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0212061]
synonym: "secondary neuroblast" EXACT []
synonym: "TA secondary neuroblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205129]
synonym: "TA-GMC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194268]
synonym: "transiently amplifying ganglion mother cell" EXACT []
synonym: "transiently amplifying GMC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194268]
synonym: "transit-amplifying secondary neuroblast" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205129]
is_a: FBbt:00007344 ! somatic stem cell
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100533 ! develops from type II neuroblast
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0000137 ! expresses ase
relationship: RO:0002292 http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0010109 ! expresses dpn
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-07-13T11:17:23Z" xsd:dateTime

