[Term]
id: FBbt:00110034
name: neuron of the dorsal anterior lateral group of the protocerebrum
def: "A neuron whose cell body is located in the adult dorsal anteriolateral protocerebrum (Xia et al., 2005), extending its dendrites mainly in the superior dorsofrontal protocerebrum. There are two pairs of such neuron per hemisphere, called DAL and DAL2 (Feng et al., 2021). They are involved in long-term memory processing." [FlyBase:FBrf0187341, FlyBase:FBrf0252199]
