[Term]
id: FBbt:00110052
name: obsolete larval anterior Leucokinin neuron
def: "Larval neuron that expresses Leucokinin (FBgn0028418) whose cell body is located in the lateral protocerebrum and projects towards the midline forming a loop and innervating the corpus cardiacum and the prothoracic gland within the ring gland. There are three to four neuron per hemisphere (de Haro et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0209907, FlyBase:FBrf0238083]
comment: These neurons are not labelled by a leucokinin antibody, suggesting they correspond to faint leucokinergic cells appearing during the second and third instar (de Haro et al., 2010). Obsoleting as these cells express Ion transport peptide and are the same as the ipc-1 cells (Zandawala et al., 2018).
synonym: "larval ALK neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0209907]
synonym: "larval anterior LK Leucokinin neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "larval Leucokinin LK anterior neuron" EXACT []
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2011-12-08T02:39:29Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/633" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00047844

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110053
name: larval abdominal ganglion Leucokinin neuron
def: "Larval neuron that expresses Leucokinin (FBgn0028418) whose cell body is located ventrolaterally in each neuromere of the abdominal ganglion. Each neuron produces a pair of axons, one of which projects dorsally and emerges from the ventral ganglia through an anterior segmental nerve of each hemineuromere. The other branch divides centrally into two branches: one send its neurites to the anterior ABLK and the other ventrally to the posterior ABLK. From each segmental nerve one axon emerges that synapses to the adjacent segment border muscle, close to the spiracle (Haro et al., 2010; Landgraf et al., 2003). These synapses lack the typical morphology of motor-neuron synapses (Landgraf et al., 2003) and are not glutamatergic (Haro et al., 2010). There is one pair of neurons in each of seven abdominal neuromeres (de Haro et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155902, FlyBase:FBrf0160715, FlyBase:FBrf0209907, FlyBase:FBrf0210278]
comment: The more anterior ABLK neurons are connected to the leucokinin SELK neuron of the subesophageal ganglion in the dorsal-medial tract (de Haro et al., 2010). Landgraf et al. (2003), also detected leucokinin positive terminals on A1-7 ventral longitudinal (VL) muscles. It is not clear where these neuron originate from.
subset: cur
synonym: "larval ABLK neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0209907]
synonym: "larval Leucokinin ABLK neuron of the abdominal ganglion" EXACT []
synonym: "LK-immunoreactive cell" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0155902]
is_a: FBbt:00005106 ! neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111264 ! has soma location cell body rind of larval abdominal neuromere
