[Term]
id: FBbt:00110056
name: adult subesophageal Leucokinin neuron
def: "Adult neuron that expresses Leucokinin whose cell body is located in the ventromedial subesophageal zone (de Haro et al., 2010). In the brain, it arborizes bilaterally in the gnathal ganglion and tritocerebrum (de Haro et al., 2010). It follows the cervical connective to innervate the thoracic neuromeres (de Haro et al., 2010). It also exits the central nervous system to follow the maxillary and labro-frontal nerves (de Haro et al., 2010). There are two of these neurons per organism (Cavey et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155902, FlyBase:FBrf0209907, FlyBase:FBrf0231598]
comment: de Haro et al. (2010) find 2-3 pairs with Lk-GAL4, Cavey et al. (2016) find one pair with Lk antibody.
