[Term]
id: FBbt:00110066
name: proximal medullary amacrine neuron Pm3
def: "Proximal medullary amacrine neuron that branches at the proximal surface of the medulla, with both branches forming a broad terminal arbor in medulla layer M9. The processes of different cells intermingle significantly, and the arbor density is heterogeneous. It occupies a peripheral intracolumnar position. It is GABAergic (Davis et al., 2020). There are around 35-40 of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0213020, FlyBase:FBrf0228639, FlyBase:FBrf0244935, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
