[Term]
id: FBbt:00110159
name: octopaminergic VUMa4 neuron
def: "Octopaminergic neuron of the VUMa cluster that arborizes extensively in the ventrolateral and ventromedial protocerebra (Busch et al., 2009). One branch enters and arborizes in the middle inferior medial protocerebrum, between the fan-shaped body and the pedunculus (Busch et al., 2009). It belongs to the VM I cluster (Masuzzo et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0207458, FlyBase:FBrf0243879]
comment: The neurotransmitter was assessed by immunostaining with an anti-octopamine (OA) antibody in cells labelled with tdc2-GAL4 (FBti0101786) and NP7088-GAL4 (FBti0037217) (Busch et al., 2009).
