[Term]
id: FBbt:00110178
name: embryonic posterior midline glial cell
def: "Embryonic midline glial cell found in a posterior position in the neuromere (Wheeler et al., 2006). Four of these cells are generated in the embryo, but they all die by apoptosis before they can become mature glia in the larva (Dong and Jacobs, 1997; Wheeler et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0098773, FlyBase:FBrf0195284]
