[Term]
id: FBbt:00110205
name: enteroblast
def: "Non-proliferative cell that arises from the division of an intestinal stem cell in the adult midgut and is committed to differentiate into an enterocyte (Zeng and Hou, 2015; He et al., 2018; Reiff et al., 2019)." [FlyBase:FBrf0191251, FlyBase:FBrf0227510, FlyBase:FBrf0238268, FlyBase:FBrf0243895]
comment: These cells can be identified by their expression of a Su(H)GBE reporter, indicating active Notch signaling (He et al., 2018; Reiff et al., 2019). Cells expressing this reporter do not differentiate into enteroendocrine cells under normal conditions (Zeng and Hou, 2015). They also express klumpfuss (Reiff et al., 2019).
