[Term]
id: FBbt:00110322
name: dFB neuron of the dopaminergic PPL1 cluster
def: "Adult neuron of the dopaminergic PPL1 cluster, whose main projection terminates in the dorsal fan-shaped body with a large-field arborization pattern consisting of mainly presynaptic terminals (Liu et al., 2012; Hulse et al., 2021). It receives input in the superior protocerebrum (Hulse et al., 2021). There are three of these cells per hemisphere, each arborizing in a different layer (Hulse et al., 2021). These cells promote wakefulness (Liu et al., 2012)." [FlyBase:FBrf0220041, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
comment: Ren et al. (2016) - FBrf0233706 report that two of these arise from CP2 (DM1), but do not say which layers they innervate.
synonym: "PPL1-dFB" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0220041]
is_a: FBbt:00100219 ! dopaminergic PPL1 neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0042321 ! capable of part of negative regulation of circadian sleep/wake cycle, sleep
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00049532 ! sends synaptic output to region adult dorsal fan-shaped body
relationship: RO:0013006 FBbt:00040035 ! sends synaptic output throughout fan-shaped body layer
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-04-05T04:03:58Z" xsd:dateTime

