[Term]
id: FBbt:00110327
name: EB neuron of the dopaminergic PPM3 cluster
def: "Extrinsic ring neuron that is part of the dopaminergic PPM3 cluster and innervates the bulb and the lateral surface of the lateral accessory lobe, bilaterally (Omoto et al., 2018). It projects along the lateral ellipsoid fascicle, entering the ellipsoid body at a dorsolateral position (Omoto et al., 2018). It has mainly postsynaptic terminals in the lateral accessory lobe and mixed terminals in the outer central (sparse) and outer posterior (concentrated) domains of the ellipsoid body (Omoto et al., 2018; Hulse et al., 2021). Its terminals in the bulb are mostly presynaptic (Hulse et al., 2021). There are two of these cells per hemisphere and they develop from neuroblast DM6 (Kandimalla et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0220041, FlyBase:FBrf0240929, FlyBase:FBrf0254510, FlyBase:FBrf0257023]
comment: ExR2 was not fully reconstructed by Hanesch et al. (1989), so although it is thought that they are represented by this class, it is possible that the Hanesch et al. (1989) ExR2 neurons are the Omoto et al. (2018) ExR4 neurons (Omoto et al., 2018).
subset: cur
synonym: "extrinsic ring neuron ExR2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0240929]
synonym: "PPM3-EB" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0240929]
is_a: FBbt:00003654 ! adult ellipsoid body extrinsic ring neuron
is_a: FBbt:00100218 ! dopaminergic PPM3 neuron
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00003624 ! part of adult brain
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00003667 ! fasciculates with adult lateral ellipsoid fascicle
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00050142 ! develops from neuroblast CM3
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003681 ! receives synaptic input in region adult lateral accessory lobe
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007554 ! receives synaptic input in region ellipsoid body outer posterior domain
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007556 ! receives synaptic input in region ellipsoid body outer central domain
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00003682 ! sends synaptic output to region bulb
