[Term]
id: FBbt:00110328
name: larval dopaminergic TM1-1 neuron
def: "Subtype of the dopaminergic TM1 neuron that has symmetrical arborizations in the subesophageal and thoracic ganglia. It is an unpaired neuron whose primary process splits into four secondary neurites with two of these running along the midline dorsally and the other two projecting laterally. Secondary neurites innervate the first thoracic segment and the basal subesophageal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
comment: Dopaminergic cells were identified by double labeling with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody and a TH-GAL4 driver (FBtp0020119) (Selcho et al., 2009).
synonym: "TM1-1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
is_a: FBbt:00052749 ! unpaired neuron
is_a: FBbt:00100768 ! larval dopaminergic TM1 neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-08T02:34:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110329
name: larval dopaminergic TM1-2 neuron
def: "Subtype of the dopaminergic TM1 neuron that has ipsilateral arborizations in the subesophageal ganglion and ventral nerve cord. It is a paired neuron that projects dorsally next to the midline and upon reaching the dorsal margin extends laterally sending arbors in the medial and lateromedial subesophageal ganglion, the ventromedial thoracic, anterior ventro-medial abdominal ganglion and basomedial protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
comment: Dopaminergic cells were identified by double labeling with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody and a TH-GAL4 driver (FBtp0020119) (Selcho et al., 2009).
synonym: "TM1-2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
is_a: FBbt:00100768 ! larval dopaminergic TM1 neuron
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-08T02:34:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110330
name: octopaminergic VUMd4 neuron
def: "Adult octopaminergic descending neuron of the VUMd cluster, with its soma posterior-ventral to the gnathal ganglion (Busch and Tanimoto, 2010; Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the brain, it has postsynapses and presynapses in the saddle, the gnathal ganglion and the flange, and also has postsynapses in the cantle (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the VNC, it follows the median dorsal abdominal tract (Sturner et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 1-2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0210649, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
comment: The neurotransmitter was assessed by labelling cells with tdc2-GAL4 (FBti0101786) (Busch and Tanimoto, 2010). Pre- or post-synapse locations are the fewest regions that collectively contain at least 80 percent of all pre- or post-synapses of these (DNg66) neurons in FlyWire.
synonym: "descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg66" EXACT [doi:10.1101/2025.07.31.667571]
synonym: "DNad002" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
synonym: "OA VUMd4" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210649]
is_a: FBbt:00047516 ! descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion
is_a: FBbt:00110160 ! octopaminergic VUMd neuron
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00047544 ! fasciculates with median dorsal abdominal tract
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00014013 ! receives synaptic input in region adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00045048 ! receives synaptic input in region saddle
