[Term]
id: FBbt:00110339
name: larval mushroom body dopaminergic neuron f1
def: "Larval dopaminergic neuron of the DL1 cluster that projects to the region beneath the dorsal tips (V2) of both vertical lobes (Selcho et al., 2009). It has postsynaptic sites in the anterior and posterior superior medial protocerebrum and the centroposterior lateral compartment (clamp) (Saumweber et al., 2018). It is activated downstream of mechanosensory chordotonal neurons and class IV multidendritic neurons and it receives direct input from FBNs, FFNs, FB2N-12 and FB2N-18 (Eschbach et al., 2020). It develops from the CP3 (DL2) neuroblast and develops into an adult PPL1 SMP neuron during metamorphosis (Saumweber et al., 2018; Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208252, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0245294, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
