[Term]
id: FBbt:00110342
name: larval mushroom body dopaminergic neuron c1
def: "Larval dopaminergic neuron of the DL1 cluster that projects to both spurs and to the anterior parts of the pedunculi of the mushroom bodies (Selcho et al., 2009). In contrast to the other DL1 subtypes, the neurite which innervates the dorsomedial protocerebrum bifurcates laterally to the vertical lobe with an axon innervating this lobe. It has postsynapses in the anterior and posterior superior medial protocerebrum (dorsoanterior and dorsoposterior compartments). It receives input from FBNs, FFN-2, and FFN-15 (Eschbach et al., 2020). It develops from the CP3 (DL2) neuroblast and becomes a PPL101 (MB-MP1) neuron during metamorphosis (Saumweber et al., 2018; Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208252, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0245294, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
