id: FBbt:00110347
name: larval dopaminergic DL2b neuron
def: "Larval dopaminergic DL2 neuron of the larval brain with a contralateral projection (Selcho et al., 2009; Blanco et al., 2011). It is a primary neuron of a BLVa primary lineage (Hartenstein et al., 2017). The primary neurite turns in the basolateral protocerebrum towards the midline and bifurcates before reaching the esophagus (Selcho et al., 2009). It then innervates the basal protocerebrum on both sides of the brain and extends to innervate the ipsilateral posterior subesophageal ganglion (Selcho et al., 2009). A secondary neurite extends contralaterally via the dorsoposterior commissure (Selcho et al., 2009). There are also arborizations in the dorsal parts of the basolateral protocerebrum and terminals surrounding the contralateral pedunculus of the mushroom body (Selcho et al., 2009). There are 2 neurons in this cluster (Blanco et al., 2011). It persists into adulthood to become a PPL2c neuron (Hartenstein et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0208252, FlyBase:FBrf0216686, FlyBase:FBrf0234128]
comment: Dopaminergic cells were identified by double labeling with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody and a TH-GAL4 driver (FBtp0020119) (Selcho et al., 2009) and with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody (Blanco et al., 2011).
synonym: "DL2-3 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
synonym: "DL2b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216686]
synonym: "larval dopaminergic DL2-3 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
is_a: FBbt:00052517 ! primary interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00110344 ! larval dopaminergic DL2 neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100750 ! develops from neuroblast BLV
relationship: RO:0002203 FBbt:00100221 ! develops into dopaminergic PPL2c neuron
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00100138 ! has synaptic IO in region larval gnathal ganglion
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-08T02:34:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110348
name: larval dopaminergic SM1 neuron
def: "Dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in the larval anteromedial subesophageal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0108241, FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
comment: Dopaminergic cells were identified by double labeling with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody and a TH-GAL4 driver (FBtp0020119). Four cells were labelled with TH-GAL4 (FBtp0020119) but only one of these was positive for the TH-antibody (Selcho et al., 2009).
synonym: "SbU" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0108241]
synonym: "SM1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
