[Term]
id: FBbt:00110359 ! neuroblast LHa4
def: "Neuroblast that produces a secondary lineage of approximately 50 cells, with anterior somas, that innervate the lateral horn and superior lateral protocerebrum (Ito et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
comment: Suggested to be equivalent to neuroblast BLVa2 in Hartenstein et al. (2017) - FBrf0234128, but BLVa2 mapped to LHa3 in Bates et al. (2020) - FBrf0246460 and Eckstein et al. (2024) - FBrf0259490 and Schlegel et al. (2024) - FlyBase:FBrf0260535. Schlegel et al. (2024) suggest that the LHa4 clone might be LHa2 with shifted cell bodies (can happen for lateral lineages).
