comment: Ito et al. (2013) only found two-cell clones of this lineage and note the possibility that these are first born neurons of another lineage (most likely SMPad2), so the 'SMPad4' neuroblast may not exist. This possibility is also noted in Schlegel et al. (2024) - FlyBase:FBrf0260535.
is_a: FBbt:00001334 ! protocerebral neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00100532 ! type I neuroblast
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T02:17:43Z" xsd:dateTime

