[Term]
id: FBbt:00110418
name: obsolete adult fruitless aDT-c lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult brain that expresses fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the anterior protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
comment: These clones were obtained by MARCM using a fru-GAL4 driver (FBal0276838), with clones induced at the first instar larval stage (Cachero et al., 2010). Obsoleted as this clone only contains one neuron, so is redundant with the respective neuron term.
