[Term]
id: FBbt:00110419
name: adult fruitless aDT-c neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its soma in the anterior brain, near the antennal lobe (Kimura et al., 2008; Cachero et al., 2010). It arborizes in the ipsilateral lateral accessory lobe and superior protocerebrum and a branch crosses the midline to form an arbor in the contralateral protocerebrum (Cachero et al., 2010). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Kimura et al., 2008; Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
comment: Arbor locations determined by visualization of Cachero et al. (2010) clone in Virtual Fly Brain.
synonym: "aDT-c neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "AL2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "fru-AL neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00003681 ! has synaptic IO in region adult lateral accessory lobe
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00007145 ! has synaptic IO in region adult protocerebrum
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110420
name: obsolete adult fruitless aDT-d (female) lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult female brain that expresses fruitless, whose cell bodies are located junction of the ventrolateral protocerebrum and the antennal lobe. A neurite projects medially and forms two arbors: a dendritic arbor in the lateral junction and an axonal arbor in the anterior medial protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
