[Term]
id: FBbt:00110461
name: adult fruitless aSP-g (female) neuron
def: "Adult fruitless aSP-g neuron of the female. It has sex-specific arborization in a female-enlarged region of the superior protocerebrum (Cachero et al., 2010; Kohl et al., 2013). It receives input in the lateral horn and integrates sensory information of multiple modalities, including taste and smell (Taisz et al., 2023). It also has arborization outside of the lateral horn and an axon that crosses the midline (Taisz et al., 2023). There are approximately 11 of these cells per hemisphere and they can be divided into three morphological subtypes (Taisz et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438, FlyBase:FBrf0223724, FlyBase:FBrf0256726]
synonym: "adult female fruitless aSP6 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female aSP-g neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female aSP3b2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female fru-aSP3 neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0007608 ! capable of part of sensory perception of smell
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0050909 ! capable of part of sensory perception of taste
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00045030 ! has synaptic IO in region superior neuropils
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007053 ! receives synaptic input in region adult lateral horn
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime

