[Term]
id: FBbt:00110469
name: adult fruitless aSP-k (female) neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron of the female with its cell body lateral to the lateral horn, dendritic arborization in the lateral horn and axonal projections to the lateral protocerebral complex (Yu et al., 2010). It receives input in the wedge and outputs onto and inhibits the female doublesex pMN2 (vpoDN) neuron (Wang et al., 2021). Most of its synaptic terminals are in the anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (Yu et al., 2010; Baker et al., 2022). A projection also extends across the midline (Yu et al., 2010; Baker et al., 2022). It preferentially responds to male sine song, rather than pulse song (Baker et al., 2022). There are approximately 20 of these cells per hemisphere (Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221438, FlyBase:FBrf0247919, FlyBase:FBrf0254226]
comment: Wang et al. (2020) - FBrf0247919 states that aSP-k neurons are probably a subset of vpoIN. Based on Hemibrain data, all these (aSP8) cells cross the midline, so probably correspond to the 'commissural' subset of vpoIN neurons, AVLP_pr02, in Baker et al. (2022) - FBrf0254226.
synonym: "adult female fruitless aSP8 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "AVLP_pr02" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0254226]
synonym: "female aSP-k neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female aSP3c neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female fru-aSP3 neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female LC1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0212443]
is_a: FBbt:00049948 ! vaginal plate opening inhibitory neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 ! capable of gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0007605 ! capable of part of sensory perception of sound
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00040043 ! has synaptic IO in region anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00045027 ! receives synaptic input in region wedge
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110470
name: obsolete adult fruitless aSP-l lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult brain that expresses fruitless, all of which develop from neuroblast SLPav2. Its cell bodies are located in the lateral cell body region. A neurite makes a distinct turn, travels on the surface of the neuropil around the lateral horn to the posterior superior lateral protocerebrum to form broad superficial web-like arborizations in the superior medial and intermediate protocerebrum. A neurite also crosses the midline and arborizes in a small region at the medial end of the contralateral superior medial and intermediate protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "aSP-l clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "aSP7 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "fru-aSP3 clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
