[Term]
id: FBbt:00110471
name: adult fruitless aSP-l neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron that develops from neuroblast SLPav2 (Ito et al., 2013; Yu et al., 2013). It has its cell body located anteroventral to the lateral horn, almost on the surface of the ventrolateral protocerebrum (Yu et al., 2010). The neurite makes a distinct turn, travels on the surface of the neuropil around the lateral horn to the posterior superior lateral protocerebrum to form broad superficial web-like arborizations in the posterior superior medial protocerebrum (PSMP) (Yu et al., 2010). It also crosses the midline and arborizes in a small region at the medial end of the contralateral PSMP (Yu et al,. 2010). There are approximately 24 of these cells per hemisphere (Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
synonym: "adult fruitless aSP3 neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "adult fruitless aSP7 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00040063 ! has synaptic IO in region posterior superior medial protocerebrum
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime

