[Term]
id: FBbt:00110483
name: adult fruitless pIP-c neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its soma in the posterior inferior protocerebrum (Cachero et al., 2010). It develops from neuroblast BLP2 (VLPp1) (Ito et al., 2013; Yu et al., 2013). These neurons show no gross sexual dimorphism (Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
comment: Cachero et al. (2010) say that pIP3 and pIP7 from Yu et al. (2010) are morphologically distinct subtypes of pIP-c.
synonym: "pIP-c neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
