[Term]
id: FBbt:00110487
name: adult fruitless pIP-e (female) neuron
def: "Adult female fruitless neuron that develops from neuroblast DL1 (CP2) (Ren et al., 2016) and has its cell body in the posterior inferior protocerebrum (Cachero et al., 2010). There are approximately 20 of these cells per hemisphere (Ren et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221438, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: pC2 has been listed as an exact synonym for this in the past, but pC2 is actually a partially overlapping class of doublesex-expressing neurons (Rideout et al., 2010 - FBrf0210397), which now has its own class - FBbt:00047350. Cachero et al. (2010) report 34 cells per hemisphere. Cachero et al. (2010) list pIP-e as corresponding to the Yu et al. (2010) pIP5/6 and aIP-g also corresponding to pIP6.
synonym: "adult female fruitless P4a neuron" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "adult female fruitless P4b neuron" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "adult female fruitless pIP5 neuron" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "adult female fruitless pIP6 neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female fru-P neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "female pC2 neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0159058, FlyBase:FBrf0210397]
synonym: "female pIP-e neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
