[Term]
id: FBbt:00110492
name: obsolete adult fruitless pIP-h (female) lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult female brain that expresses fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the posterior inferior protocerebrum. The cell bodies are located medial to pIP-a neurons. Neurites enter the neuropil through the same tract opening as pIP-a and branches. One branch travels dorsoanteriorly, towards the medial ring. Another projects to the ventromedial region of the contralateral ring. The third branch crosses the midline above the esophageal foramen and travels ventrally and exits the brain to terminate in the ventral nerve cord." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: These clones were obtained by MARCM using a fru-GAL4 driver (FBal0276838), with clones induced at the first instar larval stage (Cachero et al., 2010). There is only one cell in this clone and it is part of the pMP-f clone (Ren et al., 2016). Obsoleted as this clone only contains one neuron, so is redundant with the respective neuron term.
synonym: "female fru-P clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "female P2a clone" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0205974]
synonym: "female P2c clone" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0205974]
synonym: "female pIP-h clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female pIP9 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00110493

