[Term]
id: FBbt:00110506
name: obsolete adult fruitless pMP-e (female) lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult female brain that expresses fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the posterior medial protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead. Ren et al. (2016) identify the DM4-derived female equivalent of the male pMP-e (P1) neurons and note that the female pMP-e clone in Cachero et al. (2010) may be a misidentified unrelated clone. Unlike in the male, there does not appear to be overlap between dsx pC1 and fru pMP-e in the female (Ren et al., 2016).
synonym: "female fru-P clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "female pMP-e clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "female pMP4 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
