def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its soma in the posterior superior protocerebrum (Cachero et al., 2010). There are approximately two of these cells per hemisphere (Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "pSP-f neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-05-23T03:45:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110536
name: obsolete adult fruitless aDT1 lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult brain that expresses fruitless, whose cell bodies are located dorsomedial to the antennal lobe. Neurites project bilaterally terminating with granular arborizations in the medial subesophageal zone and in the ipsilateral dorsal medial protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
