[Term]
id: FBbt:00110557
name: adult fruitless pIP4 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body in the lateral posterior brain (Yu et al., 2010). It enters the neuropil through a tract opening below that of plP6 (pIP-e) (Yu et a., 2010). Within the neuropil, the neurite travels medially to towards the medial ring of the lateral protocerebral complex (Yu et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
