[Term]
id: FBbt:00110594
name: obsolete adult fruitless aSP-a (male) lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult male brain that expresses fruitless, all of which develop from neuroblast SMPad1. Its cell bodies located are located in the pars intercerebralis. Projections extend laterally away from the pars intercerebralis and then ventrally to the lateral junction. The extensive arbors span the arch, lateral junction and the medial ring. The axonal arbors are likely to be enriched in the lateral junction. Females have less extensive arbors compared with males." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "male aSP-a clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male aSP2 clone" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "male fru-aSP2 clone" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-07-25T19:28:10Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
consider: FBbt:00110595

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110595
name: adult fruitless aSP-a (male) neuron
def: "Adult male fruitless-expressing neuron that develops from the SMPad1 neuroblast (Ito et al., 2013; Yu et al., 2013). It has its soma in the pars intercerebralis and projects laterally, arborizing extensively in the lateral protocerebral complex (Yu et al., 2010). Many of these cells are activated by the presence of females, but not males (Takayanagi-Kiya and Kiya, 2019). There are approximately 50-60 of these cells per hemisphere (Lee et al., 2000; Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438, FlyBase:FBrf0241873]
synonym: "adult male fru-aSP2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "adult male fruitless aSP2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male aSP-a neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-07-25T19:28:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110596
name: obsolete adult fruitless aSP-b (male) lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult male brain that expresses fruitless, all of which develop from neuroblast SMPad2. Its cell bodies are located in the dorsal pars intercerebralis. Neurites project ventroposteriorly and then bifurcate. One branch projects ipsilaterally and terminates in the medial protocerebrum. The other branch projects ventromedially, turns dorsally at the midline and then joins the path of the same cluster on the contralateral side possibly arborizing in the contralateral hemisphere. The dendritic arbors are likely to be located in the lateral junction while the axonal arbors are in the ventral medial protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "male aSP-b clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male aSP1 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "male fru-aSP1 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-07-25T19:28:10Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
consider: FBbt:00110597

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110597
name: adult fruitless aSP-b (male) neuron
def: "Adult male fruitless neuron that develops from neuroblast SMPad2 (Ito et al., 2013; Yu et al., 2013). There are approximately 15 of these cells per hemisphere, with their somas in the pars intercerebralis (Lee et al., 2000; Cachero et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0221412, FlyBase:FBrf0221438]
comment: Correspondence of Yu et al. (2010) - FBrf0211884 aSP1 to aSP1 in other studies is unclear - they also seem to call this aSP2-p in fig S2 and give contradictory correspondences in table S1. and Cachero et al. (2010) list Yu et al. (2010) aSP1 as possibly corresponding to aSP-b and aSP-c.
synonym: "adult male fruitless aSP1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male aSP-b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male fru-aSP1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
