[Term]
id: FBbt:00110608
name: obsolete adult fruitless pIP-a (male) lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult male brain that expresses fruitless, all of which develop from neuroblast PSp3. Its cell bodies are located laterally in a cluster close to the tract entrance below the protocerebral bridge. A neurite projects anteriorly before branching. The dorsal branch leads to dense arborizations in the ventral and medial ipsilateral ring. The dorsal projection travels lateroventrally forming dense arborizations in multiple regions including the lateral accessory lobe, posterior antennal mechanosensory motor center and subesophageal zone before exiting the brain. In the ventral nerve cord, the projections travel along a lateral tract and arborize mostly in the meso- and metathoracic neuromeres." [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "male fru-P clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "male P2b clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974]
synonym: "male pIP-a clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male pIP1 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2013-07-25T20:29:41Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
consider: FBbt:00110609

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110609
name: adult fruitless pIP-a (male) neuron
def: "Adult male fruitless neuron that develops from neuroblast DL2 (CP3) (Ren et al., 2016) and has its cell body in the posterior inferior protocerebrum (Yu et al., 2010). In the brain, it has arbors in the lateral protocerebral complex (Yu et al., 2010). It descends to the ventral nerve cord, where it has presynaptic terminals in all three thoracic neuromeres (Cachero et al., 2010; Yu et al., 2010). There are approximately 22 of these cells per hemisphere (Ren et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926, FlyBase:FBrf0233706]
comment: Cachero et al. (2010) report 14 cells per hemisphere.
synonym: "adult male fruitless pIP1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male fru-P neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "male P2b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974]
synonym: "male pIP-a neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
