[Term]
id: FBbt:00110642
name: obsolete fan-shaped body slice 1
def: "Medial-most slice in each hemisphere of the fan-shaped body." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0205148, FlyBase:FBrf0213955, FlyBase:FBrf0221742, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
comment: Obsoleted as the number of columns is variable for different cell types (Hulse et al., 2021 - FBrf0254510) and the most common number is nine, rather than eight or 16 (Wolff et al., 2015 - FBrf0227801; Boyan et al., 2017 - FBrf0236238; Hulse et al., 2021 - FBrf0254510). Each of the two neighboring slices (1-2, 3-4, 5-6, 7-8) are associated more closely because they receive small-field columnar neurons generated by the same neuroblasts, forming four groups on each side of the midline, from lateral to medial: segment pair W, X, Y and Z, respectively (Boyan and Williams et al., 2011; Ito and Awasaki, 2008). Lin et al. (2013) names these four groups from 1 to 4, from medial to lateral.
synonym: "column 1 of fan-shaped body" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
