[Term]
id: FBbt:00110666
name: obsolete antennal basiconic sensillum ab11
def: "Olfactory basiconic sensillum, located on the lateral surface of the antenna, that houses the dendrites of three olfactory receptor neurons (Kwon et al., 2010). It responds strongly to citronellal, dependent on TRPA1 expression in one of the sensory neurons (Kwon et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211878]
comment: Obsoleted as this was not molecularly-defined and likely represents a variant of another basiconic sensillum type (Benton et al., 2025).
