[Term]
id: FBbt:00110854
name: adult fruitless pIP10 (male) neuron
def: "Male-specific fruitless neuron with its soma in the medial posterior brain (von Phillipsborn et al., 2011). It extends neurites bilaterally innervating the periesophageal region and the lateral protocerebrum; one long process descends to the ventral nerve cord, where it extensively innervates the wing neuropil (von Phillipsborn et al., 2011). There is one of these cells per hemisphere and it is cholinergic (Lillvis et al., 2024). It is involved in pulse and sine song generation (von Phillipsborn et al., 2011; O'Sullivan et al., 2018; Lillvis et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0212984, FlyBase:FBrf0240039, FlyBase:FBrf0258823]
synonym: "adult fruitless pIP10 neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "pIP10 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0212984]
