[Term]
id: FBbt:00110856
name: adult fruitless dPR1 neuron
def: "Male-specific fruitless neuron with its soma in the anterior prothoracic neuromere (von Philipsborn et al., 2011). It innervates the wing neuropil bilaterally (von Philipsborn et al., 2011). It plays a role in male pulse song (von Philipsborn et al., 2011; Lillvis et al., 2024). There is one of these cells per hemisphere and it also expresses doublesex (von Philipsborn et al., 2011; Lillvis et al., 2024). It is cholinergic (Lillvis et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0212984, FlyBase:FBrf0258823]
comment: Might be a subtype of TN2 dsx neuron (von Philipsborn et al., 2011).
