[Term]
id: FBbt:00110860
name: adult fruitless vPR6 (male) neuron
def: "Adult male fruitless neuron that is derived from hemilineage 12A and has a ventrolateral cell body, between the first and second thoracic neuromeres (Yu et al., 2010; Shirangi et al., 2016). It has bilateral arborization in the dorsal mesothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010; Shirangi et al., 2016). It plays a role in male courtship song (Shirangi et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0232698]
comment: Yu et al. (2010) map this to Cachero et al. (2010) vPR-k, which is not dimorphic and has additional arborization in the prothoracic neuromere.
synonym: "adult male fruitless vPR-k neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
