[Term]
id: FBbt:00110927
name: larval dopaminergic DM1a neuron
def: "Larval dopaminergic neuron of the DM1 cluster that develops from neuroblast DPMm1 (Hartenstein et al., 2017). Its soma and ventrally-directed projection is found medial to DM1b (Blanco et al., 2011; Hartenstein et al., 2017). It follows the medial cervical connective and terminates in the tritocerebrum and gnathal neuromeres (Hartenstein et al., 2017). There are one or two of these neurons per hemisphere (Blanco et al., 2011; Hartenstein et al., 2017)." [FlyBase:FBrf0216686, FlyBase:FBrf0234128]
comment: Dopaminergic cells were identified by labeling with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody (Blanco et al., 2011).
synonym: "DM1a neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216686]
