[Term]
id: FBbt:00110976
name: obsolete serotonergic abdominal medial neuron
def: "Serotonergic neuron whose cell body is located medially in one of two clusters either side of the ventral midline in the larval abdominal segments A1 to A7 or adult abdominal neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0048551, FlyBase:FBrf0207378]
comment: Cited references do not describe adult abdominal neurons. The pattern of cell body pairs seems to belong to the larva, making this synonymous with FBbt:00001583 (which has associated records, this does not as at 26-Jun-18). Adult pattern is somewhat irregular, making this classification irrelevant (Sykes et al., 2004 - FBrf0180031) - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705.
