[Term]
id: FBbt:00110985
name: adult feeding interneuron
def: "Adult subesophageal zone intrinsic neuron whose soma is located in the lateral gnathal ganglion (Flood et al., 2013). The primary neurite extends ventromedially into the gnathal ganglion and splits into several dendritic branches that form a dense network of arborization medial to the axonal arbors (Flood et al., 2013). This arborization is predominantly ipsilateral, but dendrites may spread into the contralateral hemisphere (Flood et al., 2013). It is involved in inducing the proboscis extension reflex and might also be involved in regulating consumption (Flood et al., 2013; Pool et al., 2014; Shiu et al., 2022). There is one of these neurons in each hemisphere (Flood et al., 2013). It is predicted to be cholinergic (Shiu et al., 2022). It is predicted to be a primary neuron (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0222061, FlyBase:FBrf0225542, FlyBase:FBrf0251280, FlyBase:FBrf0254006, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0260565]
comment: Neurotransmitter prediction based on machine learning classification (Shiu et al., 2022). Mapped to FlyWire CB0038 in Shiu et al. (2024) supplement.
subset: cur
synonym: "adult CB0038 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260565]
synonym: "CB0038" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260565]
synonym: "Fdg interneuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222061]
synonym: "FDG neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0225542]
synonym: "feeding command neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0225542]
is_a: FBbt:00047097 ! primary neuron
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00100210 ! has soma location cell body rind of adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0014055 ! capable of acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0007637 ! capable of part of proboscis extension reflex
relationship: RO:0002216 GO:0008343 ! capable of part of adult feeding behavior
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00014013 ! receives synaptic input in region adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00014013 ! sends synaptic output to region adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013010 FBbt:00014013 ! synapses restricted to region adult gnathal ganglion
