[Term]
id: FBbt:00111056
name: adult intrinsic protocerebral bridge 4 glomeruli neuron
def: "Large field neuron of the central complex that is intrinsic to the protocerebral bridge. It has ipsilateral dendritic arbors in the four lateralmost glomeruli (6 to 9) and axon terminals in glomerulus 9 (Wolff et al., 2015; Hulse et al., 2021). It develops from neuroblast PBp1 (Kandimalla et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221742, FlyBase:FBrf0227801, FlyBase:FBrf0257023]
comment: This neuron type was initially identified as synapsing in 6 glomeruli (Lin et al., 2013). Arborizations were later redescribed by Wolff et al. (2015) (4 glomeruli) and Hulse et al. (2021) (4 + small amount in G5).
synonym: "P6-8-P9" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0240744]
synonym: "PB6-glomeruli neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "PBG6-8.sG9.b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227801]
synonym: "PBL3-8 glomeruli neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "PBL7,L8 neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "PBR3-8 glomeruli neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "PBR7,R8 neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "protocerebral bridge 6 glomeruli neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
is_a: FBbt:00003666 ! adult intrinsic protocerebral bridge neuron
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00050169 ! develops from neuroblast CM6
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003674 ! receives synaptic input in region protocerebral bridge glomerulus 6
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00003675 ! receives synaptic input in region protocerebral bridge glomerulus 7
