[Term]
id: FBbt:00111095
name: adult fruitless dMS2 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body in the dorsal mesothoracic neuromere (Yu et a., 2010). It enters the neuropil in the dorsal anterior mesothoracic neuromere, then projects ventromedially and turns back dorsally (Yu et al., 2010). Dendritic arbors are found dorsally while the axonal arbors are found ventrally (Yu et al., 2010). It is cholinergic (Lillvis et al., 2024). There are approximately 18 of these cells per organism (Lillvis et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0258823]
comment: Mainly studies in males - unclear whether sexually dimorphic.
synonym: "fru-PrMs neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00110175 ! receives synaptic input in region adult mesothoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00110175 ! sends synaptic output to region adult mesothoracic neuromere
