[Term]
id: FBbt:00111100
name: obsolete adult fruitless dMS5 lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult female that express fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the dorsal region between the mesothoracic and metathoracic segments, very close to those of the dMS4 lineage clone. Arborization is confined in the mesothoracic neuromere. This clone is not found in males." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: These clones were obtained by FLP recombinase, combining a fru[FLP] allele (FBal0248671) and several GAL4 drivers whose expression includes subsets of fruitless neurons (Yu et al., 2010). Obsoleted as this clone only contains one neuron, so is redundant with the respective neuron term.
synonym: "dMS5 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "fru-MsMt clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00111101

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111101
name: adult fruitless dMS5 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body located at the junction between the dorsal mesothoracic and metathoracic neuromeres, very close dMS4 (Yu et al., 2010). It projects medially towards the midline and turns anteriorly (Yu et al., 2010). Arborization is found in the mesothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010). There is one of these cells per hemisphere and it is cholinergic (Lillvis et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0258823]
comment: No male examples found by Yu et al. (2010). Found in the male by Lillvis et al. (2024).
synonym: "fru-MsMt neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
