id: FBbt:00111112
name: obsolete adult fruitless vMS2 lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult that express fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the ventroanterior region of the mesothoracic segment. Its neurite projects dorsally forming thick arbors in the dorsal mesothoracic neuromere. One branch exits the VNC via the anterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve to innervate direct and indirect flight muscles (basalar muscles and coxal tergal remotor muscles, respectively)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "fru-PrMs clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "vMS2 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
consider: FBbt:00111113

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111113
name: adult fruitless vMS2 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with a large cell body in the ventral region of the anterior mesothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010). It projects dorsally forming thick arbors in the dorsal mesothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010). One branch exits the ventral nerve cord via the anterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve to innervate a flight muscle (Yu et al., 2010). Muscles innervated by these neurons include a tergal remotor of coxa indirect flight muscle and the basilar direct flight muscles (Yu et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "fru-PrMs neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00004060 ! fasciculates with adult anterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve
relationship: RO:0013009 FBbt:00003360 ! sends synaptic output to cell flight muscle cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111114
name: obsolete adult fruitless vMS3 lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult that express fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the anteriolateral region of the mesothoracic segment. Neurites project medially and slightly posteriorly, bifurcating into an ipsilateral and a contralateral branches that run along close to the midline. Both branches terminate in the prothoracic neuromere possibly connecting to the foreleg afferents. The contralateral branch then exits the ventral nerve cord." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "dMs-b clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "fru-PrMs clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "vMS3 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
consider: FBbt:00111115

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111115
name: adult fruitless vMS3 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body located in the lateral region of the anterior mesothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010). It projects medially and bifurcates into an ipsilateral and a contralateral branch that run anteriorly close to the midline, with synapses in the prothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010). The contralateral branch exits the VNC (Yu et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Unclear whether contralateral branch is ascending or peripheral.
synonym: "adult fruitless dMs-b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "fru-PrMs neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00110174 ! has synaptic IO in region adult prothoracic neuromere
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111116
name: obsolete adult fruitless vMS4 lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult that express fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the ventroanterior region of the mesothoracic segment, adjacent to the vMS2 lineage clone. A neurite projects medially and branches. The ipsilateral branch projects anteriorly to the prothoracic neuromere to arborize in the anterior region. The other branch crosses the midline and forms a contralateral arbor in the prothoracic neuromere before projecting to the metathoracic neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "fru-PrMs clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
synonym: "vMs-e clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "vMS4 clone" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1712" xsd:anyURI
is_obsolete: true
consider: FBbt:00111117

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111117
name: adult fruitless vMS4 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body located in the ventral anterior mesothoracic neuromere, adjacent to the vMS2 neurons (Yu et al., 2010). It projects medially and branches, with ipsilateral and contralateral branches that both arborize in the prothoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010). The contralateral branch additionally projects posteriorly to the metathoracic neuromere (Yu et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "adult fruitless vMs-e neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211884, FlyBase:FBrf0211926]
synonym: "fru-PrMs neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002131 FBbt:00110176 ! overlaps adult metathoracic neuromere
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00110174 ! has synaptic IO in region adult prothoracic neuromere
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-08-05T17:26:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111118
name: obsolete adult fruitless vMS5 lineage clone
def: "A clone of neurons in the adult that express fruitless, whose cell bodies are located in the ventromedial region of the anterior mesothoracic segment. The ipsilateral branch projects anteriorly and terminates in the prothoracic neuromere. The other branch crosses the midline and projects posteriorly. The arborization is similar to that of the vMS4 lineage clone." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Obsoleted as we do not maintain terms for groups of cells. Consider using the appropriate neuron term instead.
synonym: "fru-PrMs clone" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
