[Term]
id: FBbt:00111194
name: adult fruitless aSP10 neuron
def: "Adult fruitless neuron with its cell body located dorsolateral to the ventrolateral protocerebrum (VLP) (Yu et al., 2010). Its neurite enters a tract below the anterior optic tubercle and branches, with one branch arborizing in the ipsilateral VLP and the other continuing medially and crossing the midline (Yu et al., 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
comment: Yu et al. (2010) map this to Kimura et al. (2008) - FBrf0205974 AL5b and Cachero et al. (2010) - FBrf0211926 aIP-c. aIP-c seems to correspond to two clusters - mapped to AL5b and AL6b by Cachero et al. (2010). Therefore, aSP10/AL5b, is probably a subtype of aIP-c.
synonym: "adult fruitless AL5b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205974, FlyBase:FBrf0211884]
synonym: "fru-AL neuron" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0128543]
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
