[Term]
id: FBbt:00111210
name: adult olfactory receptor neuron Ir64a DC4
def: "Adult olfactory receptor neuron Ir64a that innervates the antennal lobe DC4 glomerulus, bilaterally (Ai et al., 2010; Silbering et al., 2011). Its dendrite transduces signals from a grooved sensillum of the ventral compartment of chamber III of sacculus (Shanbhag et al., 1995). It responds to acid (H+ ions) and carbon dioxide (Ai et al., 2010). There are around 10 of these cells on each side (Benton et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361, FlyBase:FBrf0212455, FlyBase:FBrf0215822, FlyBase:FBrf0222046, FlyBase:FBrf0262710]
synonym: "ionotropic receptor neuron DC4" EXACT []
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-09-16T12:25:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111211
name: adult antennal lobe projection neuron DC4 adPN
def: "Adult uniglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron from the ad neuroblast (ALad1) lineage whose dendrites mainly innervate antennal lobe glomerulus DC4 (Ai et al., 2013; Bates et al., 2020). It follows the medial antennal lobe tract to innervate the mushroom body and lateral horn (Ai et al., 2013). Its axon bifurcates to form stereotypical dorsal and ventral branches in the anterior medial region of the lateral horn (Ai et al., 2013). There is around one of these per hemisphere, it fasciculates with the medial antennal lobe tract and it is cholinergic (Bates et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0222046, FlyBase:FBrf0246460]
comment: Ai et al. (2013) found 2-3 of these cells, but only one in Bates et al. (2020). One of these is embryonic-born according to Schlegel et al. (2021) Fig 6 S1, but 2 listed in supplement 5 csv.
synonym: "DC4 adPN" EXACT []
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00007053 ! sends synaptic output to region adult lateral horn
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00007385 ! sends synaptic output to region calyx of adult mushroom body
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2015-09-16T12:25:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111212
name: adult olfactory receptor neuron Ir64a DP1m
def: "Adult olfactory receptor neuron Ir64a that innervates the antennal lobe DP1m glomerulus, bilaterally (Ai et al., 2010; Silbering et al., 2011). Its dendrite transduces signals from a grooved sensillum of the dorsal compartment of chamber III of sacculus (Shanbhag et al., 1995). It responds to various olfactory cues associated with alcoholic fermentation (Benton et al., 2025). There are around 15 of these cells on each side (Benton et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361, FlyBase:FBrf0212455, FlyBase:FBrf0215822, FlyBase:FBrf0222046, FlyBase:FBrf0262710]
