id: FBbt:00111241
name: larval subesophageal zone descending SEZ DN neuron
def: "Larval neuron with its soma is located at the level of the subesophageal zone (Ohyama ey al., 2015). Its dendrites are located medially in both hemispheres in the subesophageal zone (Ohyama ey al., 2015). Its axon extends posteriorly, close to the midline (Ohyama ey al., 2015). It receives input from and outputs onto A00c and Basin neurons in multiple neuromeres (Ohyama ey al., 2015). There is one of these cells on each side (Ohyama ey al., 2015)." [FlyBase:FBrf0228257]
