[Term]
id: FBbt:00111282
name: proximal medullary amacrine neuron Pm4
def: "Proximal medullary amacrine neuron that branches at the proximal surface of the medulla. It covers around 10-20 columns with its pre- and post-synapses mostly in layers M8-M9 (Nern et al., 2025). It occupies a central intracolumnar position. It is GABAergic (Davis et al., 2020). There are around 75-85 of these neurons per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0228639, FlyBase:FBrf0244935, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
