[Term]
id: FBbt:00111404
name: protocerebral bridge 1 glomerulus-fan-shaped body-nodulus 3 posterior domain neuron
def: "Small field neuron of the central complex with dendritic arbors in a single glomerulus of the protocerebral bridge, presynaptic terminals in a tooth of fan-shaped body layer 1 and mixed or presynaptic terminals in the posterior domain of contralateral nodulus 3 (Wolff et al., 2015; Hulse et al., 2021). These cells collectively target protocerebral bridge glomeruli 2-9 (Wolff et al., 2015; Hulse et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221742, FlyBase:FBrf0227801, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
comment: Hulse et al. (2021) divide PFNp into five (a-e) subtypes, but it is not clear how these are different from each other or which cells correspond to the type in Wolff et al. (2015).
subset: cur
