[Term]
id: FBbt:00111425
name: protocerebral bridge glomerulus 1-fan-shaped body-round body type a neuron
def: "Adult protocerebral bridge 1 glomerulus-fan-shaped body-round body type a neuron (PFR_a) that targets protocerebral bridge glomerulus 1. It has the lateralmost arbor in the fan-shaped body (FB) relative to other PFR_a neurons, but this projection is ipsilateral relative to the protocerebral bridge (PB) arbor, breaking the pattern formed by the other PFR_a neurons (Wolff et al., 2015; Hulse et al., 2021). It targets the round body in the same hemisphere as its PB and FB arbors, though this may be the opposite hemisphere to its cell body position (Wolff et al., 2015; Hulse et al., 2021)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221742, FlyBase:FBrf0227801, FlyBase:FBrf0254510]
comment: PB glomerulus 1 neuron described by Lin et al. (2013) includes both the glomerulus 1 and 2 neurons from Wolff et al. (2015) and later, due to identification of an additional medial PB glomerulus (checked by comparing wiring diagrams). This term refers to the glomerulus 1 neuron of Wolff et al. (2015).
subset: cur
synonym: "PB slice 1-FB layers 3-5-IDFP RB neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "PBR1-FBR4c,d>IDFPR-RB" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
synonym: "PRL1-FBL4c,d>IDFPL-RB" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0221742]
intersection_of: FBbt:00111424 ! adult protocerebral bridge 1 glomerulus-fan-shaped body-round body type a neuron
intersection_of: RO:0013005 FBbt:00111511 ! receives synaptic input throughout protocerebral bridge glomerulus 1
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
