[Term]
id: FBbt:00111633
name: larval dopaminergic pPAM neuron
def: "Dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in the anteriomedial region of the larval brain (Rohwedder et al., 2016). The primary neurite extends posteriorly to an area medial to the base of the vertical lobe of the mushroom body (Rohwedder et al., 2016). It then branches: one branch extends dorsally to form postsynaptic terminals in the dorsal protocerebrum, medial to the vertical lobe of the mushroom body; the other branch runs basomedially to form, mostly presynaptic terminals, in a specific domain of the medial lobe of the mushroom body (Rohwedder et al., 2016). A single projection crosses the midline to innervate the same domain in the contralateral medial lobe of the mushroom body (Rohwedder et al., 2016). There are 4 neurons in this cluster, belonging to different subtypes (Rohwedder et al., 2016; Truman et al., 2023). These neurons develop from a DALcm neuroblast and die early during the pupal stage (Saumweber et al., 2018; Truman et al., 2023)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231223, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
comment: Dopaminergic cells were identified by double labeling with a tyrosine hydroxylase (anti-TH) antibody and a TH-GAL4 driver (Rohwedder et al., 2016). Lineage either DALcm1 or DALcm2 (Saumweber et al., 2018).
synonym: "larval DAN of pPAM cluster" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0238440]
synonym: "larval PAM neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
synonym: "primary-lineage protocerebral anterior medial cluster neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0231223]
is_a: FBbt:00047952 ! mushroom body modulatory input neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0002100 FBbt:00111226 ! has soma location cell body rind of larval brain
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00100740 ! develops from neuroblast DAL
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061527 ! capable of dopamine secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00001925 ! receives synaptic input in region larval protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00110188 ! sends synaptic output to region medial lobe of larval mushroom body
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2016-04-29T14:34:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111634
name: larval mushroom body dopaminergic neuron h1
def: "Dopaminergic neuron of the pPAM cluster, whose cell body is located in the anteriomedial region of the larval brain. The primary neurite extends posteriorly to the base of the vertical lobe of the mushroom body. It then branches: one branch extends dorsally to form postsynaptic terminals in the dorsal protocerebrum, in an area medial and lateral to the vertical lobe of the mushroom body; the other branch runs basomedially to form presynaptic terminals in the most lateral domain of the medial lobe of the mushroom body (M2/shaft), and lateral to the innervation of the other pPAM neurons. A single projection crosses the midline to innervate the same domain in the contralateral medial lobe of the mushroom body." [FlyBase:FBrf0231223, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
comment: Saumweber et al. (2018) found this neuron in the L3 larva, but were not able to identify it in the L1.
synonym: "larval DAN-h1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0238440]
synonym: "larval dopaminergic pPAM1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
is_a: FBbt:00111633 ! larval dopaminergic pPAM neuron
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0000618 ! has characteristic bilateral
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007065 ! receives synaptic input in region embryonic/larval anterior superior medial protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0013002 FBbt:00007066 ! receives synaptic input in region embryonic/larval posterior superior medial protocerebrum
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00110196 ! sends synaptic output to region M2 segment of the larval medial lobe
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2016-04-29T14:34:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111635
name: larval mushroom body dopaminergic neuron k1
def: "Dopaminergic neuron of the pPAM cluster, whose cell body is located in the anteriomedial region of the larval brain. The primary neurite extends posteriorly to the base of the vertical lobe of the mushroom body. It then branches: one branch extends dorsally to form postsynaptic terminals in the superior medial protocerebrum and lateral accessory lobe, medial to the vertical lobe of the mushroom body; the other branch runs basomedially to form, mostly presynaptic terminals, in the basal tip of the medial lobe of the mushroom body (lower toe), and ventral to the innervation of the other pPAM neurons. A single projection crosses the midline to innervate the same domain in the contralateral medial lobe of the mushroom body. Often, a second contralateral branch crosses the midline, dorsal to the other branch and terminates in the superior medial protocerebrum. It receives input from FBNs, FFNs and MBONs (Eschbach et al., 2020)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231223, FlyBase:FBrf0238440, FlyBase:FBrf0245294, FlyBase:FBrf0255928]
