[Term]
id: FBbt:00111686
name: embryonic/larval medial antennal lobe tract
def: "The most medial of the antennal lobe tracts of the larva (Das et al., 2013). It connects the antennal lobe to the mushroom body calyx and lateral horn (Das et al., 2013). It contains fibers from the BAlc (ALl1), BAlp4 (ALlv1), BAmv3 (ALad1) and DPMpm1 (DM2) lineages (Hartenstein et al., 2015). Most uniglomerular neurons follow this tract (Berck et al., 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0220443, FlyBase:FBrf0229672, FlyBase:FBrf0232785]
