[Term]
id: FBbt:00111737 ! neuroblast NB5-7
def: "Neuroblast that is located medial to NB5-4 in the embryo, but does not generate any embryonic progeny (Lacin and Truman, 2016). It proliferates during the larval stage in all thoracic segments to generate postembryonic lineage 20 (Lacin and Truman, 2016). These cells are only found in thoracic segments (Lacin and Truman, 2016)." [FlyBase:FBrf0231327]
comment: Birkholz et al. (2015) suggest that NB5-4 generates postembryonic lineage 20; Lacin and Truman (2016) identify neuroblast NB5-7 and provide lineage tracing data showing that it generates lineage 20. NB5-7 may have evolved as a duplication of NB5-4 (Lacin and Truman, 2016).
subset: cur
subset: EmbDevSlim
is_a: FBbt:00001409 ! stage 4 neuroblast
is_a: FBbt:00051362 ! segmentally-repeated neuroblast
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2017-01-26T18:29:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FBbt:00111738
name: optic lobe neuroepithelial cell
def: "Symmetrically-dividing stem cell with epithelial properties and a columnar morphology that is a precursor to an optic neuroblast (Egger et al., 2007). These cells increase in number by symmetric divisions during embryonic and larval development (Egger et al., 2007). A small number differentiate into optic neuroblasts during the embryonic stage, while the remainder enter G0 quiescence prior to larval hatching (Hakes et al., 2018). Divisions resume in the first instar (Hakes et al., 2018), followed by differentiation to neuroblasts mainly during the third instar stage (Yasugi et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0193624, FlyBase:FBrf0204205, FlyBase:FBrf0240123]
synonym: "optic lobe NE cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0204205]
is_a: FBbt:00007344 ! somatic stem cell
relationship: BFO:0000050 FBbt:00001930 ! part of embryonic/larval optic lobe
relationship: RO:0002202 FBbt:00000186 ! develops from embryonic optic lobe primordium
