[Term]
id: FBbt:20001062
name: adult clamp neuron 357
def: "Adult brain-intrinsic neuron with its soma posterior to the posterior lateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the SMPp&v1 ventral hemilineage (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). It receives input in the superior and posterior lateral protocerebrum and clamp in both hemispheres (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its main outputs are to the contralateral superior and posterior lateral protocerebrum, clamp and lateral horn (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Cell type based on Hemibrain data (Scheffer et al., 2020), updated using FlyWire (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024) and identified at light level by Nern et al. (2025). Soma location is based on the closest annotated neuropil region in FlyWire.
