[Term]
id: FBbt:20001695
name: adult lobula visual centrifugal neuron LoVC15
def: "Adult visual centrifugal neuron with its soma posterior to the posterior lateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). It belongs to the VLPp&l1 posterior hemilineage (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). It is predominantly presynaptic in the lobula, arborizing mainly in layer 4 and spanning up to 50 columns (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). In the central brain, it remains mostly ipsilateral and has mixed pre- and post-synapses in the superior posterior slope and posterior lateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It also receives input in the inferior posterior slope (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Some of these neurons have small midline-crossing fibers (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is GABA (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are approximately 3 of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
