[Term]
id: FBbt:20001744
name: obsolete adult posterior lateral protocerebrum neuron 244
def: "Adult visual centrifugal neuron of the PLP244 group, with its soma in the brain, ventral-medial to the antennal lobe (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It is a putative embryonic-born neuron (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the contralateral lobula, the ipsilateral lobula, the ipsilateral superior posterior slope, the contralateral posterior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral posterior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral cantle and the contralateral superior posterior slope (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the contralateral lobula, the ipsilateral lobula, the contralateral posterior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral posterior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum and the contralateral posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is octopamine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type based on Hemibrain data (Scheffer et al., 2020) and updated using FlyWire (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Identified at light level and mapped to OA-AL2b1 in Nern et al. (2025).
synonym: "PLP244" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0246888]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2020-07-30T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00110146

[Term]
id: FBbt:20001833
name: adult bilateral LPT cell recurrent neuron
def: "Adult interneuron with its soma in the brain, anterior to the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the LALv1 ventral hemilineage (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). It projects to both hemispheres of the dorsal inferior posterior slope, reciprocally connecting with ipsilateral horizontal and vertical system cells (Erginkaya et al., 2025). It is GABAergic (Eckstein et al., 2024; Erginkaya et al., 2025). There are approximately 7 of these cells per hemisphere (Erginkaya et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0246888, FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262578]
comment: Cell type from Janelia hemibrain data (Scheffer et al., 2020), updated in FlyWire (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024), renamed and identified at light level in Erginkaya et al. (2025). FlyWire subtypes based on annotations in Codex (2025-06-05).
