[Term]
id: FBbt:20003954
name: obsolete adult CB0110 neuron
def: "Adult brain-intrinsic neuron of the CB0110 group, with its soma in the brain, anterior to the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the TRdm hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the prow and the gnathal ganglia (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the gnathal ganglia and the prow (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is glutamate (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: FlyWire CB0110 mapped to gnome in Shiu et al. (2024) - FBrf0260565 supplement. CB0110 was an uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024).
