[Term]
id: FBbt:20004313
name: adult medulla visual projection neuron MeVPMe13
def: "Adult interneuron with its soma ventral to the protocerebral bridge (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It is mostly postsynaptic in the ipsilateral medulla, spanning around 200 columns of layer M6, and it has mixed pre- and post-synapses in around 200 columns of contralateral layer M6 (Nern et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024), identified at light level by Nern et al. (2025). Soma location is based on the closest annotated neuropil region in FlyWire. All FlyWire cells have some synapses in the PVLP, so this does not seem to be an intrinsic neuron.
