[Term]
id: FBbt:20004631
name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg52
def: "Adult descending neuron with its soma and brain arbors in the gnathal ganglion (Sturner et al., 2025). It enters the VNC via the cervical connective (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Within the VNC, it fasciculates with the dorsal lateral tract of dorsal cervical fasciculus and sends output to the leg neuropil (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is GABA (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 4 of these cells per organism (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
comment: Type identified at light level and matched across EM datasets by Sturner et al. (2025). Pre- or post-synapse locations are the fewest regions that collectively contain at least 80 percent of all pre- or post-synapses of these neurons in FlyWire.
synonym: "DNfl006" NARROW [doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1]
synonym: "DNxl031" NARROW [doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1]
is_a: FBbt:00047516 ! descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0002101 FBbt:00047533 ! fasciculates with dorsal lateral tract of dorsal cervical fasciculus
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 ! capable of gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission
relationship: RO:0013001 FBbt:00014013 ! has synaptic IO in region adult gnathal ganglion
relationship: RO:0013003 FBbt:00047139 ! sends synaptic output to region adult leg neuropil
