name: obsolete adult CB1166 neuron
def: "Adult brain-intrinsic neuron with its soma in the central brain, lateral to the lateral horn. It belongs to the VPNl&d1_dorsal hemilineage. It has presynapses in the ipsilateral superior lateral protocerebrum. It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral lateral horn and the ipsilateral superior lateral protocerebrum. Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Soma locations are based on the closest annotated neuropil region. Pre- or post-synapse locations are the fewest regions that collectively contain at least 80 percent of all pre- or post-synapses of these neurons in FlyWire. Neurotransmitter predictions are from Eckstein et al. (2024). Other annotations are based on annotations in FlyWire and are available in the supplemental material of Schlegel et al. (2024). Obsoleted as all FlyWire individuals of this type have been retyped as LHAV5a1.
synonym: "CB1166" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260535]
