id: FBbt:20007261
name: obsolete adult CB3846 neuron
def: "Adult optic-lobe-intrinsic neuron of the CB3846 group, with its soma in the brain, medial to the lobula plate (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral lobula plate (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the ipsilateral lobula plate and the ipsilateral lobula (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is glutamate (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 150 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Mapped to Y11 in Nern et al. (2025) - FBrf0262545, but some individuals alternatively typed as Tlp5 (=Tlp11) in Codex.
synonym: "CB3846" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
