[Term]
id: FBbt:20007267
name: obsolete adult CB3852 neuron
def: "Adult optic-lobe-intrinsic neuron of the CB3852 group, with its soma in the brain, lateral to the medulla (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral medulla and the ipsilateral lobula (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the ipsilateral lobula and the ipsilateral medulla (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). There are approximately 408 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Mapped to Tm5b in Nern et al. (2025) - FBrf0262545.
