id: FBbt:20007289
name: adult lobula plate tangential neuron LPT111
def: "Adult lobula plate tangential neuron with its soma posterior to the inferior posterior slope (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the central brain, it remains ipsilateral, receiving input in the inferior posterior slope (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the lobula plate, mainly in layer 4, from around 10 columns (Nern et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is GABA (Eckstein et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025). There are approximately 40-50 of these cells per optic lobe (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
