[Term]
id: FBbt:20007449
name: obsolete descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNge138
def: "Adult descending neuron of the DNge138 group, with its soma in the brain, posterior to the gnathal ganglia (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the LB0 anterior hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the gnathal ganglia, the saddle, the superior posterior slope, the vest, the cantle, the anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum and the wedge (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the gnathal ganglia, the saddle, the wedge, the anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum and the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is octopamine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Obsoleted as mapped to OA-VUMd1 in Bates et al. (2025) - doi:10.1101/2025.07.31.667571.
