id: FBbt:20007461
name: obsolete descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNge150
def: "Adult descending neuron of the DNge150 group, with its soma in the brain, posterior-ventral to the gnathal ganglia (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the LB0 posterior hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the flange, the gnathal ganglia, the prow, the saddle and the cantle (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the gnathal ganglia, the prow and the flange (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is octopamine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There is approximately one of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Obsoleted as mapped to OA-VUMd3 in Bates et al. (2025) - doi:10.1101/2025.07.31.667571.
synonym: "DNge150" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260535]
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5633-1314
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/date "2024-02-05T12:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00110163

[Term]
id: FBbt:20007466
name: obsolete descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNge155
def: "Adult descending neuron with its soma in the central brain, near to the gnathal ganglia. Its predicted neurotransmitter is glutamate." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Soma locations are based on the closest annotated neuropil region. Pre- or post-synapse locations are the fewest regions that collectively contain at least 80 percent of all pre- or post-synapses of these neurons in FlyWire. Neurotransmitter predictions are from Eckstein et al. (2024). Other annotations are based on annotations in FlyWire and are available in the supplemental material of Schlegel et al. (2024). Obsoleted as all FlyWire individuals of this type have been retyped as DNge153.
synonym: "DNge155" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260535]
