name: descending neuron of the gnathal ganglion DNg79
def: "Adult descending neuron with its soma in the gnathal ganglion, ventral to the prow (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the brain, it has postsynapses in the ipsilateral inferior and superior posterior slope and the gnathal ganglion, and presynapses in the gnathal ganglion, the ipsilateral superior posterior slope and the saddle (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the VNC, it follows the median tract of dorsal cervical fasciculus I (Sturner et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 4 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
