name: descending neuron of the posterior brain DNp73
def: "Adult descending neuron with its soma in the brain, posterior-lateral to the inferior bridge (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the brain, it has postsynapses in the saddle, the ipsilateral antennal mechanosensory and motor center and the gnathal ganglion (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the contralateral inferior posterior slope, the gnathal ganglion and the saddle (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). In the VNC, it follows the median tract of dorsal cervical fasciculus I (Sturner et al., 2025). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
