[Term]
id: FBbt:20007559
name: obsolete adult lobula columnar neuron e07
def: "Adult visual projection neuron of the LCe07 group, with its soma in the brain, ventral-lateral to the lateral horn (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the VPNp1_lateral hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral lobula (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the ipsilateral superior posterior slope, the ipsilateral posterior lateral protocerebrum and the contralateral superior posterior slope (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 12 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546]
comment: Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Found to be the same cell type as LC23 by Nern et al. (2025) - FBrf0262545.
synonym: "adult LCe07 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0260535]
