is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FBbt:00111758

[Term]
id: FBbt:20007573
name: adult lobula visual projection neuron LoVP109
def: "Adult visual projection neuron with its soma ventral to the posterior lateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It remains ipsilateral, receiving input in the lobula and sending output to the anterior and posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There is one of these cells per hemisphere (Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0259490, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
comment: Cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Identified at light level, but not in optic lobe EM dataset, by Nern et al. (2025). Soma location based on the closest annotated neuropil region in FlyWire.
