[Term]
id: FBbt:20008193
name: labial nerve sensory descending neuron 1
def: "Adult sensory neuron that enters the brain via the maxillary-labial nerve and arborizes in the gnathal ganglion (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025). It descends to the ventral nerve cord and follows the ventral median tract of ventral cervical fasciculus (Takemura et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025). It sends output to the T1 leg neuropil (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There is one of these cells on each side (Sturner et al., 2025)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
comment: Type identified at light level and matched across EM datasets by Sturner et al. (2025).
synonym: "adult DNfl013 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
synonym: "adult LN-DN1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
