[Term]
id: FBbt:20008422
name: obsolete adult DNxn164 neuron
def: "Adult descending neuron of the DNxn164 group (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). It enters the VNC via the cervical connective (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Within the VNC it fasciculates with the dorsal median tract (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). It receives input in the brain and sends output to multiple regions (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1, FlyBase:FBrf0259490]
