name: descending neuron of the anterior dorsal brain DNa14
def: "Adult descending neuron with its soma in the brain, anterior to the mushroom body vertical lobe (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the WEDd1 (DALd) lineage (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). In the brain, it has postsynapses ipsilaterally in the inferior and superior clamp, gorget, inferior bridge and superior medial protocerebrum, and presynapses in the gnathal ganglion (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Within the VNC, it fasciculates with the median dorsal abdominal tract and sends output to the leg neuropil (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Sturner et al., 2025)." [doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1, doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1, FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262850]
