[Term]
id: FBbt:20011498
name: adult transmedullary Y neuron TmY19b
def: "Adult transmedullary Y neuron with its soma lateral to the medulla (Nern et al., 2025; Valentino et al., 2025). It remains in the ipsilateral optic lobe, with the majority of its input and output synapses found in lobula layers 2-5A (Nern et al., 2025; Valentino et al., 2025). It also receives input in medulla layers M8-M10 and has a small arbor in lobula plate layer 1 (Nern et al., 2025; Valentino et al., 2025). It is GABAergic (Nern et al., 2025). There are approximately 20 of these cells per hemisphere (Matsliah et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025)." [FlyBase:FBrf0260535, FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0260546, FlyBase:FBrf0262545, FlyBase:FBrf0263481]
comment: Cell type identified in multiple EM datasets and at light level (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Matsliah et al., 2024; Nern et al., 2025; Valentino et al., 2025). Nern et al. (2025) TmY19a mapped to Valentino et al. (2025) TmY17 based on manual inspection of morphology, however around double the number of cells are reported in Valentino et al. (2025).
synonym: "LMa3" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0260545, FlyBase:FBrf0262545]
synonym: "TmY17" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0263481]
